{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HpNJoVfPg9CE7UjmMrNHu","type":"tool_result","content":"new-game: made the game \"probe\" in probe-game: the engine at my-3dge@e7a1243 (2135 files, read-only, pinned by engine-lock.json) and the starter game in labs/game/\nnext: cd probe-game && bash scripts/setup.sh && npm test\nthen: read AGENTS.md and docs/GAME-GUIDE.md, make the game in labs/game/, and commit as you go\ntotal 768\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 .claude\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    210 Nov  4 21:23 .editorconfig\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    139 Nov  4 21:23 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha      8 Nov  4 21:23 .nvmrc\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    991 Nov  4 21:23 .prettierignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha     47 Nov  4 21:23 .prettierrc.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   3585 Nov  4 21:23 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    273 Nov  4 21:23 CLAUDE.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   4596 Nov  4 21:23 DOCTRINE.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    797 Nov  4 21:23 ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha     13 Nov  4 21:23 GEMINI.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    426 Nov  4 21:23 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 data\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 docs\ndrwxr-xr-x 13 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 engine\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 263822 Nov  4 21:23 engine-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   4050 Nov  4 21:23 eslint.config.js\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    975 Nov  4 21:23 index.html\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 labs\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 379341 Nov  4 21:23 package-lock.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   1255 Nov  4 21:23 package.json\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 tests\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:23 tools\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    584 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.apps.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    544 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.base.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   1392 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.check.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    345 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.engine.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    512 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    546 Nov  4 21:23 tsconfig.tests.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   4934 Nov  4 21:23 vite.config.ts\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha    387 Nov  4 21:23 x.js\n# AGENTS.md: probe\n\nprobe is a game made with my-3dge, a 3D web game engine built for AI coding agents: TypeScript, three.js on\nWebGPU, Rapier physics, gameplay reproducible on the CPU and checked without a screen, the UI in HTML/CSS. The engine\nis in this repository, pinned to the commit engine-lock.json names; you make the game.\n\nBefore your first change, read docs/GAME-GUIDE.md once: how a game is built on this engine, the commands that prove\nit works, and where to look things up. Then grow the game from the starter in labs/game/, which already plays, wins\nthrough its bot, and passes its tests.\n\n## Set up (once per machine)\n\n    bash scripts/setup.sh\n\nIt installs Node 24 when missing (Linux x64), Chromium for the browser commands when missing, then `npm ci`. Plain\n`npm ci` is enough for everything except `x shot`, `x film` and `x replay --browser`.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. Edit the game in labs/game/: sim-side code (the rules) in labs/game/scenes/ and labs/game/cast/, the page in\n   labs/game/main.ts.\n2. `npm run check`: types, lint, format, the asset rules, and the engine unchanged.\n3. `npm test`: the game's tests (its replay's golden hashes, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds).\n4. See it without a screen: `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` (the hash and the events), `node x shot labs/game`\n   (what the page draws, as numbers and a text thumbnail), `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim` (the\n   goldens, in Node and Chromium). `node x help` lists every command; each prints its verdict first and writes\n   out/<cmd>/…/report.json.\n5. Commit, and keep labs/game/README.md current: what the game is, how it plays, the calls you made.\n\n`npm run dev` serves the game at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ for a person to play.\n\n## Rules\n\n- **The engine is read-only.** engine/, tools/, data/, labs/box/ (the engine's worked example), scripts/setup.sh, the\n  configs and the docs it shipped: engine-lock.json lists every one, and `npm run check` fails when one changes. When\n  the engine is in your way, work round it in the game and write what you needed in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. Only when no\n  workaround exists, patch the engine file and list it under \"Local engine patches\" there, with why.\n- **Only the public API.** Pages import engine/index.ts; sim-side code imports engine/sim-api.ts (lint enforces it).\n- **Reproducible play.** Sim-side code reads no clock, no `Math.random`, no DOM: randomness comes from named streams\n  (`w.rng('loot')`), time is whole 60 Hz steps. The same intents and seed give the same hashes, in Node and Chromium.\n- **Assets are code or text first**: geometry, textures, materials and sounds as data. A binary file only with the\n  owner's approval, listed in APPROVED-BINARIES.json with their answer (`npm run check` fails one unlisted); fonts are\n  approved, anywhere in labs/game/ with their license beside them.\n- SI units, +Y up, characters face +Z. Every file opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines.\n- **Ask the owner** before anything outward or costly: a binary asset, a new npm dependency, spending money,\n  publishing. No answer within 15 minutes: take the safer choice, note it in labs/game/README.md, carry on.\n- Update the engine only when the owner asks: `node x engine --update`.\n\n## Done means\n\n`npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the bot still wins (teach it each new rule); a change that alters play on\npurpose records the replay's goldens again (`node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`) with the reason\nin the commit; labs/game/README.md says what the game is now.\n{\n  \"name\": \"probe\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"A game made with the my-3dge engine.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=24.10 <25\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -b tsconfig.check.json\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write --cache .\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"0.21.0\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-cos\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-pow\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-sin\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"three\": \"0.182.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.32.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"1.64.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/core\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n    \"@types/three\": \"0.182.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.5\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-jsdoc\": \"61.7.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"3.9.10\",\n    \"tsx\": \"4.23.15\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"7.3.7\",\n    \"vitest\": \"4.1.12\"\n  },\n  \"allowScripts\": {\n    \"esbuild\": false\n  }\n}\nprobe-game/labs/game:\nREADME.md\nbest.test.ts\nbest.ts\nbot.ts\ncast\nindex.html\nmain.ts\nreplays\nscenes\n\nprobe-game/labs/game/cast:\nplayer.ts\n\nprobe-game/labs/game/replays:\nbot.replay.json\n\nprobe-game/labs/game/scenes:\nplay.test.ts\nplay.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"c7a73570-0184-4a48-ae04-e58382d9be44","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:55.717Z","tool_use_result":{"