{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P9HuYBbyz9nfHuQDAT9EUT","type":"tool_result","content":"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n...\naccount.test.mjs\natlas.test.mjs\naudio-inventory.test.mjs\naudio-review-browser.mjs\naudit3d.mjs\naudit3d.test.mjs\ncatalogue.test.mjs\ncheck-libraries.mjs\ncheck3d.py\ncouch.test.mjs\ndates.test.mjs\ndeck.test.mjs\ndesktop-import.test.mjs\ndev.mjs\nexplore-browser.mjs\nexplore.test.mjs\nfill.mjs\nfill.test.mjs\nfilter.test.mjs\nframes.test.mjs\nfriends.test.mjs\nhub-check.mjs\nhub-client.mjs\nhub-client.test.mjs\nhub-pages.test.mjs\nhub.test.mjs\nimport-catalogue.test.mjs\nimport-hub-pages.mjs\nimport-matrix-runs.mjs\nimport-registry.test.mjs\ningest.mjs\nintake.test.mjs\nkit.test.mjs\nlayout.test.mjs\nlib\nlibraries.test.mjs\nlibrary-browser.mjs\nmatrix-runs.test.mjs\nmatrix3d.py\nmesh.test.mjs\n#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * hub-check.mjs — does a game keep the AI Hub Session Protocol?\n *\n * Runs lib/hub/harness.html?auto=1 against each game, at the player counts its\n * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n * press, the start, traffic, a player leaving, time-up and a valid result. Then\n * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n * errors, the session client inactive and Math.random left alone. Before any\n * game script runs, every frame in session mode gets alert, confirm, prompt,\n * window.open and socket constructors wrapped, so calling them is caught.\n * Needs Playwright, which is not a dependency (see shots.mjs).\n *\n * Parallel is played at 1 and 2 players: nothing is shared, so more copies\n * prove nothing more. Its checks expect Math.random seeded the same on every\n * copy, progress from every copy, and no game traffic.\n *\n * Ghost and shared world are played at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network\n * (150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss). Ghost is checked like parallel, except that every\n * copy sends its player. A shared world wants traffic both ways, and is\n * played once more at 2 players with its world hosted by one more copy that\n * has no player of its own, as a dedicated server would host it (README,\n * \"Shared world\"). That run is reported like any; --record does not hold it\n * against a game, since no server runs yet.\n *\n * --retrofit is for an existing game upgraded to parallel: it is played once,\n * at 2 players with one of them leaving. With --original <path>, errors the\n * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n * a game before spending a model on it, since a page this browser cannot run\n * cannot be checked here. A WebGPU-only game without WebGPU is caught even\n * when its title screen shows: it asked for an adapter, got none, and drew\n * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n * Chromium; on a machine without a GPU, SwiftShader gives such games a\n * software adapter:\n *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n *\n * Every game's pasted client is also read from disk and must be exactly a\n * released one (scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs).\n *\n * --record writes the outcome into data/overrides.json, which is how the hub\n * keeps a failing game out of sessions: a game that fails gets \"session\": \"0\"\n * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n * it) and a sessionNote naming what failed; a game that passes loses both.\n *\n * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n *         (games default to the three examples in lib/hub/examples/)\n */\n\nimport { createServer } from