{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9QBZpHdMS99eVcyvTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0182UuzPAdFiQZpx13BAvDGy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge/lean/README.md","offset":517,"limit":120},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20990,"cache_read_input_tokens":145774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20990},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"4785d211-a002-4402-a531-5bbcbc49d17d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:03.659Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9QBAGizL1sx6XA71Ev","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0182UuzPAdFiQZpx13BAvDGy":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge/lean/README.md","offset":517,"limit":120}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0182UuzPAdFiQZpx13BAvDGy","type":"tool_result","content":"517\t- `crt` (the whole picture): A CRT's glass: phosphor glow, an aperture grille and a flicker (curvature: screen; lines: scanlines). `mask` 0.25 (0–1), `glow` 0.25 (0–1), `flicker` 0.1 (0–1).\n518\t- `vhs` (the whole picture): VHS tape: rows slipping sideways, colour bleeding to the right, snow in a rolling band. `jitter` 0.5 (0–1), `bleed` 0.5 (0–1), `noise` 0.3 (0–1).\n519\t- `speedlines` (the whole picture): Speed lines: comic-book streaks round a clear centre, redrawn 12 times a second. `density` 0.6 (0–1), `clear` 0.35 (0–0.9), `x` 0.5 (0–1), `y` 0.5 (0–1), `color` '#ffffff'.\n520\t- `vignette` (the whole picture): A vignette: the corners toward a colour, round or following the screen, soft or hard. `strength` 0.45 (0–1), `softness` 0.5 (0.05–1), `roundness` 1 (0–1), `color` '#000000'.\n521\t- `grain`: Film grain that changes every frame. `amount` 0.35 (0–1).\n522\t- `chroma`: Colour fringes: red and blue pulled apart toward the screen edges. `amount` 0.5 (0–1).\n523\t- `letterbox` (the whole picture): Letterbox bars that crop the picture to a film aspect ratio. `aspect` 2.39 (1.2–2.8), `color` '#000000'.\n524\t- `screen` (the whole picture): The screen itself: CRT curvature, a vignette, low resolution. `curvature` 0 (0–0.5), `vignette` 0 (0–1), `pixelate` 1 (1–16 px).\n525\t\n526\t**A look's other fields** (`defineLook(id, { description, filters, combine, … })`):\n527\t\n528\t- `style`: The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\n529\t- `sky`: The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\n530\t- `skyGradient`: How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\n531\t- `toon`: The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\n532\t- `shells`: Outline shells round the props and bodies (engine/gfx/stageShells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.\n533\t- `resolution`: The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\n534\t- `textures`: How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\n535\t- `perspective`: The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\n536\t- `strength`: How much of the whole look shows, 0 to 1: every filter's amount is scaled by it, so 0 draws the scene clean.\n537\t<!-- lean:looks:end -->\n538\t\n539\t## Built-in ids and the level legend\n540\t\n541\t<!-- lean:ids:start -->\n542\t**Built-in ids**, by kind, as a scene names them (`material: 'material:glow'`, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench',\n543\tat: [x, 0, z], yaw: 0 })`); `__engine.describe('<kind>')` in a running page lists a kind's fields, and\n544\t`define<Kind>` adds your own.\n545\t\n546\t- `sky:` dawn, daylight, dusk, hall, night, noon. Sky presets.\n547\t- `material:` asphalt, barrel, barrelLid, barrelStaves, blobShadow, brick, carpet, checker, cloth, concrete, crate, default, flagstone, flame, glass, glow, iron, paint, planks, puppet, puppetGlow, puppetHalo, shingles, siding, stone, tiles, wallpaper, wood. Materials as data with three.js's classic parameters.\n548\t- `texture:` asphalt, brick, carpet, checker, concrete, crate, dirt, flagstone, glass, grass, metal, moss, planks, plaster, runes, shingles, siding, staves, stone, tiles, wallpaper, water, wood. Seeded, periodic texture generators.\n549\t- `geometry:` box, frustum, limb, pillar, ramp, ring, roundedBox. Shapes props, levels and bodies name by id.\n550\t- `prop:` banner, barrel, bench, brazier, chair, chest, crate, door, garageDoor, lamp, lantern, pane, pillar, sconce, statue, switch, table. Props: things that stand in a level, as data: meshes (geometry and material by id), a body, an optional light spot, where a level places them, and interaction hooks.\n551\t- `light:` torch. What a level's light spot shines with.\n552\t- `emitter:` bits, block, bubbles, confetti, destroyed, dust, embers, explosion, fire, fireflies, fountain, glass, glints, hit, impact, land, magic, rain, shatter, shot, slain, slam, smoke, snow, sparks, splinters, steam. Emitters. Burst by a sim event of the type: block, destroyed, explosion, glass, hit, land, shatter, shot, slain, slam, splinters. Running at a rate (lay them into your own): bubbles, confetti, dust, embers, fire, fireflies, fountain, magic, rain, smoke, snow, sparks, steam.\n553\t- `telegraph:` arc, cone, line, ring. Telegraphs.\n554\t- `sfx:` blip, bodyFall, boom, bump, cancel, charge, climbGrip, coin, confirm, crouchCloth, die, door, doorBreak, doorClose, doorLocked, doorOpen, drawGun, drumCrash, drumHat, drumKick, drumOpenHat, drumSnare, drumTom, dryFire, explode, glassBreak, grab, heal, hit, holsterGun, hurt, impactBody, impactConcrete, impactDirt, impactGlass, impactMetal, impactWood, jump, jump2, key, kick, kickHit, ladderRung, land, landBody, laser, launch, mantle, oneup, pause, pickup, pistolShot, powerup, punch, punchHit, reload, rifleShot, secret, select, shoot, slide, step, stepCarpet, stepConcrete, stepGrass, stepGravel, stepMetal, stepTile, stepWood, stomp, swing, swish, switchClick, text, warp, whoosh, wind, windowSlide, zipAttach, zipRun. A sound effect.\n555\t- `song:` adventure, boss, dungeon, title, victory. A looping tune in tracker notation.\n556\t- `body:` humanoid. Puppet bodies.\n557\t- `build:` adult, bulky, chibi, heroic, skeleton. Body proportions for the humanoid skeleton, in metres before size.\n558\t- `movement:` apex, platformer. How a character moves.\n559\t- `move:` axekick, backslash, bash, breach, cast, claw, cross, elbow, flyingkick, haymaker, hook, jab, kick, knee, overhead, plunge, rising, roundhouse, slash, spin, sweep, throw, thrust, twohand, uppercut. A named strike.\n560\t- `weapon:` gun. Firearms.\n561\t- `thing:` target. Things that can be hit.\n562\t- `actionMap:` firstPerson, platformer, shmup, thirdPerson. Named actions and the physical codes bound to each.\n563\t\n564\t**The level legend**, a character a tile (`compileLevel`; `defineGlyph` adds one):\n565\t\n566\t- `t`: A brazier: an iron bowl on a stone foot, 0.75 m high (a cylinder collider, 0.3125 m in radius), with a torch spot 1 m up.\n567\t- `o`: The dais: an octagonal platform 0.5 m up (a hull frustum), its edge a 1.5 m slope all round.\n568\t- `+`: A doorway in a wall, 2.1 m high: walk through; the wall stands over its head.\n569\t- `<`: A flight of stairs up to the storey above: a ramp (a hull wedge) from this floor to that one, rising toward the one side that floor meets.\n570\t- `.`: Open floor at ground level: walkable.\n571\t- `=`: A gallery: a walkway 1 m up, a block from the ground (a box collider).\n572\t- `@`: Floor with the hero's spawn point (spawn:hero).\n573\t- `|`: A ladder: open floor with a ladder against the neighbouring tile that stands highest (a wall, a tower), up to its top.\n574\t- `_`: Floor under a low ceiling 1.4 m up (a crawlspace): crouch or slide under it.\n575\t- `w`: A low wall (0.75 m): solid at ground level, but a body may jump onto it and stand on its top.\n576\t- `P`: A pillar (3.5 m), 2 × 2 tiles: write it PP over PP.\n577\t- `!`: A railing 1 m high round a landing, a deck or a stairwell: solid at ground level, a box collider.\n578\t- `^`: Stairs: a ramp from the ground up to 1 m (a hull wedge), rising toward the one side that meets a gallery.\n579\t- `~`: Void: no floor on this storey (a stairwell, a double height, the air beside a building).\n580\t- `#`: A full-height wall (3 m): solid, a box collider, nobody walks or stands on it.\n581\t- `:`: A window in a wall: solid to its sill 0.9 m up, open to its head 2.1 m up, the wall over it.\n582\t- `1` to `9`: Floor with the spawn marker n (spawn:n): where a scene places what it numbers n, such as a mover's start.\n583\t<!-- lean:ids:end -->\n584\t\n585\t## The API by area\n586\t\n587\t<!-- lean:api:start -->\n588\tEvery name below is an export of `my3dge` (`import { createEngine, defineScene } from 'my3dge'`). Each has the\n589\tfirst sentence of its doc comment in docs/API.md, and its whole manual where engine/ declares it.\n590\t\n591\t**Scenes**: defined as data with a setup and a step, run by x sim, x replay and createHeadless.\n592\t`defineScene`, `defineDevAction`; types `Scene`, `SceneSpec`, `SceneAction`, `SceneSound`, `DevActionSpec`.\n593\t\n594\t**The world**: entities, components, systems, timers, events.\n595\t`defineComponent`, `PHASES`; types `World`, `SimRng`, `WorldTimers`, `WorldEvents`, `Entity`, `With`, `SpawnSpec`, `ComponentOf`, `Phase`, `SystemFn`.\n596\t\n597\t**Registries and settings**: content as data, one schema for every setting.\n598\t`defineKind`, `def`, `defineSettings`; types `Entry`, `Kind`, `KindSpec`, `Field`, `Schema`, `SimSettings`, `SettingValue`.\n599\t\n600\t**Intents**: what the sim reads from outside each step.\n601\t`held`, `pressed`, `fromCamera`, `INTENT_KEYS`, `createInputBuffer`, `updateInputBuffer`, `released`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`, `repeated`, `BUFFER_STEPS`, `REPEAT_DELAY`, `REPEAT_RATE`; types `Intents`, `IntentValue`, `CustomIntentKey`, `InputBuffer`.\n602\t\n603\t**Math**: three.js's math classes and the engine's helpers (MathUtils covers clamp, lerp, damp, smoothstep).\n604\t`Vector3`, `Quaternion`, `Matrix4`, `Euler`, `Box3`, `Sphere`, `Ray`, `Plane`, `Color`, `MathUtils`, `approach`, `angDiff`, `lerpAng`, `approachAng`, `smoothDamp`, `ease`, `swingTwist`.\n605\t\n606\t**Randomness**: seeded streams (the world's are w.rng('<stream>')).\n607\t`Rng`.\n608\t\n609\t**Events**: emitted with w.emit, heard with w.events.on.\n610\ttypes `EventMap`, `Listener`, `TraceRecord`.\n611\t\n612\t**Levels**: a legend of glyphs, level text compiled to plain data (heights, solid grid, colliders, meshes, spawns).\n613\t`compileLevel`, `validateLevel`, `defineGlyph`, `defineLevel`, `getLevel`, `floorHeight`, `topHeight`, `solidAt`, `tileAt`, `LEVEL_FORMAT`; types `CompileOptions`, `LevelSource`, `LevelProblem`, `Glyph`, `GlyphSpec`, `LevelEntry`, `CompiledLevel`, `LevelGlyph`, `BoxCollider`, `ColliderDescriptor`, `GroundDescriptor`, `MeshDescriptor`, `SpawnPoint`, `LightSpot`, `TileRect`, `Point3`.\n614\t\n615\t**Animation (WP 3.4)**: the humanoid skeleton (a root plus 23 joints) and its builds, poses with three.js quaternions, blending under bone masks, additive layers, forward kinematics, SVG contact sheets and the pose checks.\n616\t`JOINTS`, `SOCKETS`, `MASKS`, `createSkeleton`, `boneMask`, `defineBuild`, `getBuild`, `Pose`, `blendPoses`, `makeAdditive`, `addPose`, `hashPose`, `forwardKinematics`, `createWorldPose`, `jointPosition`, `jointRotation`, `jointMatrix`, `jointToWorld`, `socketPosition`, `tipPosition`, `animSheet`, `animCheck`, `twoBone`, `twoBoneRot`, `LIMBS`, `aim`, `AIM_CHAIN`, `footPlant`, `createFootPlantState`, `FOOT_LOCK`, `FOOT_PLANT`, `FootPlant`, `queryGround`, `handTo`; types `JointName`, `SocketName`, `MaskName`, `Skeleton`, `BoneMask`, `Build`, `BuildSpec`, `JointRef`, `BlendOptions`, `WorldPose`, `Sheet`, `SheetFrame`, `SheetOptions`, `SheetView`, `AnimCheckSpec`, `AnimCheckReport`, `AnimProblem`, `RigidPair`, `PointName`, `TwoBoneOptions`, `LimbEnd`, `Limb`, `AimOptions`, `AimLink`, `FootPlantOptions`, `FootPlantState`, `FootLock`, `FootPlantLayerOptions`, `GroundQueries`, `GroundProbe`, `GroundHit`.\n617\t\n618\t**The procedural humanoid (WP 3.6)**: my-3d2dge's gait, idle, lean, arm swing, held poses and stances as effector targets written with B(forward, right, up), solved onto the skeleton; a fixed step and a seeded stream.\n619\t`Humanoid`, `POSES`, `STANCES`, `WEAPONS`, `B`, `turnRight`; types `HumanoidOptions`, `HumanoidInput`, `HumanoidState`, `HumanoidWeights`, `BodyMotion`, `PoseName`, `StanceName`, `Weapon`, `Effectors`, `FRU`, `LimbSide`, `Sided`.\n620\t\n621\t**The character animator (WP 3.7)**: a body driven through an explicit layer stack (weights, base, override, solve, then layers in clips, additive, post, physics and secondary), told its body states each step (unknown words warn with the closest), with footsteps, sockets, a trail and detail levels; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n622\t`Animator`, `BODY_STATES`, `checkBodyStates`, `TRAILS`, `SAMPLE_STATES`, `SLOTS`, `LAYER_SLOTS`, `LOD`, `easeWeight`, `HUMANOID_WEIGHTS`; types `AnimatorOptions`, `PoseOptions`, `AnimatorReport`, `AnimEvent`, `TrailSample`, `BodyStateName`, `AnimatorInput`, `TrailName`, `SampleState`, `SlotName`, `LayerSlot`, `AnimLayer`, `WeightRates`, `WeightInfo`.\n623\t\n624\t**Blob and floater rigs (WP 5.3)**: my-3d2dge's squash-and-stretch blob on a minimal skeleton (a volume-preserving squash spring, a smoothed look, wings, its moves as data: bite, leap, pounce, spit) and a floater that hovers over the floor, banks into turns and carries orbiting motes; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n625\t`Blob`, `BLOB`, `BLOB_JOINTS`, `BLOB_LEAP`, `BLOB_MOVES`, `blobMove`, `blobMoveTimes`, `Floater`, `FLOATER`; types `BlobOptions`, `BlobInput`, `BlobState`, `BlobJoint`, `BlobPose`, `BlobLeap`, `BlobMove`, `BlobMoveName`, `BlobMoveFrame`, `FloaterOptions`, `FloaterInput`, `FloaterState`, `FloaterPose`.\n626\t\n627\t**The animation library (WP 8.4)**: readable key-pose clips (format 1 and 2: parse, print, check, the normalized lens, mirroring, the decode to 36 body points), loaded per set; baked to 30 fps rotation tracks on the skeleton, retargeted onto any build (rotation copy aligned at rest, the hip-height ratio, contact IK) or given to three.js as AnimationClip JSON; played by the clip layer in the animator's clip slot, loops at the ground speed, with shardfall's walk-run switch and strike time.\n628\t`parseClip`, `parseClipSet`, `validateClip`, `poseError`, `poseMeanError`, `clipText`, `normalizedLens`, `mirrorClip`, `decodePose`, `samplePose`, `POSE_POINTS`, `POINT_INDEX`, `bakeClip`, `sampleBaked`, `travelAt`, `BAKE_FPS`, `retargetPose`, `clipJSON`, `hipRatio`, `standingHipHeight`, `restSkeleton`, `restPoints`, `restBuild`, `RETARGET`, `loadClipLibrary`, `clipPace`, `walkRate`, `runOverWalk`, `strikeTime`, `GROUND_SPEED`, `STRIKE`, `ClipLayer`, `CLIP_LAYER`; types `ClipSet`, `ClipSource`, `RestBody`, `ClipWarning`, `Clip`, `ClipKey`, `KeyPose`, `LimbPose`, `ClipEvent`, `ClipContact`, `BakedClip`, `RetargetOptions`, `AnimationClipJSON`, `ClipLibrary`, `ClipOrigin`, `ClipLayerOptions`, `ClipPlay`, `ClipSlot`, `ClipLayerState`, `ClipLayerEvent`, `ClipStepInput`.\n629\t\n630\t**Moves (WP 6.1)**: moves as data in metres (the kind move: my-3d2dge's 24, converted by Appendix C's table), timelines whose events carry leftover time, attacks and combos with hit windows, sweeps and root motion, moves played on a humanoid through its body state (the arm path), moves at a moment for previews, measured hit shapes, the cone helpers and a hit's knockback velocity.\n631\t`defineMove`, `getMove`, `resolveMove`, `MOVE_PHASES`, `LEGACY_FIELDS`, `fromLegacy`, `Timeline`, `Attack`, `Combo`, `moveAt`, `measureMove`, `strikePart`, `strikeSegment`, `inArc`, `inHitShape`, `knockbackVelocity`; types `Move`, `MoveSpec`, `MoveInput`, `MovePhase`, `LegacyMove`, `TimelinePhase`, `TimelineMark`, `TimelineEvent`, `TimelineState`, `AttackState`, `ComboState`, `Sweep`, `HitShape`, `StrikeBody`, `StrikeAnimator`, `ArmState`.\n632\t\n633\t**Reactions and secondary motion (WP 6.2)**: a directional flinch, knockdown, death and the get-up chosen by how the body lies (face up or face down), stepped in the sim; verlet chains (hair, tails) with bone-capsule colliders, a floor probe and a rest shape, a cape of two chains, and the squash spring as a volume-preserving root scale, drawn by an animator layer in the view.\n634\t`Reactions`, `REACTION`, `REACTIONS`, `lyingOf`, `Chain`, `CHAIN`, `Cape`, `Secondary`, `HAIR`, `CAPE`, `TAIL`, `SQUASH`, `squashScale`, `BODY_CAPSULES`, `bodyCapsules`; types `ReactionOptions`, `ReactionState`, `ReactionBody`, `ReactionName`, `Lying`, `ChainOptions`, `ChainTuning`, `BoneCapsule`, `CapeOptions`, `SecondaryOptions`.\n635\t\n636\t**Animation checks (WP 6.6)**: the state matrix (each body state held at each facing, from rest and back to rest) and animCheckBody, which checks a whole body over it: every pose, the same hashes twice, 1/60 s against 1/120 s; and the camera presets sheets of it are drawn from."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"591661ab-2d59-4c01-9d74-700c7ddeb63c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:03.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge/lean/README.md","content":"- `crt` (the whole picture): A CRT's glass: phosphor glow, an aperture grille and a flicker (curvature: screen; lines: scanlines). `mask` 0.25 (0–1), `glow` 0.25 (0–1), `flicker` 0.1 (0–1).\n- `vhs` (the whole picture): VHS tape: rows slipping sideways, colour bleeding to the right, snow in a rolling band. `jitter` 0.5 (0–1), `bleed` 0.5 (0–1), `noise` 0.3 (0–1).\n- `speedlines` (the whole picture): Speed lines: comic-book streaks round a clear centre, redrawn 12 times a second. `density` 0.6 (0–1), `clear` 0.35 (0–0.9), `x` 0.5 (0–1), `y` 0.5 (0–1), `color` '#ffffff'.\n- `vignette` (the whole picture): A vignette: the corners toward a colour, round or following the screen, soft or hard. `strength` 0.45 (0–1), `softness` 0.5 (0.05–1), `roundness` 1 (0–1), `color` '#000000'.\n- `grain`: Film grain that changes every frame. `amount` 0.35 (0–1).\n- `chroma`: Colour fringes: red and blue pulled apart toward the screen edges. `amount` 0.5 (0–1).\n- `letterbox` (the whole picture): Letterbox bars that crop the picture to a film aspect ratio. `aspect` 2.39 (1.2–2.8), `color` '#000000'.\n- `screen` (the whole picture): The screen itself: CRT curvature, a vignette, low resolution. `curvature` 0 (0–0.5), `vignette` 0 (0–1), `pixelate` 1 (1–16 px).\n\n**A look's other fields** (`defineLook(id, { description, filters, combine, … })`):\n\n- `style`: The material style everything is drawn in (lambert, toon, flat, pbr); '' keeps the scene's own.\n- `sky`: The sky preset that lights the scene (a 'sky' id: sky:hall, the torch-lit hall); '' keeps the scene's own lights.\n- `skyGradient`: How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\n- `toon`: The toon style's bands, rim, shade and dither, used when the style is 'toon'.\n- `shells`: Outline shells round the props and bodies (engine/gfx/stageShells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.\n- `resolution`: The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\n- `textures`: How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\n- `perspective`: The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\n- `strength`: How much of the whole look shows, 0 to 1: every filter's amount is scaled by it, so 0 draws the scene clean.\n<!-- lean:looks:end -->\n\n## Built-in ids and the level legend\n\n<!-- lean:ids:start -->\n**Built-in ids**, by kind, as a scene names them (`material: 'material:glow'`, `spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:bench',\nat: [x, 0, z], yaw: 0 })`); `__engine.describe('<kind>')` in a running page lists a kind's fields, and\n`define<Kind>` adds your own.\n\n- `sky:` dawn, daylight, dusk, hall, night, noon. Sky presets.\n- `material:` asphalt, barrel, barrelLid, barrelStaves, blobShadow, brick, carpet, checker, cloth, concrete, crate, default, flagstone, flame, glass, glow, iron, paint, planks, puppet, puppetGlow, puppetHalo, shingles, siding, stone, tiles, wallpaper, wood. Materials as data with three.js's classic parameters.\n- `texture:` asphalt, brick, carpet, checker, concrete, crate, dirt, flagstone, glass, grass, metal, moss, planks, plaster, runes, shingles, siding, staves, stone, tiles, wallpaper, water, wood. Seeded, periodic texture generators.\n- `geometry:` box, frustum, limb, pillar, ramp, ring, roundedBox. Shapes props, levels and bodies name by id.\n- `prop:` banner, barrel, bench, brazier, chair, chest, crate, door, garageDoor, lamp, lantern, pane, pillar, sconce, statue, switch, table. Props: things that stand in a level, as data: meshes (geometry and material by id), a body, an optional light spot, where a level places them, and interaction hooks.\n- `light:` torch. What a level's light spot shines with.\n- `emitter:` bits, block, bubbles, confetti, destroyed, dust, embers, explosion, fire, fireflies, fountain, glass, glints, hit, impact, land, magic, rain, shatter, shot, slain, slam, smoke, snow, sparks, splinters, steam. Emitters. Burst by a sim event of the type: block, destroyed, explosion, glass, hit, land, shatter, shot, slain, slam, splinters. Running at a rate (lay them into your own): bubbles, confetti, dust, embers, fire, fireflies, fountain, magic, rain, smoke, snow, sparks, steam.\n- `telegraph:` arc, cone, line, ring. Telegraphs.\n- `sfx:` blip, bodyFall, boom, bump, cancel, charge, climbGrip, coin, confirm, crouchCloth, die, door, doorBreak, doorClose, doorLocked, doorOpen, drawGun, drumCrash, drumHat, drumKick, drumOpenHat, drumSnare, drumTom, dryFire, explode, glassBreak, grab, heal, hit, holsterGun, hurt, impactBody, impactConcrete, impactDirt, impactGlass, impactMetal, impactWood, jump, jump2, key, kick, kickHit, ladderRung, land, landBody, laser, launch, mantle, oneup, pause, pickup, pistolShot, powerup, punch, punchHit, reload, rifleShot, secret, select, shoot, slide, step, stepCarpet, stepConcrete, stepGrass, stepGravel, stepMetal, stepTile, stepWood, stomp, swing, swish, switchClick, text, warp, whoosh, wind, windowSlide, zipAttach, zipRun. A sound effect.\n- `song:` adventure, boss, dungeon, title, victory. A looping tune in tracker notation.\n- `body:` humanoid. Puppet bodies.\n- `build:` adult, bulky, chibi, heroic, skeleton. Body proportions for the humanoid skeleton, in metres before size.\n- `movement:` apex, platformer. How a character moves.\n- `move:` axekick, backslash, bash, breach, cast, claw, cross, elbow, flyingkick, haymaker, hook, jab, kick, knee, overhead, plunge, rising, roundhouse, slash, spin, sweep, throw, thrust, twohand, uppercut. A named strike.\n- `weapon:` gun. Firearms.\n- `thing:` target. Things that can be hit.\n- `actionMap:` firstPerson, platformer, shmup, thirdPerson. Named actions and the physical codes bound to each.\n\n**The level legend**, a character a tile (`compileLevel`; `defineGlyph` adds one):\n\n- `t`: A brazier: an iron bowl on a stone foot, 0.75 m high (a cylinder collider, 0.3125 m in radius), with a torch spot 1 m up.\n- `o`: The dais: an octagonal platform 0.5 m up (a hull frustum), its edge a 1.5 m slope all round.\n- `+`: A doorway in a wall, 2.1 m high: walk through; the wall stands over its head.\n- `<`: A flight of stairs up to the storey above: a ramp (a hull wedge) from this floor to that one, rising toward the one side that floor meets.\n- `.`: Open floor at ground level: walkable.\n- `=`: A gallery: a walkway 1 m up, a block from the ground (a box collider).\n- `@`: Floor with the hero's spawn point (spawn:hero).\n- `|`: A ladder: open floor with a ladder against the neighbouring tile that stands highest (a wall, a tower), up to its top.\n- `_`: Floor under a low ceiling 1.4 m up (a crawlspace): crouch or slide under it.\n- `w`: A low wall (0.75 m): solid at ground level, but a body may jump onto it and stand on its top.\n- `P`: A pillar (3.5 m), 2 × 2 tiles: write it PP over PP.\n- `!`: A railing 1 m high round a landing, a deck or a stairwell: solid at ground level, a box collider.\n- `^`: Stairs: a ramp from the ground up to 1 m (a hull wedge), rising toward the one side that meets a gallery.\n- `~`: Void: no floor on this storey (a stairwell, a double height, the air beside a building).\n- `#`: A full-height wall (3 m): solid, a box collider, nobody walks or stands on it.\n- `:`: A window in a wall: solid to its sill 0.9 m up, open to its head 2.1 m up, the wall over it.\n- `1` to `9`: Floor with the spawn marker n (spawn:n): where a scene places what it numbers n, such as a mover's start.\n<!-- lean:ids:end -->\n\n## The API by area\n\n<!-- lean:api:start -->\nEvery name below is an export of `my3dge` (`import { createEngine, defineScene } from 'my3dge'`). Each has the\nfirst sentence of its doc comment in docs/API.md, and its whole manual where engine/ declares it.\n\n**Scenes**: defined as data with a setup and a step, run by x sim, x replay and createHeadless.\n`defineScene`, `defineDevAction`; types `Scene`, `SceneSpec`, `SceneAction`, `SceneSound`, `DevActionSpec`.\n\n**The world**: entities, components, systems, timers, events.\n`defineComponent`, `PHASES`; types `World`, `SimRng`, `WorldTimers`, `WorldEvents`, `Entity`, `With`, `SpawnSpec`, `ComponentOf`, `Phase`, `SystemFn`.\n\n**Registries and settings**: content as data, one schema for every setting.\n`defineKind`, `def`, `defineSettings`; types `Entry`, `Kind`, `KindSpec`, `Field`, `Schema`, `SimSettings`, `SettingValue`.\n\n**Intents**: what the sim reads from outside each step.\n`held`, `pressed`, `fromCamera`, `INTENT_KEYS`, `createInputBuffer`, `updateInputBuffer`, `released`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`, `repeated`, `BUFFER_STEPS`, `REPEAT_DELAY`, `REPEAT_RATE`; types `Intents`, `IntentValue`, `CustomIntentKey`, `InputBuffer`.\n\n**Math**: three.js's math classes and the engine's helpers (MathUtils covers clamp, lerp, damp, smoothstep).\n`Vector3`, `Quaternion`, `Matrix4`, `Euler`, `Box3`, `Sphere`, `Ray`, `Plane`, `Color`, `MathUtils`, `approach`, `angDiff`, `lerpAng`, `approachAng`, `smoothDamp`, `ease`, `swingTwist`.\n\n**Randomness**: seeded streams (the world's are w.rng('<stream>')).\n`Rng`.\n\n**Events**: emitted with w.emit, heard with w.events.on.\ntypes `EventMap`, `Listener`, `TraceRecord`.\n\n**Levels**: a legend of glyphs, level text compiled to plain data (heights, solid grid, colliders, meshes, spawns).\n`compileLevel`, `validateLevel`, `defineGlyph`, `defineLevel`, `getLevel`, `floorHeight`, `topHeight`, `solidAt`, `tileAt`, `LEVEL_FORMAT`; types `CompileOptions`, `LevelSource`, `LevelProblem`, `Glyph`, `GlyphSpec`, `LevelEntry`, `CompiledLevel`, `LevelGlyph`, `BoxCollider`, `ColliderDescriptor`, `GroundDescriptor`, `MeshDescriptor`, `SpawnPoint`, `LightSpot`, `TileRect`, `Point3`.\n\n**Animation (WP 3.4)**: the humanoid skeleton (a root plus 23 joints) and its builds, poses with three.js quaternions, blending under bone masks, additive layers, forward kinematics, SVG contact sheets and the pose checks.\n`JOINTS`, `SOCKETS`, `MASKS`, `createSkeleton`, `boneMask`, `defineBuild`, `getBuild`, `Pose`, `blendPoses`, `makeAdditive`, `addPose`, `hashPose`, `forwardKinematics`, `createWorldPose`, `jointPosition`, `jointRotation`, `jointMatrix`, `jointToWorld`, `socketPosition`, `tipPosition`, `animSheet`, `animCheck`, `twoBone`, `twoBoneRot`, `LIMBS`, `aim`, `AIM_CHAIN`, `footPlant`, `createFootPlantState`, `FOOT_LOCK`, `FOOT_PLANT`, `FootPlant`, `queryGround`, `handTo`; types `JointName`, `SocketName`, `MaskName`, `Skeleton`, `BoneMask`, `Build`, `BuildSpec`, `JointRef`, `BlendOptions`, `WorldPose`, `Sheet`, `SheetFrame`, `SheetOptions`, `SheetView`, `AnimCheckSpec`, `AnimCheckReport`, `AnimProblem`, `RigidPair`, `PointName`, `TwoBoneOptions`, `LimbEnd`, `Limb`, `AimOptions`, `AimLink`, `FootPlantOptions`, `FootPlantState`, `FootLock`, `FootPlantLayerOptions`, `GroundQueries`, `GroundProbe`, `GroundHit`.\n\n**The procedural humanoid (WP 3.6)**: my-3d2dge's gait, idle, lean, arm swing, held poses and stances as effector targets written with B(forward, right, up), solved onto the skeleton; a fixed step and a seeded stream.\n`Humanoid`, `POSES`, `STANCES`, `WEAPONS`, `B`, `turnRight`; types `HumanoidOptions`, `HumanoidInput`, `HumanoidState`, `HumanoidWeights`, `BodyMotion`, `PoseName`, `StanceName`, `Weapon`, `Effectors`, `FRU`, `LimbSide`, `Sided`.\n\n**The character animator (WP 3.7)**: a body driven through an explicit layer stack (weights, base, override, solve, then layers in clips, additive, post, physics and secondary), told its body states each step (unknown words warn with the closest), with footsteps, sockets, a trail and detail levels; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n`Animator`, `BODY_STATES`, `checkBodyStates`, `TRAILS`, `SAMPLE_STATES`, `SLOTS`, `LAYER_SLOTS`, `LOD`, `easeWeight`, `HUMANOID_WEIGHTS`; types `AnimatorOptions`, `PoseOptions`, `AnimatorReport`, `AnimEvent`, `TrailSample`, `BodyStateName`, `AnimatorInput`, `TrailName`, `SampleState`, `SlotName`, `LayerSlot`, `AnimLayer`, `WeightRates`, `WeightInfo`.\n\n**Blob and floater rigs (WP 5.3)**: my-3d2dge's squash-and-stretch blob on a minimal skeleton (a volume-preserving squash spring, a smoothed look, wings, its moves as data: bite, leap, pounce, spit) and a floater that hovers over the floor, banks into turns and carries orbiting motes; step runs in the sim, pose in the view.\n`Blob`, `BLOB`, `BLOB_JOINTS`, `BLOB_LEAP`, `BLOB_MOVES`, `blobMove`, `blobMoveTimes`, `Floater`, `FLOATER`; types `BlobOptions`, `BlobInput`, `BlobState`, `BlobJoint`, `BlobPose`, `BlobLeap`, `BlobMove`, `BlobMoveName`, `BlobMoveFrame`, `FloaterOptions`, `FloaterInput`, `FloaterState`, `FloaterPose`.\n\n**The animation library (WP 8.4)**: readable key-pose clips (format 1 and 2: parse, print, check, the normalized lens, mirroring, the decode to 36 body points), loaded per set; baked to 30 fps rotation tracks on the skeleton, retargeted onto any build (rotation copy aligned at rest, the hip-height ratio, contact IK) or given to three.js as AnimationClip JSON; played by the clip layer in the animator's clip slot, loops at the ground speed, with shardfall's walk-run switch and strike time.\n`parseClip`, `parseClipSet`, `validateClip`, `poseError`, `poseMeanError`, `clipText`, `normalizedLens`, `mirrorClip`, `decodePose`, `samplePose`, `POSE_POINTS`, `POINT_INDEX`, `bakeClip`, `sampleBaked`, `travelAt`, `BAKE_FPS`, `retargetPose`, `clipJSON`, `hipRatio`, `standingHipHeight`, `restSkeleton`, `restPoints`, `restBuild`, `RETARGET`, `loadClipLibrary`, `clipPace`, `walkRate`, `runOverWalk`, `strikeTime`, `GROUND_SPEED`, `STRIKE`, `ClipLayer`, `CLIP_LAYER`; types `ClipSet`, `ClipSource`, `RestBody`, `ClipWarning`, `Clip`, `ClipKey`, `KeyPose`, `LimbPose`, `ClipEvent`, `ClipContact`, `BakedClip`, `RetargetOptions`, `AnimationClipJSON`, `ClipLibrary`, `ClipOrigin`, `ClipLayerOptions`, `ClipPlay`, `ClipSlot`, `ClipLayerState`, `ClipLayerEvent`, `ClipStepInput`.\n\n**Moves (WP 6.1)**: moves as data in metres (the kind move: my-3d2dge's 24, converted by Appendix C's table), timelines whose events carry leftover time, attacks and combos with hit windows, sweeps and root motion, moves played on a humanoid through its body state (the arm path), moves at a moment for previews, measured hit shapes, the cone helpers and a hit's knockback velocity.\n`defineMove`, `getMove`, `resolveMove`, `MOVE_PHASES`, `LEGACY_FIELDS`, `fromLegacy`, `Timeline`, `Attack`, `Combo`, `moveAt`, `measureMove`, `strikePart`, `strikeSegment`, `inArc`, `inHitShape`, `knockbackVelocity`; types `Move`, `MoveSpec`, `MoveInput`, `MovePhase`, `LegacyMove`, `TimelinePhase`, `TimelineMark`, `TimelineEvent`, `TimelineState`, `AttackState`, `ComboState`, `Sweep`, `HitShape`, `StrikeBody`, `StrikeAnimator`, `ArmState`.\n\n**Reactions and secondary motion (WP 6.2)**: a directional flinch, knockdown, death and the get-up chosen by how the body lies (face up or face down), stepped in the sim; verlet chains (hair, tails) with bone-capsule colliders, a floor probe and a rest shape, a cape of two chains, and the squash spring as a volume-preserving root scale, drawn by an animator layer in the view.\n`Reactions`, `REACTION`, `REACTIONS`, `lyingOf`, `Chain`, `CHAIN`, `Cape`, `Secondary`, `HAIR`, `CAPE`, `TAIL`, `SQUASH`, `squashScale`, `BODY_CAPSULES`, `bodyCapsules`; types `ReactionOptions`, `ReactionState`, `ReactionBody`, `ReactionName`, `Lying`, `ChainOptions`, `ChainTuning`, `BoneCapsule`, `CapeOptions`, `SecondaryOptions`.\n\n**Animation checks (WP 6.6)**: the state matrix (each body state held at each facing, from rest and back to rest) and animCheckBody, which checks a whole body over it: every pose, the same hashes twice, 1/60 s against 1/120 s; and the camera presets sheets of it are drawn from.","numLines":120,"startLine":517,"totalLines":854}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0182UuzPAdFiQZpx13BAvDGy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9QBZpHdMS99eVcyvTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UeCzwT3j19QbgzyehZAwdw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; cat engine/input/actionMaps.ts | sed -n 1,220p; echo ------; sed -n 1,90p engine/input/input.ts","description":"Read action maps and input docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20990,"cache_read_input_tokens":145774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20990},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"f0258c63-be41-4f86-b8a5-0fa088362fc3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:05.708Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9QBAGizL1sx6XA71Ev","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UeCzwT3j19QbgzyehZAwdw":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; cat engine/input/actionMaps.ts | sed -n 1,220p; echo ------; sed -n 1,90p engine/input/input.ts","description":"Read action maps and input docs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UeCzwT3j19QbgzyehZAwdw","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\n *\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\n *\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n * shared registry when this module loads.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n *\n * @example\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\n\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n});\n\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n  'Escape',\n  'PadStart',\n  'PadHome',\n  'F5',\n  'F11',\n  'F12',\n  'MetaLeft',\n  'MetaRight',\n]);\n\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\n  actions: {\n    type: 'object',\n    required: true,\n    description:\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\n  },\n  move: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\n  },\n  values: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Custom intent key (\"game:throttle\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\n  },\n  look: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description: \"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\",\n  },\n  aimWith: {\n    type: 'string',\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\n    default: 'none',\n    description:\n      \"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\",\n  },\n  lock: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description:\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\n  },\n  view: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description:\n      \"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\",\n  },\n  reserved: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\n  },\n} as const satisfies Schema;\n\n/** An action map entry. */\nexport type ActionMap = Entry & {\n  readonly description: string;\n  readonly actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  readonly move: readonly string[];\n  readonly values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  readonly look: boolean;\n  readonly aimWith: AimRule;\n  readonly lock: boolean;\n  readonly view: readonly string[];\n  readonly reserved: readonly string[];\n};\n\n/** An action name: a lower-case word, letters and digits. */\nconst ACTION = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$/;\n\n/** The problems of a map beyond its fields (the file comment lists them). */\nfunction mapProblems(map: ActionMap): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  const reserved = new Set([...RESERVED_CODES, ...map.reserved]);\n  for (const [action, codes] of Object.entries(map.actions)) {\n    if (!ACTION.test(action)) problems.push(`the action ${show(action)} must be a lower-case word (jump, skill2)`);\n    if (Object.hasOwn(SYSTEM_ACTIONS, action)) problems.push(`${action} is a system action, never rebound: rename it`);\n    if (!Array.isArray(codes)) {\n      problems.push(`actions.${action} is ${show(codes)}; it must be a list of codes`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    for (const code of codes) {\n      if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} holds ${show(code)}, not a code (KeyW, MouseLeft, PadSouth)`);\n      else if (reserved.has(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} binds the reserved code ${code}`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (map.move.length !== 4) problems.push(`move names ${map.move.length} actions: give forward, back, left, right`);\n  for (const action of map.move) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`move names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n  }\n  for (const action of map.view) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`view names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    else if (map.move.includes(action)) problems.push(`view names ${action}, a move action`);\n  }\n  for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) {\n    if (!/^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(key)) problems.push(`values key ${show(key)} must be \"game:name\"`);\n    if (typeof action !== 'string' || !Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) {\n      problems.push(`values.${key} names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const code of map.reserved) if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`reserved holds ${show(code)}, not a code`);\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `actionMap` on `registry` unless it has it. */\nexport function actionMapKind(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('actionMap')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('actionMap', {\n    description:\n      'Named actions and the physical codes bound to each (keys by KeyboardEvent.code, mouse, pad by position): what the input devices turn into intents.',\n    fields: ACTION_MAP_FIELDS,\n    defineWith: \"defineActionMap('actionMap:<name>', { actions: { jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'] } })\",\n    check: (entry) => mapProblems(entry as ActionMap),\n  });\n}\n\n/** How an action map is written. */\nexport interface ActionMapSpec {\n  description?: string;\n  actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  move?: readonly [string, string, string, string];\n  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  look?: boolean;\n  aimWith?: AimRule;\n  lock?: boolean;\n  view?: readonly string[];\n  reserved?: readonly string[];\n}\n\n/** Registers an action map (on the shared registry by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each problem. */\nexport function defineActionMap(id: string, spec: ActionMapSpec, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.def('actionMap', id, spec as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as ActionMap;\n}\n\n/** The action map `id`. Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest ids. */\nexport function getActionMap(id: string, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.get('actionMap', id) as ActionMap;\n}\n\n/** Every action map, sorted by id. */\nexport function listActionMaps(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap[] {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.list('actionMap') as ActionMap[];\n}\n\n/** Walking on WASD, the arrows, the d-pad and the left stick: every preset's `move` actions. */\nconst WALK = {\n  forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n};\n------\n/**\n * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, those pressed since the last sample (a code that went\n * down, so a tap shorter than a frame still presses); `move`, the map's four move actions as `[right − left, forward −\n * back]` turned by `fromCamera(camera.yaw(), …)`, so W walks away from the camera; `cam`, the camera's heading; `look`\n * (its yaw and pitch) for maps with `look`; `aim`, the camera's point for the map's `aimWith` rule from the free\n * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\n * `view` actions and the system layer (pause, menus) are never buttons in it: `held`, `pressed` and `strength` give\n * every action to the app and the UI, and `onView` hears a view action as it is pressed (a key at once, a pad button at\n * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n * pointer lock and the right stick, scaled by the view settings `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts; the wheel; a map that\n * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n * `use(map)` switches the map live (one per camera mode, WP 13.9), what is held read through it from the next sample;\n * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n * on (WP 13.20) is held back as it goes down, until it is a tap or a hold (`sample`).\n *\n * Clearing: a page blur, the page going hidden and `clear()` let go of every held code and drop pending presses, so\n * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants: nothing here reads a clock; edges are counted per sample; a code is held only between its press and\n * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:482-512, 542-555, 594-622` (the input object, blur, `move`, `tick`),\n * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n *\n * @example\n * const window = new EventTarget();\n * const input = createInput({ window, document: new EventTarget(), element: new EventTarget() });\n * const key = (type: string, code: string) => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(type), { code }));\n * ['KeyW', 'Space'].forEach((code) => key('keydown', code)), key('keyup', 'Space'); // a tap between two frames\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => Math.PI / 2 }); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], cam: 1.5707963267948966, p: ['jump'] }\n * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => 0 }).move; // [0, 1]: still held; the camera turned, so W walks +Z now\n * @see engine/input/input.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SYSTEM_ACTIONS } from './actionMaps';\nimport { createBindings, pickLabel, type Bindings, type BindingsStorage } from './bindings';\nimport { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\nimport { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\nimport type { AimDevices, AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\nimport { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\nimport { fromCamera } from './intents';\nimport { lookOptions, scaleLook, type LookOptions } from './look';\n\n/** A camera as the input reads it (the app's, over its view): its heading, its pitch for the look, and the aim. */\nexport interface CameraLike {\n  yaw(): number;\n  pose?(): { readonly pitch: number };\n  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n}\n\n/** How an input is made; in a page every field has its default. */\nexport interface InputOptions {\n  /** The action map's id (`actionMap:thirdPerson`) or ready bindings. */\n  map?: string | Bindings;\n  /** Where bindings made from an id are saved (the page's `localStorage`). */\n  storage?: BindingsStorage;\n  /** Where keys, releases, blur and gamepad events arrive (`window`). */\n  window?: EventTarget;\n  /** The document: visibility and pointer lock (`document`). */\n  document?: MouseTargets['document'] & { visibilityState?: string };\n  /** The game's element, the canvas: mouse presses, wheel and pointer lock (`document.body`). */\n  element?: MouseTargets['element'];\n  /** Where pads come from (`navigator.getGamepads`). */\n  gamepads?: GamepadSource;\n  /** The stick deadzone (0.18), clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. */\n  deadzone?: number;\n  /** A view action pressed (the map's `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (see the file comment). */\n  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n  /** The look settings now (`lookOptions` over the view settings `input.*`), read every frame; defaults when absent. */\n  look?: () => LookOptions;\n  /** The keyboard layout for prompts (`readKeyboardLayout()`). */\n  layout?: ReadonlyMap<string, string>;\n  /** The `touch` setting now (`auto`, `on`, `off`): touch mode follows the screen unless forced. */\n  touchMode?: () => TouchSetting;\n  /** A tap on a touch tap control (`data-tap`: `menu`) or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\n  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\n  /** Where the map is registered (the shared registry). */\n  registry?: Registry;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"28f63ac3-e744-4451-b39b-e2aaa2245230","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:05.723Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Action maps and presets (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Common ground): the registry kind `actionMap`, a set\n * of named actions with the physical codes bound to each (engine/input/codes.ts), as Unity's action maps and Godot's\n * InputMap hold them; the presets; and the system layer, which no player rebinds.\n *\n * An action is a button the sim reads: held actions arrive as the intents' `b`, pressed ones as `p`\n * (engine/input/intents.ts). The four actions a map names in `move` (forward, back, left, right) are not buttons:\n * their strengths make the move axes `[right − left, forward − back]`, so keys walk at full speed and a half-pushed\n * stick at half, and `fromCamera` turns the axes into a world direction. `values` writes an action's analog strength\n * (a trigger) as a custom intent. `look: true` (first person, the shooter) adds the camera's view direction as `look`,\n * `aimWith` names the rule that gives the intents' `aim` its point (engine/input/aim.ts: the screen centre's ray, the\n * pointer's onto the floor, or none; the action `aim`, where a map has one, raises the sights), and `lock: true` takes\n * the pointer lock on a click so the mouse turns the view (with the cursor free, it points and aims). The actions a\n * map names in `view` (a camera switch, a view's turn) are the page's: bound and rebound like the others, never\n * buttons in the intents (`createEngine({ onView })`). A game with several camera modes gives each its own map\n * (`createEngine({ actionMap })`, WP 13.9).\n *\n * The system layer (`SYSTEM_ACTIONS`): pause, and the menu's accept, cancel and directions. It is always active\n * beside the map, never rebound, and never part of the intents: the app and the UI read it (`input.pressed('pause')`),\n * so remapping movement never breaks a menu (the lesson of `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md`). `RESERVED_CODES` (the\n * pause buttons, and keys the browser or system keeps) and a map's own `reserved` codes are refused by rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants (`CORE_BAD_SPEC` when broken): every code is valid (`isCode`), action names are lower-case words\n * (`jump`, `skill2`) and none is a system action, `move` names four actions of the map and `view` others, `values` keys\n * are namespaced custom intents naming actions of the map, and no action binds a reserved code. The presets are registered on the\n * shared registry when this module loads.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:670-693` (`Input.DEFAULT`, `PLATFORMER`, `SHMUP`, `MENU_KEYS`) with 3D\n * movement, and shardfall's layer that is never rebound (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:131-161`).\n *\n * @example\n * const map = getActionMap('actionMap:thirdPerson');\n * map.actions.jump; // ['Space', 'PadSouth']\n * map.move; // ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right']\n * SYSTEM_ACTIONS.pause; // ['Escape', 'PadStart']\n * listActionMaps().map((entry) => entry.id); // ['actionMap:firstPerson', 'actionMap:platformer', …]\n * @see engine/input/bindings.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { AIM_RULES, type AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { isCode } from './codes';\n\n/** The system layer: action → codes. Always active, never rebound, never in the intents. */\nexport const SYSTEM_ACTIONS: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = Object.freeze({\n  pause: ['Escape', 'PadStart'],\n  uiAccept: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'PadSouth'],\n  uiCancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'PadEast'],\n  uiUp: ['ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  uiDown: ['ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  uiLeft: ['ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  uiRight: ['ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n});\n\n/** Codes no action map binds: the pause buttons, and keys the browser or the system keeps. */\nexport const RESERVED_CODES: readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n  'Escape',\n  'PadStart',\n  'PadHome',\n  'F5',\n  'F11',\n  'F12',\n  'MetaLeft',\n  'MetaRight',\n]);\n\n/** The fields of an `actionMap` entry. */\nconst ACTION_MAP_FIELDS = {\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the map is for, in plain words.' },\n  actions: {\n    type: 'object',\n    required: true,\n    description:\n      'Action name → the codes bound to it (KeyboardEvent.code, MouseLeft…, PadSouth…, PadLeftStickUp…): held actions are the intents b, pressed ones p.',\n  },\n  move: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: ['forward', 'back', 'left', 'right'],\n    description: 'The four actions that walk, as forward, back, left, right: their strengths make the move axes.',\n  },\n  values: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description:\n      'Custom intent key (\"game:throttle\") → action: its analog strength (0 to 1, a trigger) is that intent.',\n  },\n  look: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description: \"True for first person and the shooter: the intents carry look = [the camera's yaw, its pitch].\",\n  },\n  aimWith: {\n    type: 'string',\n    enum: AIM_RULES,\n    default: 'none',\n    description:\n      \"What the intents' aim holds: none; centre, the point the screen centre's ray meets (first person, the shooter); pointer, the pointer's ray onto the player's floor or a right stick's push (isometric, top-down).\",\n  },\n  lock: {\n    type: 'boolean',\n    default: false,\n    description:\n      'True when the mouse turns the view: a click on the game takes the pointer lock, which pause and Escape give back.',\n  },\n  view: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description:\n      \"Actions the page reads for its view (a camera switch, a view's turn): bound and rebound like the others, never buttons in the intents.\",\n  },\n  reserved: {\n    type: 'array',\n    items: { type: 'string' },\n    default: [],\n    description: 'Codes the game keeps for its own hotkeys: rebinding refuses them, as it refuses RESERVED_CODES.',\n  },\n} as const satisfies Schema;\n\n/** An action map entry. */\nexport type ActionMap = Entry & {\n  readonly description: string;\n  readonly actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  readonly move: readonly string[];\n  readonly values: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  readonly look: boolean;\n  readonly aimWith: AimRule;\n  readonly lock: boolean;\n  readonly view: readonly string[];\n  readonly reserved: readonly string[];\n};\n\n/** An action name: a lower-case word, letters and digits. */\nconst ACTION = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*$/;\n\n/** The problems of a map beyond its fields (the file comment lists them). */\nfunction mapProblems(map: ActionMap): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  const reserved = new Set([...RESERVED_CODES, ...map.reserved]);\n  for (const [action, codes] of Object.entries(map.actions)) {\n    if (!ACTION.test(action)) problems.push(`the action ${show(action)} must be a lower-case word (jump, skill2)`);\n    if (Object.hasOwn(SYSTEM_ACTIONS, action)) problems.push(`${action} is a system action, never rebound: rename it`);\n    if (!Array.isArray(codes)) {\n      problems.push(`actions.${action} is ${show(codes)}; it must be a list of codes`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    for (const code of codes) {\n      if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} holds ${show(code)}, not a code (KeyW, MouseLeft, PadSouth)`);\n      else if (reserved.has(code)) problems.push(`actions.${action} binds the reserved code ${code}`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (map.move.length !== 4) problems.push(`move names ${map.move.length} actions: give forward, back, left, right`);\n  for (const action of map.move) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`move names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n  }\n  for (const action of map.view) {\n    if (!Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) problems.push(`view names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    else if (map.move.includes(action)) problems.push(`view names ${action}, a move action`);\n  }\n  for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) {\n    if (!/^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/.test(key)) problems.push(`values key ${show(key)} must be \"game:name\"`);\n    if (typeof action !== 'string' || !Object.hasOwn(map.actions, action)) {\n      problems.push(`values.${key} names ${show(action)}, which actions lacks`);\n    }\n  }\n  for (const code of map.reserved) if (!isCode(code)) problems.push(`reserved holds ${show(code)}, not a code`);\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `actionMap` on `registry` unless it has it. */\nexport function actionMapKind(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('actionMap')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('actionMap', {\n    description:\n      'Named actions and the physical codes bound to each (keys by KeyboardEvent.code, mouse, pad by position): what the input devices turn into intents.',\n    fields: ACTION_MAP_FIELDS,\n    defineWith: \"defineActionMap('actionMap:<name>', { actions: { jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'] } })\",\n    check: (entry) => mapProblems(entry as ActionMap),\n  });\n}\n\n/** How an action map is written. */\nexport interface ActionMapSpec {\n  description?: string;\n  actions: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>>;\n  move?: readonly [string, string, string, string];\n  values?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\n  look?: boolean;\n  aimWith?: AimRule;\n  lock?: boolean;\n  view?: readonly string[];\n  reserved?: readonly string[];\n}\n\n/** Registers an action map (on the shared registry by default). Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each problem. */\nexport function defineActionMap(id: string, spec: ActionMapSpec, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.def('actionMap', id, spec as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as ActionMap;\n}\n\n/** The action map `id`. Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest ids. */\nexport function getActionMap(id: string, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.get('actionMap', id) as ActionMap;\n}\n\n/** Every action map, sorted by id. */\nexport function listActionMaps(registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): ActionMap[] {\n  actionMapKind(registry);\n  return registry.list('actionMap') as ActionMap[];\n}\n\n/** Walking on WASD, the arrows, the d-pad and the left stick: every preset's `move` actions. */\nconst WALK = {\n  forward: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'PadUp', 'PadLeftStickUp'],\n  back: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'PadDown', 'PadLeftStickDown'],\n  left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'PadLeft', 'PadLeftStickLeft'],\n  right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'PadRight', 'PadLeftStickRight'],\n};\n------\n/**\n * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, those pressed since the last sample (a code that went\n * down, so a tap shorter than a frame still presses); `move`, the map's four move actions as `[right − left, forward −\n * back]` turned by `fromCamera(camera.yaw(), …)`, so W walks away from the camera; `cam`, the camera's heading; `look`\n * (its yaw and pitch) for maps with `look`; `aim`, the camera's point for the map's `aimWith` rule from the free\n * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\n * `view` actions and the system layer (pause, menus) are never buttons in it: `held`, `pressed` and `strength` give\n * every action to the app and the UI, and `onView` hears a view action as it is pressed (a key at once, a pad button at\n * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n * pointer lock and the right stick, scaled by the view settings `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts; the wheel; a map that\n * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n * `use(map)` switches the map live (one per camera mode, WP 13.9), what is held read through it from the next sample;\n * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n * on (WP 13.20) is held back as it goes down, until it is a tap or a hold (`sample`).\n *\n * Clearing: a page blur, the page going hidden and `clear()` let go of every held code and drop pending presses, so\n * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants: nothing here reads a clock; edges are counted per sample; a code is held only between its press and\n * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:482-512, 542-555, 594-622` (the input object, blur, `move`, `tick`),\n * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n *\n * @example\n * const window = new EventTarget();\n * const input = createInput({ window, document: new EventTarget(), element: new EventTarget() });\n * const key = (type: string, code: string) => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(type), { code }));\n * ['KeyW', 'Space'].forEach((code) => key('keydown', code)), key('keyup', 'Space'); // a tap between two frames\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => Math.PI / 2 }); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], cam: 1.5707963267948966, p: ['jump'] }\n * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => 0 }).move; // [0, 1]: still held; the camera turned, so W walks +Z now\n * @see engine/input/input.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SYSTEM_ACTIONS } from './actionMaps';\nimport { createBindings, pickLabel, type Bindings, type BindingsStorage } from './bindings';\nimport { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\nimport { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\nimport type { AimDevices, AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\nimport { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\nimport { fromCamera } from './intents';\nimport { lookOptions, scaleLook, type LookOptions } from './look';\n\n/** A camera as the input reads it (the app's, over its view): its heading, its pitch for the look, and the aim. */\nexport interface CameraLike {\n  yaw(): number;\n  pose?(): { readonly pitch: number };\n  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n}\n\n/** How an input is made; in a page every field has its default. */\nexport interface InputOptions {\n  /** The action map's id (`actionMap:thirdPerson`) or ready bindings. */\n  map?: string | Bindings;\n  /** Where bindings made from an id are saved (the page's `localStorage`). */\n  storage?: BindingsStorage;\n  /** Where keys, releases, blur and gamepad events arrive (`window`). */\n  window?: EventTarget;\n  /** The document: visibility and pointer lock (`document`). */\n  document?: MouseTargets['document'] & { visibilityState?: string };\n  /** The game's element, the canvas: mouse presses, wheel and pointer lock (`document.body`). */\n  element?: MouseTargets['element'];\n  /** Where pads come from (`navigator.getGamepads`). */\n  gamepads?: GamepadSource;\n  /** The stick deadzone (0.18), clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. */\n  deadzone?: number;\n  /** A view action pressed (the map's `view`: a camera switch, a view's turn), as it happens (see the file comment). */\n  onView?: (action: string) => void;\n  /** The look settings now (`lookOptions` over the view settings `input.*`), read every frame; defaults when absent. */\n  look?: () => LookOptions;\n  /** The keyboard layout for prompts (`readKeyboardLayout()`). */\n  layout?: ReadonlyMap<string, string>;\n  /** The `touch` setting now (`auto`, `on`, `off`): touch mode follows the screen unless forced. */\n  touchMode?: () => TouchSetting;\n  /** A tap on a touch tap control (`data-tap`: `menu`) or on the open game (`game`), as it happens. */\n  onTap?: (name: string) => void;\n  /** Where the map is registered (the shared registry). */\n  registry?: Registry;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UeCzwT3j19QbgzyehZAwdw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9QBZpHdMS99eVcyvTN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JquYndG4ak2dvv1Pe9PGQ4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; sed -n 1,120p engine/ui/menu.ts; echo ------; ls engine/input/devices; sed -n 1,70p engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts; echo ------; sed -n 1,60p engine/audio/runtime.ts 2>/dev/null || ls engine/audio","description":"Read menu widget, gamepad device and audio runtime docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20990,"cache_read_input_tokens":145774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20990},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"f442edf6-0679-4f95-a1c6-a6d6b122d93f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:08.236Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9QBAGizL1sx6XA71Ev","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JquYndG4ak2dvv1Pe9PGQ4":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; sed -n 1,120p engine/ui/menu.ts; echo ------; ls engine/input/devices; sed -n 1,70p engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts; echo ------; sed -n 1,60p engine/audio/runtime.ts 2>/dev/null || ls engine/audio","description":"Read menu widget, gamepad device and audio runtime docs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JquYndG4ak2dvv1Pe9PGQ4","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The menu (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50): a list with a cursor, for title screens, pause menus, settings and\n * shops, as HTML/CSS over the overlay. `createMenu(parent, items, { input, sound, title, place, onPick, onCancel,\n * onMove, send })` makes it open; `update(dt)` each frame reads the page's input and returns true when it picked or\n * cancelled.\n *\n * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\n * move the cursor over the items, round the ends, past disabled ones; `uiAccept` picks the item under it, `uiCancel`\n * calls `onCancel` when there is one; a pointer moving over an item moves the cursor there (a menu opening under a still\n * pointer, or rows shifting under it, moves none), a click picks it. A gamepad drives the menu with its buttons, and any\n * other panel through the pad's cursor (`createPadCursor`).\n *\n * Picks that change play: the system layer never enters the intents (engine/input/actionMaps.ts), so a menu never\n * reaches the sim itself. An item with an `id` is handed to `send(id)` when picked, which the page turns into input\n * the session records (a dev action, `__engine.actions.run`, or a custom intent for the next step), so the replay\n * holds the pick; `onPick` hears every pick, for what only the page changes (a look, a panel).\n *\n * Elements: `[data-ui=menu]` (`data-id`, `data-value` the cursor's index; `data-place`), its `[data-ui=menu-title]`,\n * and a `[data-ui=item]` per item (`data-id` its id or index, `data-value` `selected`, `disabled` or empty). Cues: `move`,\n * `pick`, `cancel`. Invariants: presentation only; `active: false` reads no input; the cursor never rests on a disabled\n * item while another is enabled. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:4288-4330` (`Menu`: items, disabled ones\n * skipped, onPick, onCancel, onMove) and shardfall's rule that menu actions reach the game as input (§5.8).\n *\n * @example\n * // browser: the menu needs a page\n * // const pause = createMenu(ui.root, ['Resume', { label: 'Restart', id: 'restart' }], {\n * //   input, title: 'Paused', onCancel: () => pause.remove(), send: (id) => engine.actions.run(id) });\n * // pause.update(dt); // each frame\n * @see engine/ui/menu.test.ts\n * @see tests/e2e/ui.spec.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { createRepeat, setText, uiElement, widgetStyle, type UiInput, type UiSound } from './widgets';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const MENU_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\n  UI_BAD_MENU: {\n    template: 'menu: {problem}',\n    fix: \"give items as strings or { label, id?, disabled? }, and update(dt) the frame's seconds, 0 or more\",\n    doc: 'Raised by the menu (engine/ui/menu.ts) for an item that is neither a string nor `{ label, id?, disabled? }`, or a frame time that is not a number of seconds from 0.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** One menu item: its label, or `{ label, id, disabled }` (an `id` is sent when picked). */\nexport type MenuItem = string | { readonly label: string; readonly id?: string; readonly disabled?: boolean };\n\n/** Where the menu stands. */\nexport type MenuPlace = 'center' | 'top' | 'bottom';\n\n/** How a menu is made. */\nexport interface MenuOptions {\n  input: UiInput;\n  sound?: UiSound;\n  /** Its id (`data-id`). */\n  id?: string;\n  title?: string;\n  /** Where it stands (`center`). */\n  place?: MenuPlace;\n  onPick?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\n  onCancel?(): void;\n  onMove?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\n  /** Hands a picked item's id to the page, which records it as input (see the file comment). */\n  send?(id: string): void;\n}\n\n/** The menu (see the file comment). */\nexport interface Menu {\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\n  /** The cursor's index, and its item. */\n  readonly index: number;\n  readonly selected: MenuItem | undefined;\n  /** False: it reads no input (another menu over it has the input). */\n  active: boolean;\n  /** Reads the input for a frame of `dt` s; true when it picked or cancelled. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\n  update(dt: number): boolean;\n  /** Moves the cursor to `index` (a disabled item: the next enabled one after it). */\n  select(index: number): void;\n  /** Picks the item under the cursor, as accept does; false when it is disabled. */\n  pick(): boolean;\n  /** Replaces the items, keeping the cursor where it can. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\n  setItems(items: readonly MenuItem[]): void;\n  remove(): void;\n}\n\nconst labelOf = (item: MenuItem) => (typeof item === 'string' ? item : item.label);\nconst off = (item: MenuItem | undefined) => typeof item === 'object' && item.disabled === true;\n\n/** Makes an open menu of `items` in `parent` (see the file comment). */\nexport function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\n  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\n  parent.append(el);\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\n  let index = 0;\n\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\n    let at = from;\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\n    return at;\n  };\n  const draw = () => {\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\n      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\n    });\n  };\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\n    if (!list.length) return;\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\n    if (next === index) return;\n    index = next;\n    sound('move');\n    draw();\n------\ndevices.test.ts\ngamepad.ts\ninspector.ts\nkeyboard.ts\nmouse.ts\npadScript.ts\ntouch.ts\nvirtual.test.ts\nvirtual.ts\n/**\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\n *\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\n * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\n *\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\n *\n * @example\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\n * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\n */\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\n\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\nexport interface GamepadLike {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly index: number;\n  readonly connected: boolean;\n  readonly mapping?: string;\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\n}\n\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\n\n/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\n\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\n\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\n  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\n  return [x * k, y * k];\n}\n\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\n  poll(): void;\n  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\n  readonly index: number | null;\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\n  release(): void;\n}\n\n/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\n------\napi.ts\ndata\ndsp\nruntime","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"e4b21393-e5c6-436a-9da0-b9da73725c43","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:08.255Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The menu (PLAN.md §6.7, WP 10.6, I-50): a list with a cursor, for title screens, pause menus, settings and\n * shops, as HTML/CSS over the overlay. `createMenu(parent, items, { input, sound, title, place, onPick, onCancel,\n * onMove, send })` makes it open; `update(dt)` each frame reads the page's input and returns true when it picked or\n * cancelled.\n *\n * `uiUp` and `uiDown` (keys, the pad's D-pad and left stick; held, they repeat: engine/ui/widgets.ts `createRepeat`)\n * move the cursor over the items, round the ends, past disabled ones; `uiAccept` picks the item under it, `uiCancel`\n * calls `onCancel` when there is one; a pointer moving over an item moves the cursor there (a menu opening under a still\n * pointer, or rows shifting under it, moves none), a click picks it. A gamepad drives the menu with its buttons, and any\n * other panel through the pad's cursor (`createPadCursor`).\n *\n * Picks that change play: the system layer never enters the intents (engine/input/actionMaps.ts), so a menu never\n * reaches the sim itself. An item with an `id` is handed to `send(id)` when picked, which the page turns into input\n * the session records (a dev action, `__engine.actions.run`, or a custom intent for the next step), so the replay\n * holds the pick; `onPick` hears every pick, for what only the page changes (a look, a panel).\n *\n * Elements: `[data-ui=menu]` (`data-id`, `data-value` the cursor's index; `data-place`), its `[data-ui=menu-title]`,\n * and a `[data-ui=item]` per item (`data-id` its id or index, `data-value` `selected`, `disabled` or empty). Cues: `move`,\n * `pick`, `cancel`. Invariants: presentation only; `active: false` reads no input; the cursor never rests on a disabled\n * item while another is enabled. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:4288-4330` (`Menu`: items, disabled ones\n * skipped, onPick, onCancel, onMove) and shardfall's rule that menu actions reach the game as input (§5.8).\n *\n * @example\n * // browser: the menu needs a page\n * // const pause = createMenu(ui.root, ['Resume', { label: 'Restart', id: 'restart' }], {\n * //   input, title: 'Paused', onCancel: () => pause.remove(), send: (id) => engine.actions.run(id) });\n * // pause.update(dt); // each frame\n * @see engine/ui/menu.test.ts\n * @see tests/e2e/ui.spec.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { createRepeat, setText, uiElement, widgetStyle, type UiInput, type UiSound } from './widgets';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const MENU_CODES = defineCodes('ui', {\n  UI_BAD_MENU: {\n    template: 'menu: {problem}',\n    fix: \"give items as strings or { label, id?, disabled? }, and update(dt) the frame's seconds, 0 or more\",\n    doc: 'Raised by the menu (engine/ui/menu.ts) for an item that is neither a string nor `{ label, id?, disabled? }`, or a frame time that is not a number of seconds from 0.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** One menu item: its label, or `{ label, id, disabled }` (an `id` is sent when picked). */\nexport type MenuItem = string | { readonly label: string; readonly id?: string; readonly disabled?: boolean };\n\n/** Where the menu stands. */\nexport type MenuPlace = 'center' | 'top' | 'bottom';\n\n/** How a menu is made. */\nexport interface MenuOptions {\n  input: UiInput;\n  sound?: UiSound;\n  /** Its id (`data-id`). */\n  id?: string;\n  title?: string;\n  /** Where it stands (`center`). */\n  place?: MenuPlace;\n  onPick?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\n  onCancel?(): void;\n  onMove?(index: number, item: MenuItem): void;\n  /** Hands a picked item's id to the page, which records it as input (see the file comment). */\n  send?(id: string): void;\n}\n\n/** The menu (see the file comment). */\nexport interface Menu {\n  readonly el: HTMLElement;\n  /** The cursor's index, and its item. */\n  readonly index: number;\n  readonly selected: MenuItem | undefined;\n  /** False: it reads no input (another menu over it has the input). */\n  active: boolean;\n  /** Reads the input for a frame of `dt` s; true when it picked or cancelled. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\n  update(dt: number): boolean;\n  /** Moves the cursor to `index` (a disabled item: the next enabled one after it). */\n  select(index: number): void;\n  /** Picks the item under the cursor, as accept does; false when it is disabled. */\n  pick(): boolean;\n  /** Replaces the items, keeping the cursor where it can. Throws `UI_BAD_MENU`. */\n  setItems(items: readonly MenuItem[]): void;\n  remove(): void;\n}\n\nconst labelOf = (item: MenuItem) => (typeof item === 'string' ? item : item.label);\nconst off = (item: MenuItem | undefined) => typeof item === 'object' && item.disabled === true;\n\n/** Makes an open menu of `items` in `parent` (see the file comment). */\nexport function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\n  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\n  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\n  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\n  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\n  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\n  parent.append(el);\n  const repeat = createRepeat();\n  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\n  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\n  let index = 0;\n\n  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\n  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\n    let at = from;\n    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\n    return at;\n  };\n  const draw = () => {\n    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\n    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\n      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\n      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\n    });\n  };\n  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\n    if (!list.length) return;\n    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\n    if (next === index) return;\n    index = next;\n    sound('move');\n    draw();\n------\ndevices.test.ts\ngamepad.ts\ninspector.ts\nkeyboard.ts\nmouse.ts\npadScript.ts\ntouch.ts\nvirtual.test.ts\nvirtual.ts\n/**\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\n *\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\n * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\n *\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\n *\n * @example\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\n * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\n */\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\n\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\nexport interface GamepadLike {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly index: number;\n  readonly connected: boolean;\n  readonly mapping?: string;\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\n}\n\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\n\n/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\n\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\n\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\n  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\n  return [x * k, y * k];\n}\n\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\n  poll(): void;\n  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\n  readonly index: number | null;\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\n  release(): void;\n}\n\n/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\n------\napi.ts\ndata\ndsp\nruntime","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JquYndG4ak2dvv1Pe9PGQ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
