{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SYJsBcoBVBHVZFNT4xyUuj","type":"tool_result","content":"v24.22.1\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/setup.sh: the development platform (PLAN.md §6.10, WP 0.1). Idempotent: run it as often as you like.\n#\n#   bash scripts/setup.sh\n#\n# 1. Node. When the active `node` is not the version in .nvmrc, it downloads the official Linux x64 build from\n#    nodejs.org, checks it against SHASUMS256.txt, unpacks it under ~/.cache/my3dge/ (once), puts it first on PATH\n#    for the rest of this script, and appends that PATH to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE when the variable is set, so later\n#    Claude Code shells use it. Offline, it says so and keeps the active Node (everything also runs on Node 22;\n#    Node goldens are recorded on 24).\n# 2. The read-only source checkouts. $MY3D2DGE_SRC (my-3d2dge@e37e4ee) and $SHARDFALL_SRC (shardfall@fa2dab6) are\n#    resolved in this order: the environment variable; else an existing local clone, cloned with\n#    `git clone --shared` into .cache/src-3d2dge or .cache/src-shardfall; else a clone from GitHub. Either clone is\n#    then detached at the pinned commit. The resolved paths are printed, and appended to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE when set.\n#    In a game made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, tools/game/new-game.mjs), nothing ports from the\n#    sources, so this step is skipped.\n# 3. Chromium. Outside the cloud container (no /opt/pw-browsers/chromium and no $CHROMIUM_PATH), it downloads Chrome for\n#    Testing at the platform's release (tools/deps.json) from Google's official bucket into ~/.cache/my3dge/ (once);\n#    tools/lib/browser.ts finds it there, so no shell state is needed. Offline, it warns and T2 cannot run.\n# 4. `npm ci`.\n#\n# Exit status: 0 when the dependencies are installed (an offline Node download or an unreachable source only warns);\n# 1 when `npm ci` fails.\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nrepo_root=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$repo_root\"\n\nsay() { printf 'setup: %s\\n' \"$*\"; }\n\n# Appends one line to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE, unless the variable is unset or the line is already there.\nappend_env_line() {\n  local line=\"$1\"\n  [ -n \"${CLAUDE_ENV_FILE:-}\" ] || return 0\n  touch \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\"\n  grep -qxF -- \"$line\" \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\" || printf '%s\\n' \"$line\" >>\"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\"\n}\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nnpm warn deprecated eslint@9.39.5: This version is no longer supported. Please see https://eslint.org/version-support for other options.\n\nadded 590 packages in 6s\n\nreal\t0m6.047s\nuser\t0m4.418s\nsys\t0m4.907s\n284\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   Start at  21:25:19\n   Duration  4.99s (transform 4.35s, setup 100ms, import 5.57s, tests 2.06s, environment 0ms)\n\nJSON report written to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game/out/test/report.json\n\nreal\t0m5.310s\nuser\t0m5.992s\nsys\t0m0.929s","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"0904ef42-70d7-40c8-b9b8-ee2f8b714628","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:24.188Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"v24.22.1\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# scripts/setup.sh: the development platform (PLAN.md §6.10, WP 0.1). Idempotent: run it as often as you like.\n#\n#   bash scripts/setup.sh\n#\n# 1. Node. When the active `node` is not the version in .nvmrc, it downloads the official Linux x64 build from\n#    nodejs.org, checks it against SHASUMS256.txt, unpacks it under ~/.cache/my3dge/ (once), puts it first on PATH\n#    for the rest of this script, and appends that PATH to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE when the variable is set, so later\n#    Claude Code shells use it. Offline, it says so and keeps the active Node (everything also runs on Node 22;\n#    Node goldens are recorded on 24).\n# 2. The read-only source checkouts. $MY3D2DGE_SRC (my-3d2dge@e37e4ee) and $SHARDFALL_SRC (shardfall@fa2dab6) are\n#    resolved in this order: the environment variable; else an existing local clone, cloned with\n#    `git clone --shared` into .cache/src-3d2dge or .cache/src-shardfall; else a clone from GitHub. Either clone is\n#    then detached at the pinned commit. The resolved paths are printed, and appended to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE when set.\n#    In a game made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, tools/game/new-game.mjs), nothing ports from the\n#    sources, so this step is skipped.\n# 3. Chromium. Outside the cloud container (no /opt/pw-browsers/chromium and no $CHROMIUM_PATH), it downloads Chrome for\n#    Testing at the platform's release (tools/deps.json) from Google's official bucket into ~/.cache/my3dge/ (once);\n#    tools/lib/browser.ts finds it there, so no shell state is needed. Offline, it warns and T2 cannot run.\n# 4. `npm ci`.\n#\n# Exit status: 0 when the dependencies are installed (an offline Node download or an unreachable source only warns);\n# 1 when `npm ci` fails.\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nrepo_root=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$repo_root\"\n\nsay() { printf 'setup: %s\\n' \"$*\"; }\n\n# Appends one line to $CLAUDE_ENV_FILE, unless the variable is unset or the line is already there.\nappend_env_line() {\n  local line=\"$1\"\n  [ -n \"${CLAUDE_ENV_FILE:-}\" ] || return 0\n  touch \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\"\n  grep -qxF -- \"$line\" \"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\" || printf '%s\\n' \"$line\" >>\"$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE\"\n}\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nnpm warn deprecated eslint@9.39.5: This version is no longer supported. Please see https://eslint.org/version-support for other options.\n\nadded 590 packages in 6s\n\nreal\t0m6.047s\nuser\t0m4.418s\nsys\t0m4.907s\n284\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   Start at  21:25:19\n   Duration  4.99s (transform 4.35s, setup 100ms, import 5.57s, tests 2.06s, environment 0ms)\n\nJSON report written to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game/out/test/report.json\n\nreal\t0m5.310s\nuser\t0m5.992s\nsys\t0m0.929s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SYJsBcoBVBHVZFNT4xyUuj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
