{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjA6CcCDBDdtc1fLLUCr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MgJS7kvJ5WmDQ6SpyX5Yx6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/ai-hub; sed -n 230,420p scripts/hub-check.mjs; echo -----; cat scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs | sed -n 1,60p","description":"Read hub-check solo checks and client identity check"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":197336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2013},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"6a6cdb3c-41e2-48d5-bbf2-f32cf4b319b4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:34:17.184Z","request_id":"req_011CgjA6CLpr9kLRq5Ust6aN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MgJS7kvJ5WmDQ6SpyX5Yx6":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/ai-hub; sed -n 230,420p scripts/hub-check.mjs; echo -----; cat scripts/lib/hub-client.mjs | sed -n 1,60p","description":"Read hub-check solo checks and client identity check"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgJS7kvJ5WmDQ6SpyX5Yx6","type":"tool_result","content":"      const report = await stillWorks(game, original && asPath(original));\n      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'alone', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) {\n        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n        for (const c of report.checks) if (!c.pass) console.log(`        ✗ ${c.name}${c.detail ? ` — ${c.detail}` : ''}`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n} finally {\n  await browser.close();\n  server?.close();\n}\n\n/** The pasted client, read from disk: one copy, exactly a released one. Null for a game served from elsewhere. */\nasync function clientCheck(game) {\n  if (/^https?:/.test(game)) return null;\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, decodeURI(game).replace(/^\\//, ''));\n  let text;\n  try {\n    text = await readFile(file, 'utf8');\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n  // A project folder may ship the client as its own file next to its page.\n  if (path.basename(file) === 'index.html' && !text.includes('aihub-session')) {\n    for (const name of await readdir(path.dirname(file)).catch(() => [])) {\n      if (/\\.m?js$/.test(name)) text += '\\n' + (await readFile(path.join(path.dirname(file), name), 'utf8').catch(() => ''));\n    }\n  }\n  const copies = findClients(text);\n  const name = 'the session client is pasted unmodified';\n  if (copies.length !== 1) return { name, pass: false, detail: `${copies.length} copies of the client` };\n  return { name, pass: copies[0].pristine, detail: copies[0].pristine ? copies[0].version : `${copies[0].version ?? 'unknown'} edited: paste lib/hub/session.js again` };\n}\n\n/**\n * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n * an original page already had), the client inactive and Math.random left\n * alone, and something drawn on the screen.\n */\nasync function stillWorks(game, before, { bare = false } = {}) {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n  const visit = async (page) => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    await context.addInitScript(watch);\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    const errors = [];\n    tab.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(e.message));\n    await tab.goto(/^https?:/.test(page) ? page : `${base}${page}`);\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2500);\n    for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\n      await tab.keyboard.press(key).catch(() => {});\n      await tab.waitForTimeout(500);\n    }\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2000);\n    const hub = await tab.evaluate(() => (window.AIHub ? { active: window.AIHub.active, seeded: window.AIHub.seeded } : null)).catch(() => null);\n    const gfx = await tab.evaluate(() => window.__gfx ?? null).catch(() => null);\n    // A WebGL or WebGPU canvas often reads back blank from a script, so look at the screen instead:\n    // a blank one compresses to almost nothing, so a PNG past a blank page's size means something is drawn.\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' }).catch(() => Buffer.alloc(0))).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return { errors, hub, bytes, gfx };\n  };\n  const blank = await (async () => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    await tab.setContent('<body style=\"margin:0;background:#000\"></body>');\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' })).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return bytes;\n  })();\n  const after = await visit(game);\n  // A line of text on a plain screen already adds about 2 KB; a uniform screen of any colour adds nothing.\n  after.drawn = after.bytes > blank + 1200;\n  const known = before ? new Set((await visit(before)).errors) : new Set();\n  const fresh = after.errors.filter((e) => !known.has(e));\n  if (!bare) {\n    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n    // A client before 1.3.0 has no seeded flag: it never seeds.\n    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n  }\n  const g = after.gfx;\n  const noWebGPU = g?.askedForWebGPU && !g.gotAdapter && !g.webgl && !g.twoD;\n  const asked = g ? `WebGPU ${g.askedForWebGPU ? (g.gotAdapter ? 'asked, adapter' : 'asked, no adapter') : 'not asked'}; WebGL ${g.webgl ? 'yes' : 'no'}; 2D ${g.twoD ? 'yes' : 'no'}` : 'not seen';\n  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n  // Drawing is all a bare page is asked: its own errors are the original's business.\n  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n  return { pass: checks.every((c) => c.pass), checks };\n}\n\n/**\n * Keep the verdict with the game: a failure takes it out of sessions until it\n * passes again (see the header). Games are found by path in data/games.json.\n */\nasync function recordChecks() {\n  let manifest;\n  try {\n    manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(ROOT, 'data/games.json'), 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    console.log('--record needs data/games.json: run pnpm scan first');\n    return;\n  }\n  const slugOf = new Map();\n  for (const g of manifest.games) for (const p of [g.path, ...(g.builds || []).map((b) => b.path)]) if (p) slugOf.set(decodeURI(p), g.slug);\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, 'data/overrides.json');\n  const overrides = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, 'utf8'));\n  const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n  for (const game of games) {\n    const slug = slugOf.get(decodeURI(game));\n    if (!slug) {\n      console.log(`--record: ${game} is not in the catalogue, nothing recorded`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    // A shared world that cannot yet be hosted by a server still plays: that run is reported, not held against it.\n    const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.game === game && r.scenario !== 'server');\n    const failed = [...new Set(mine.flatMap((r) => r.checks.filter((c) => !c.pass).map((c) => c.name)))];\n    const entry = { ...(overrides[slug] || {}) };\n    if (!failed.length) {\n      if (entry.session === '0') delete entry.session;\n      delete entry.sessionNote;\n    } else {\n      entry.session = '0';\n      entry.sessionNote = `hub-check failed on ${today}: ${failed.slice(0, 3).join('; ')}`.slice(0, 240);\n    }\n    if (Object.keys(entry).length) overrides[slug] = entry;\n    else delete overrides[slug];\n    console.log(`--record: ${slug} ${failed.length ? 'kept out of sessions' : 'may be dealt'}`);\n  }\n  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(overrides, null, 2)}\\n`);\n}\n\nconst pass = runs.every((r) => r.pass);\nif (record) await recordChecks();\nawait mkdir(path.join(ROOT, '.cache'), { recursive: true });\nawait writeFile(path.join(ROOT, '.cache', 'hub-check.json'), JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, base, pass, runs }, null, 2));\nif (asJson) console.log(JSON.stringify({ pass, runs }, null, 2));\nelse console.log(`\\n${pass ? 'All checks passed' : 'Some checks failed'} — report in .cache/hub-check.json`);\nprocess.exit(pass ? 0 : 1);\n-----\n/**\n * hub-client.mjs — the session client pasted into games, found, checked and\n * upgraded without a model.\n *\n * Every session game pastes lib/hub/session.js unmodified (lib/hub/README.md,\n * \"Parallel\"). A pasted copy runs from its banner, `/*! aihub-session\n * X.Y.Z`, to the client's last line. It is pristine when its text is, line\n * endings aside, exactly a released client: RELEASES holds each one's\n * SHA-256. Only a pristine copy is ever replaced, so a client someone edited\n * is reported and left alone, never overwritten.\n */\n\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n\n/** SHA-256 of each released client, banner to last line, with LF line endings. */\nexport const RELEASES = Object.freeze({\n  '1.0.0': '6fc9b691a78c237944ba0e972f506079e9906fbcc6b83e3d6acb8e832f88bb19',\n  '1.1.0': '6625a3a55ed0380baf268d593dd24e85f6c49fcd00d524fc308ae0fd4b484272',\n  '1.2.0': '2d6e9bd677210500e7683deaa88dace3f70b28295f85b0525a1811b2bc9bd088',\n  '1.3.0': '32ed0ff62e4e0880bc78db850a0cff8dd7c9277d34ef76cafc60d535d41761db',\n  '1.4.0': '529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a',\n});\n\nconst BANNER = '/*! aihub-session ';\nexport const CLIENT_END = \"})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\";\n\nconst sha256 = (text) => createHash('sha256').update(text).digest('hex');\nconst lf = (text) => text.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n');\n\n/** Compare dotted versions: negative when a is older than b. */\nexport function compareVersions(a, b) {\n  const pa = String(a).split('.').map(Number);\n  const pb = String(b).split('.').map(Number);\n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.max(pa.length, pb.length); i++) {\n    const d = (pa[i] || 0) - (pb[i] || 0);\n    if (d) return d;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\n/**\n * Every pasted client in a page or script: where it sits, the version its\n * banner names, and whether it is exactly that release.\n */\nexport function findClients(text) {\n  const out = [];\n  let from = 0;\n  for (;;) {\n    const start = text.indexOf(BANNER, from);\n    if (start === -1) break;\n    const close = text.indexOf(CLIENT_END, start);\n    const version = text.slice(start + BANNER.length).match(/^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+/)?.[0] ?? null;\n    if (close === -1) {\n      out.push({ start, end: text.length, version, pristine: false, complete: false });\n      break;\n    }\n    const end = close + CLIENT_END.length;\n    const hash = sha256(lf(text.slice(start, end)));\n    out.push({ start, end, version, pristine: !!version && RELEASES[version] === hash, complete: true, hash });\n    from = end;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"cbfade2d-1fb9-4c68-b4ad-028c9fc4509a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:34:17.217Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      const report = await stillWorks(game, original && asPath(original));\n      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'alone', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n      if (!asJson) {\n        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n        for (const c of report.checks) if (!c.pass) console.log(`        ✗ ${c.name}${c.detail ? ` — ${c.detail}` : ''}`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n} finally {\n  await browser.close();\n  server?.close();\n}\n\n/** The pasted client, read from disk: one copy, exactly a released one. Null for a game served from elsewhere. */\nasync function clientCheck(game) {\n  if (/^https?:/.test(game)) return null;\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, decodeURI(game).replace(/^\\//, ''));\n  let text;\n  try {\n    text = await readFile(file, 'utf8');\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n  // A project folder may ship the client as its own file next to its page.\n  if (path.basename(file) === 'index.html' && !text.includes('aihub-session')) {\n    for (const name of await readdir(path.dirname(file)).catch(() => [])) {\n      if (/\\.m?js$/.test(name)) text += '\\n' + (await readFile(path.join(path.dirname(file), name), 'utf8').catch(() => ''));\n    }\n  }\n  const copies = findClients(text);\n  const name = 'the session client is pasted unmodified';\n  if (copies.length !== 1) return { name, pass: false, detail: `${copies.length} copies of the client` };\n  return { name, pass: copies[0].pristine, detail: copies[0].pristine ? copies[0].version : `${copies[0].version ?? 'unknown'} edited: paste lib/hub/session.js again` };\n}\n\n/**\n * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n * an original page already had), the client inactive and Math.random left\n * alone, and something drawn on the screen.\n */\nasync function stillWorks(game, before, { bare = false } = {}) {\n  const checks = [];\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\n  const visit = async (page) => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    await context.addInitScript(watch);\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    const errors = [];\n    tab.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(e.message));\n    await tab.goto(/^https?:/.test(page) ? page : `${base}${page}`);\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2500);\n    for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\n      await tab.keyboard.press(key).catch(() => {});\n      await tab.waitForTimeout(500);\n    }\n    await tab.waitForTimeout(2000);\n    const hub = await tab.evaluate(() => (window.AIHub ? { active: window.AIHub.active, seeded: window.AIHub.seeded } : null)).catch(() => null);\n    const gfx = await tab.evaluate(() => window.__gfx ?? null).catch(() => null);\n    // A WebGL or WebGPU canvas often reads back blank from a script, so look at the screen instead:\n    // a blank one compresses to almost nothing, so a PNG past a blank page's size means something is drawn.\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' }).catch(() => Buffer.alloc(0))).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return { errors, hub, bytes, gfx };\n  };\n  const blank = await (async () => {\n    const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 800 } });\n    const tab = await context.newPage();\n    await tab.setContent('<body style=\"margin:0;background:#000\"></body>');\n    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' })).length;\n    await context.close();\n    return bytes;\n  })();\n  const after = await visit(game);\n  // A line of text on a plain screen already adds about 2 KB; a uniform screen of any colour adds nothing.\n  after.drawn = after.bytes > blank + 1200;\n  const known = before ? new Set((await visit(before)).errors) : new Set();\n  const fresh = after.errors.filter((e) => !known.has(e));\n  if (!bare) {\n    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n    // A client before 1.3.0 has no seeded flag: it never seeds.\n    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n  }\n  const g = after.gfx;\n  const noWebGPU = g?.askedForWebGPU && !g.gotAdapter && !g.webgl && !g.twoD;\n  const asked = g ? `WebGPU ${g.askedForWebGPU ? (g.gotAdapter ? 'asked, adapter' : 'asked, no adapter') : 'not asked'}; WebGL ${g.webgl ? 'yes' : 'no'}; 2D ${g.twoD ? 'yes' : 'no'}` : 'not seen';\n  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n  // Drawing is all a bare page is asked: its own errors are the original's business.\n  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n  return { pass: checks.every((c) => c.pass), checks };\n}\n\n/**\n * Keep the verdict with the game: a failure takes it out of sessions until it\n * passes again (see the header). Games are found by path in data/games.json.\n */\nasync function recordChecks() {\n  let manifest;\n  try {\n    manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(ROOT, 'data/games.json'), 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    console.log('--record needs data/games.json: run pnpm scan first');\n    return;\n  }\n  const slugOf = new Map();\n  for (const g of manifest.games) for (const p of [g.path, ...(g.builds || []).map((b) => b.path)]) if (p) slugOf.set(decodeURI(p), g.slug);\n  const file = path.join(ROOT, 'data/overrides.json');\n  const overrides = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, 'utf8'));\n  const today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n  for (const game of games) {\n    const slug = slugOf.get(decodeURI(game));\n    if (!slug) {\n      console.log(`--record: ${game} is not in the catalogue, nothing recorded`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    // A shared world that cannot yet be hosted by a server still plays: that run is reported, not held against it.\n    const mine = runs.filter((r) => r.game === game && r.scenario !== 'server');\n    const failed = [...new Set(mine.flatMap((r) => r.checks.filter((c) => !c.pass).map((c) => c.name)))];\n    const entry = { ...(overrides[slug] || {}) };\n    if (!failed.length) {\n      if (entry.session === '0') delete entry.session;\n      delete entry.sessionNote;\n    } else {\n      entry.session = '0';\n      entry.sessionNote = `hub-check failed on ${today}: ${failed.slice(0, 3).join('; ')}`.slice(0, 240);\n    }\n    if (Object.keys(entry).length) overrides[slug] = entry;\n    else delete overrides[slug];\n    console.log(`--record: ${slug} ${failed.length ? 'kept out of sessions' : 'may be dealt'}`);\n  }\n  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(overrides, null, 2)}\\n`);\n}\n\nconst pass = runs.every((r) => r.pass);\nif (record) await recordChecks();\nawait mkdir(path.join(ROOT, '.cache'), { recursive: true });\nawait writeFile(path.join(ROOT, '.cache', 'hub-check.json'), JSON.stringify({ schemaVersion: 1, base, pass, runs }, null, 2));\nif (asJson) console.log(JSON.stringify({ pass, runs }, null, 2));\nelse console.log(`\\n${pass ? 'All checks passed' : 'Some checks failed'} — report in .cache/hub-check.json`);\nprocess.exit(pass ? 0 : 1);\n-----\n/**\n * hub-client.mjs — the session client pasted into games, found, checked and\n * upgraded without a model.\n *\n * Every session game pastes lib/hub/session.js unmodified (lib/hub/README.md,\n * \"Parallel\"). A pasted copy runs from its banner, `/*! aihub-session\n * X.Y.Z`, to the client's last line. It is pristine when its text is, line\n * endings aside, exactly a released client: RELEASES holds each one's\n * SHA-256. Only a pristine copy is ever replaced, so a client someone edited\n * is reported and left alone, never overwritten.\n */\n\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n\n/** SHA-256 of each released client, banner to last line, with LF line endings. */\nexport const RELEASES = Object.freeze({\n  '1.0.0': '6fc9b691a78c237944ba0e972f506079e9906fbcc6b83e3d6acb8e832f88bb19',\n  '1.1.0': '6625a3a55ed0380baf268d593dd24e85f6c49fcd00d524fc308ae0fd4b484272',\n  '1.2.0': '2d6e9bd677210500e7683deaa88dace3f70b28295f85b0525a1811b2bc9bd088',\n  '1.3.0': '32ed0ff62e4e0880bc78db850a0cff8dd7c9277d34ef76cafc60d535d41761db',\n  '1.4.0': '529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a',\n});\n\nconst BANNER = '/*! aihub-session ';\nexport const CLIENT_END = \"})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\";\n\nconst sha256 = (text) => createHash('sha256').update(text).digest('hex');\nconst lf = (text) => text.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n');\n\n/** Compare dotted versions: negative when a is older than b. */\nexport function compareVersions(a, b) {\n  const pa = String(a).split('.').map(Number);\n  const pb = String(b).split('.').map(Number);\n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.max(pa.length, pb.length); i++) {\n    const d = (pa[i] || 0) - (pb[i] || 0);\n    if (d) return d;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\n/**\n * Every pasted client in a page or script: where it sits, the version its\n * banner names, and whether it is exactly that release.\n */\nexport function findClients(text) {\n  const out = [];\n  let from = 0;\n  for (;;) {\n    const start = text.indexOf(BANNER, from);\n    if (start === -1) break;\n    const close = text.indexOf(CLIENT_END, start);\n    const version = text.slice(start + BANNER.length).match(/^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+/)?.[0] ?? null;\n    if (close === -1) {\n      out.push({ start, end: text.length, version, pristine: false, complete: false });\n      break;\n    }\n    const end = close + CLIENT_END.length;\n    const hash = sha256(lf(text.slice(start, end)));\n    out.push({ start, end, version, pristine: !!version && RELEASES[version] === hash, complete: true, hash });\n    from = end;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MgJS7kvJ5WmDQ6SpyX5Yx6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjA6CcCDBDdtc1fLLUCr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xen9NTTUzjYbMKbaq62bqQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/ai-hub; sed -n 480,500p README.md; sed -n 725,770p README.md; grep -n -E \"exit-interview|hub:type|hub:players|hub:name|hub:description|hub:tagline|hub:genre|hub:tags|hub:controls\" -r scripts/scan.mjs scripts/ingest.mjs scripts/import-matrix-runs.mjs README.md lib/hub/retrofit.md | head -30; sed -n 60,110p scripts/scan.mjs | head -5; grep -n \"meta\" scripts/scan.mjs | head -30","description":"Read how the hub catalogues games and what metadata it reads"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2013,"cache_read_input_tokens":197336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2013},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"80d161f7-8bbf-4181-86e3-8342df66e22f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:34:19.760Z","request_id":"req_011CgjA6CLpr9kLRq5Ust6aN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Xen9NTTUzjYbMKbaq62bqQ":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/ai-hub; sed -n 480,500p README.md; sed -n 725,770p README.md; grep -n -E \"exit-interview|hub:type|hub:players|hub:name|hub:description|hub:tagline|hub:genre|hub:tags|hub:controls\" -r scripts/scan.mjs scripts/ingest.mjs scripts/import-matrix-runs.mjs README.md lib/hub/retrofit.md | head -30; sed -n 60,110p scripts/scan.mjs | head -5; grep -n \"meta\" scripts/scan.mjs | head -30","description":"Read how the hub catalogues games and what metadata it reads"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xen9NTTUzjYbMKbaq62bqQ","type":"tool_result","content":"  and it is how the existing library joins sessions.\n- **Ghost**: parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters while they are in the same area of the game, without them\n  touching its world.\n- **Shared world**: one world for everyone, run by the host's copy.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` plays as ghost, `co-op`\nand `versus` as a shared world.\n\nIn short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\npasted in unmodified as the first script, a round reported with its stats and\nawards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\nthe hub does around a round (points, awards, formats, the deal, the\nscoreboard, what travels where) is in\n[`docs/session-hub.md`](docs/session-hub.md). The plan behind all of it, and\nwhy, is [`docs/multiplayer-plan.md`](docs/multiplayer-plan.md).\n\nA game that declares it shows a *Hub session* line in its details\n(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\nwith `has:session`. Those fields never become rails. A parallel game is\nnot a multiplayer game on the wall: each player plays alone.\n    \"tags\": [\"pixel-art\", \"dungeon\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere is the part worth knowing: **the filter rails are not declared anywhere.**\nThey are read off whatever the games actually carry. Fill in `model` on a few\ngames and a Model rail appears on the wall by itself; remove them and it goes.\nAny field works, including ones invented on the spot. A game can also carry its\nown, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\nvalues are nearly all different (a build id, a URL) is searchable but never\nbecomes a rail. Every field is searchable. `harness` is searched and shown in\nthe drawer but never gets a rail, and neither do `source` and `series`, which\nhave Original, Inspired and the stacks.\n\n`collection` comes from the folder a game sits in, but it is an ordinary field:\nan override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n\nThe library's own catalogue uses these fields, all in `data/overrides.json`:\n\n| Field | What it is | On the wall |\n|---|---|---|\n| `genre` | one of a fixed list (Racing, Platformer, Life Sim, Tech Demo…) | the Genre rail, and the cabinet's panel |\n| `type` | `Game`, `Tech demo` or `Tool` | the shelf: games, or tech demos & tools |\n| `tags` | 2–5 from a fixed vocabulary (`3d`, `retro`, `co-op`, `touch`…) | the Tags rail |\n| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n| `source` | the classic a game riffs on, as it is titled (`Dragon Quest IX`); none for an original | Original or Inspired, the stacks, the drawer, and search |\n| `series` | the franchise, only when it is not the source itself (`Dragon Quest` for `Dragon Quest IX`) | the stacks |\n| `controls` | a one-line summary | the drawer |\n| `description` | one or two plain sentences | the drawer |\n\nEvery game with the same `source` must have the same `series`; `pnpm test`\nchecks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\nGenre, Collection, Type and Players follow it when they exist; the\nrest follow by how many games carry them. `docs/curation-2026-09-24.md`\nrecords how the library was curated: which file of each game was kept, and\nwhich older iterations it replaced. `docs/curation-2026-09-28.md` records the\nimport from the source-named GPT-games folder and maps the old slugs to the\ncurrent ones; `docs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md` records the smaller\nimport that followed it.\n\nSetting `\"hidden\": true` drops a game from the catalogue entirely.\n`\"restricted\": true` keeps it in the catalogue but off the wall, where only dev\nsettings can bring it back — used for the companionship-business sims.\n\n    return fallback;\n  }\n}\n\nconst skipName = (name) => name.startsWith('.') || name.startsWith('_');\n24:export const ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\n368:      // hub:* meta from the game's own head, then data/overrides.json on top.\n474:if (import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}` || process.argv[1]?.endsWith('scan.mjs')) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"25468e26-6189-42fd-b5a7-07e92da32501","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:34:19.854Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  and it is how the existing library joins sessions.\n- **Ghost**: parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters while they are in the same area of the game, without them\n  touching its world.\n- **Shared world**: one world for everyone, run by the host's copy.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` plays as ghost, `co-op`\nand `versus` as a shared world.\n\nIn short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\npasted in unmodified as the first script, a round reported with its stats and\nawards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\nthe hub does around a round (points, awards, formats, the deal, the\nscoreboard, what travels where) is in\n[`docs/session-hub.md`](docs/session-hub.md). The plan behind all of it, and\nwhy, is [`docs/multiplayer-plan.md`](docs/multiplayer-plan.md).\n\nA game that declares it shows a *Hub session* line in its details\n(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\nwith `has:session`. Those fields never become rails. A parallel game is\nnot a multiplayer game on the wall: each player plays alone.\n    \"tags\": [\"pixel-art\", \"dungeon\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere is the part worth knowing: **the filter rails are not declared anywhere.**\nThey are read off whatever the games actually carry. Fill in `model` on a few\ngames and a Model rail appears on the wall by itself; remove them and it goes.\nAny field works, including ones invented on the spot. A game can also carry its\nown, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\nvalues are nearly all different (a build id, a URL) is searchable but never\nbecomes a rail. Every field is searchable. `harness` is searched and shown in\nthe drawer but never gets a rail, and neither do `source` and `series`, which\nhave Original, Inspired and the stacks.\n\n`collection` comes from the folder a game sits in, but it is an ordinary field:\nan override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n\nThe library's own catalogue uses these fields, all in `data/overrides.json`:\n\n| Field | What it is | On the wall |\n|---|---|---|\n| `genre` | one of a fixed list (Racing, Platformer, Life Sim, Tech Demo…) | the Genre rail, and the cabinet's panel |\n| `type` | `Game`, `Tech demo` or `Tool` | the shelf: games, or tech demos & tools |\n| `tags` | 2–5 from a fixed vocabulary (`3d`, `retro`, `co-op`, `touch`…) | the Tags rail |\n| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n| `source` | the classic a game riffs on, as it is titled (`Dragon Quest IX`); none for an original | Original or Inspired, the stacks, the drawer, and search |\n| `series` | the franchise, only when it is not the source itself (`Dragon Quest` for `Dragon Quest IX`) | the stacks |\n| `controls` | a one-line summary | the drawer |\n| `description` | one or two plain sentences | the drawer |\n\nEvery game with the same `source` must have the same `series`; `pnpm test`\nchecks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.\nGenre, Collection, Type and Players follow it when they exist; the\nrest follow by how many games carry them. `docs/curation-2026-09-24.md`\nrecords how the library was curated: which file of each game was kept, and\nwhich older iterations it replaced. `docs/curation-2026-09-28.md` records the\nimport from the source-named GPT-games folder and maps the old slugs to the\ncurrent ones; `docs/curation-2026-09-28-new-ai-stuff.md` records the smaller\nimport that followed it.\n\nSetting `\"hidden\": true` drops a game from the catalogue entirely.\n`\"restricted\": true` keeps it in the catalogue but off the wall, where only dev\nsettings can bring it back — used for the companionship-business sims.\n\n    return fallback;\n  }\n}\n\nconst skipName = (name) => name.startsWith('.') || name.startsWith('_');\n24:export const ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\n368:      // hub:* meta from the game's own head, then data/overrides.json on top.\n474:if (import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}` || process.argv[1]?.endsWith('scan.mjs')) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xen9NTTUzjYbMKbaq62bqQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
