{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjALQQVd1fZBtdwyUF3h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PaJpiXESCdkSbXDEtYVQ4p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; ls -a .claude .claude/*; sed -n 1,140p ../my-3dge/.claude/skills/animation-authoring/SKILL.md","description":"Read the animation authoring guide"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":221522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2018},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"e7e7a69e-a8c7-4ddf-9f9e-4bbe88376998","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:37:29.138Z","request_id":"req_011CgjALQ9s6CVjqQTXWtP7g","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PaJpiXESCdkSbXDEtYVQ4p":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; ls -a .claude .claude/*; sed -n 1,140p ../my-3dge/.claude/skills/animation-authoring/SKILL.md","description":"Read the animation authoring guide"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PaJpiXESCdkSbXDEtYVQ4p","type":"tool_result","content":".claude/settings.json\n\n.claude:\n.\n..\nhooks\nsettings.json\n\n.claude/hooks:\n.\n..\npost-tool-use.ts\n---\nname: animation-authoring\ndescription: Authoring animation in my-3dge — poses as effector targets in metres (B(forward, right, up)) solved by IK onto the humanoid's rotation skeleton, builds and bodies, moves (strikes as data), actions (multi-beat sequences), library clips (find, show, play), procedural rigs, reactions and secondary motion — and checking it by numbers (animCheck, animCheckBody, actionCheck, rigCheck, node x qa anim, node x sheet, the gallery, the Animation Lab). Use when you add or change a build, body, move, action, clip, pose, rig or reaction, touch engine/anim, or an anim QA metric fails.\n---\n\n# Animation authoring\n\nADR-0009 is the rule: poses are authored in effector space, solved by IK and applied to a rotation skeleton (a root\nplus 23 joints, engine/anim/skeleton.ts); `anim.step` runs in the sim for every character and is hashed, `anim.pose`\nruns in the view for what is drawn and is not; the camera never feeds animation. ADR-0010 is the clip library's.\nGame code takes every name from engine/sim-api.ts (engine/anim/api.ts lists them by area).\n\n## The frame and the units\n\n- The model frame: +Y up, the character faces +Z, its left is +X. Effector tables write `B(f, r, u)`: metres forward,\n  right and up (engine/anim/authoring.ts), rig-local before the build's `size`, the floor at y = 0; `turnRight(a)`\n  turns toward the right hand. Angles in radians, times in seconds, the sim's fixed step; nothing random but the\n  named streams.\n- The humanoid (engine/anim/humanoid.ts) solves the spine, the arms and the legs from those targets; the animator\n  (engine/anim/character.ts) stacks the layers (base, override, solve, clips, additive, post, physics, secondary)\n  and is told its body states each step (`states.body`; an unknown word warns with the closest).\n\n## What to write, and the template for it\n\nEach is an `x new` kind (the `add-entry` skill): its test is the first check, and `node x describe <kind>` lists the\nfields with their defaults.\n\n| You want | Write | Checked by its test with |\n|---|---|---|\n| Proportions (a taller, heavier, smaller body) | `node x new build labs/<lab>/builds/<name>` (`defineBuild`) | `animCheck`: its rest pose on the floor |\n| How a body looks on the skeleton | `node x new body labs/<lab>/bodies/<name>` (`defineBody`) | compiled for every build, at most 10 draw calls |\n| A strike (arc, height, reach, phases, hit window) | `node x new move labs/<lab>/moves/<name>` (`defineMove`) | an `Attack` from wind to end, `measureMove`'s reach |\n| A sequence (beats of states, effectors, clips, events, cancel windows) | `node x new action labs/<lab>/actions/<name>` (`defineAction`) | `actionCheck` through `animCheckBody` on a humanoid |\n| A creature that is not a humanoid | `node x new rig labs/<lab>/rigs/<name>` (engine/anim/proc's blocks) | `rigCheck`, and a walk on its gait |\n\nEngine content lives in data, not labs: the engine's actions are data/anim/actions/ (one JSON file each, loaded by\n`loadActions`), its moves engine/anim/moves-data.ts, its builds engine/anim/builds.ts (`build:adult`, `build:heroic`,\n`build:bulky`, `build:chibi`, `build:skeleton`), its poses and stances engine/anim/poses.ts, its sample states\nengine/anim/states.ts. A game's stay in its lab (PLAN.md §5.7).\n\n## Playing it on an actor\n\n- `spawnActor(w, { at, character, anim: { build: 'build:adult' } })` animates an actor; its body states come from its\n  movement (the locomotion, engine/anim/locomotion/) and from what the scene tells it.\n- An action: `actOn(w, id, (a) => a.play('bow'))` (engine/sim/actorActions.ts); `a.next()`, `a.finish()`,\n  `a.cancel(...)`; its events go out as `action` `{ id, type, phase, late }`.\n- A clip: give the actor `clips: { sets: ['clipset:<set>'] }`, then `playClip(w, id, '<SET>/<Clip>')`\n  (engine/sim/actorClips.ts); `locomoteClips` plays an idle, a walk or a run by its ground speed. The sets are\n  data/anim/sets/<set>/, one file a clip, registered as `clipset:<set>` (`defineClipSet`; a page loads them, as\n  labs/box/library.ts does).\n- Reactions and secondary motion: `reactTo(w, id, act)` runs a flinch, a knockdown, a death or the get-up on the\n  component `reactions`; `secondary` holds hair, tails and a cape; both given at spawn (engine/sim/reactions.ts).\n\n## The clip library, from the command line\n\n`node x anim find <words> [--cat tag]` searches every set's catalog and the CMU ledger;\n`node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip as text and what the validator warns of;\n`node x anim sheet <set>/<clip>` draws its contact sheet; `node x anim bake <set>/<clip>` bakes it and checks FK\nparity. A clip is readable key poses\n(engine/anim/clip/readable.ts: hips, the body's turns, each limb a direction and a bend), so it fits any build and\nmirrors by swapping L and R. Importing and cutting sets are `x anim import`, `cut`, `cmu`: `node x help anim`.\n\n## Checking it\n\n- `node x qa anim [--only move:|action:|clip:|state:]` drives the engine's bodies through the state matrix (every\n  state, pose, stance, move, reaction and action at both facings, from rest and back) and every library clip, and\n  measures `pop`, `footSlide`, `loopClosure`, `jointLimit`, `twistJump`, `stretch`, `underFloor`, `reach`,\n  `unstableHash` and `rateDrift` against tests/baselines/qa-anim*.json (an accepted exception carries its reason).\n  It reads the engine's content; a lab's entry is checked by its own test.\n- `node x sheet <subject> [--build id] [--cams body|move|turntable]` (`move:slash`, `pose:kneel`, `state:`,\n  `humanoid`) draws the humanoid's states as a contact sheet beside their QA violations; `node x gallery body` and\n  `node x gallery move` film the bodies and moves the gallery's page registers; the Animation Lab (labs/anim/,\n  `npm run dev`) lines every build up under one clock, its timeline scrubbing a move (`lab.anim.time`).\n- docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.1's bounds hold on every feel course: a planted foot drifts at most 5 cm a contact, a hand\n  stays within 3 cm of its contact, no point pops, the muzzle within 2° of the aim.\n- Pictures only when a number points at one: the `visual-qa` skill, and the `visual-reviewer` subagent for the sheet.\n\n## Traps\n\n- Animation in the sim is hashed: a change to a move, a build or the humanoid moves goldens. Re-record a replay only\n  for a change meant to, with the reason in the commit (the `determinism-debugging` skill when they part).\n- Bones keep their lengths: a stretch means a rotation that is not a unit quaternion (`animCheck` names the joint).\n- A foot target is the sole, not the ankle: the ankle stands `ankleHeight` above it (ADR-0009 amendment 1).\n- An action's beat held `until: 'next'`, or a loop, needs `check.signals` for its check to end it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"0a989907-20d3-4ae0-8255-8b1a0787a9b7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:37:29.172Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".claude/settings.json\n\n.claude:\n.\n..\nhooks\nsettings.json\n\n.claude/hooks:\n.\n..\npost-tool-use.ts\n---\nname: animation-authoring\ndescription: Authoring animation in my-3dge — poses as effector targets in metres (B(forward, right, up)) solved by IK onto the humanoid's rotation skeleton, builds and bodies, moves (strikes as data), actions (multi-beat sequences), library clips (find, show, play), procedural rigs, reactions and secondary motion — and checking it by numbers (animCheck, animCheckBody, actionCheck, rigCheck, node x qa anim, node x sheet, the gallery, the Animation Lab). Use when you add or change a build, body, move, action, clip, pose, rig or reaction, touch engine/anim, or an anim QA metric fails.\n---\n\n# Animation authoring\n\nADR-0009 is the rule: poses are authored in effector space, solved by IK and applied to a rotation skeleton (a root\nplus 23 joints, engine/anim/skeleton.ts); `anim.step` runs in the sim for every character and is hashed, `anim.pose`\nruns in the view for what is drawn and is not; the camera never feeds animation. ADR-0010 is the clip library's.\nGame code takes every name from engine/sim-api.ts (engine/anim/api.ts lists them by area).\n\n## The frame and the units\n\n- The model frame: +Y up, the character faces +Z, its left is +X. Effector tables write `B(f, r, u)`: metres forward,\n  right and up (engine/anim/authoring.ts), rig-local before the build's `size`, the floor at y = 0; `turnRight(a)`\n  turns toward the right hand. Angles in radians, times in seconds, the sim's fixed step; nothing random but the\n  named streams.\n- The humanoid (engine/anim/humanoid.ts) solves the spine, the arms and the legs from those targets; the animator\n  (engine/anim/character.ts) stacks the layers (base, override, solve, clips, additive, post, physics, secondary)\n  and is told its body states each step (`states.body`; an unknown word warns with the closest).\n\n## What to write, and the template for it\n\nEach is an `x new` kind (the `add-entry` skill): its test is the first check, and `node x describe <kind>` lists the\nfields with their defaults.\n\n| You want | Write | Checked by its test with |\n|---|---|---|\n| Proportions (a taller, heavier, smaller body) | `node x new build labs/<lab>/builds/<name>` (`defineBuild`) | `animCheck`: its rest pose on the floor |\n| How a body looks on the skeleton | `node x new body labs/<lab>/bodies/<name>` (`defineBody`) | compiled for every build, at most 10 draw calls |\n| A strike (arc, height, reach, phases, hit window) | `node x new move labs/<lab>/moves/<name>` (`defineMove`) | an `Attack` from wind to end, `measureMove`'s reach |\n| A sequence (beats of states, effectors, clips, events, cancel windows) | `node x new action labs/<lab>/actions/<name>` (`defineAction`) | `actionCheck` through `animCheckBody` on a humanoid |\n| A creature that is not a humanoid | `node x new rig labs/<lab>/rigs/<name>` (engine/anim/proc's blocks) | `rigCheck`, and a walk on its gait |\n\nEngine content lives in data, not labs: the engine's actions are data/anim/actions/ (one JSON file each, loaded by\n`loadActions`), its moves engine/anim/moves-data.ts, its builds engine/anim/builds.ts (`build:adult`, `build:heroic`,\n`build:bulky`, `build:chibi`, `build:skeleton`), its poses and stances engine/anim/poses.ts, its sample states\nengine/anim/states.ts. A game's stay in its lab (PLAN.md §5.7).\n\n## Playing it on an actor\n\n- `spawnActor(w, { at, character, anim: { build: 'build:adult' } })` animates an actor; its body states come from its\n  movement (the locomotion, engine/anim/locomotion/) and from what the scene tells it.\n- An action: `actOn(w, id, (a) => a.play('bow'))` (engine/sim/actorActions.ts); `a.next()`, `a.finish()`,\n  `a.cancel(...)`; its events go out as `action` `{ id, type, phase, late }`.\n- A clip: give the actor `clips: { sets: ['clipset:<set>'] }`, then `playClip(w, id, '<SET>/<Clip>')`\n  (engine/sim/actorClips.ts); `locomoteClips` plays an idle, a walk or a run by its ground speed. The sets are\n  data/anim/sets/<set>/, one file a clip, registered as `clipset:<set>` (`defineClipSet`; a page loads them, as\n  labs/box/library.ts does).\n- Reactions and secondary motion: `reactTo(w, id, act)` runs a flinch, a knockdown, a death or the get-up on the\n  component `reactions`; `secondary` holds hair, tails and a cape; both given at spawn (engine/sim/reactions.ts).\n\n## The clip library, from the command line\n\n`node x anim find <words> [--cat tag]` searches every set's catalog and the CMU ledger;\n`node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip as text and what the validator warns of;\n`node x anim sheet <set>/<clip>` draws its contact sheet; `node x anim bake <set>/<clip>` bakes it and checks FK\nparity. A clip is readable key poses\n(engine/anim/clip/readable.ts: hips, the body's turns, each limb a direction and a bend), so it fits any build and\nmirrors by swapping L and R. Importing and cutting sets are `x anim import`, `cut`, `cmu`: `node x help anim`.\n\n## Checking it\n\n- `node x qa anim [--only move:|action:|clip:|state:]` drives the engine's bodies through the state matrix (every\n  state, pose, stance, move, reaction and action at both facings, from rest and back) and every library clip, and\n  measures `pop`, `footSlide`, `loopClosure`, `jointLimit`, `twistJump`, `stretch`, `underFloor`, `reach`,\n  `unstableHash` and `rateDrift` against tests/baselines/qa-anim*.json (an accepted exception carries its reason).\n  It reads the engine's content; a lab's entry is checked by its own test.\n- `node x sheet <subject> [--build id] [--cams body|move|turntable]` (`move:slash`, `pose:kneel`, `state:`,\n  `humanoid`) draws the humanoid's states as a contact sheet beside their QA violations; `node x gallery body` and\n  `node x gallery move` film the bodies and moves the gallery's page registers; the Animation Lab (labs/anim/,\n  `npm run dev`) lines every build up under one clock, its timeline scrubbing a move (`lab.anim.time`).\n- docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.1's bounds hold on every feel course: a planted foot drifts at most 5 cm a contact, a hand\n  stays within 3 cm of its contact, no point pops, the muzzle within 2° of the aim.\n- Pictures only when a number points at one: the `visual-qa` skill, and the `visual-reviewer` subagent for the sheet.\n\n## Traps\n\n- Animation in the sim is hashed: a change to a move, a build or the humanoid moves goldens. Re-record a replay only\n  for a change meant to, with the reason in the commit (the `determinism-debugging` skill when they part).\n- Bones keep their lengths: a stretch means a rotation that is not a unit quaternion (`animCheck` names the joint).\n- A foot target is the sole, not the ankle: the ankle stands `ankleHeight` above it (ADR-0009 amendment 1).\n- An action's beat held `until: 'next'`, or a loop, needs `check.signals` for its check to end it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PaJpiXESCdkSbXDEtYVQ4p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjALQQVd1fZBtdwyUF3h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019mVk5243PL4d4kgww3YSBm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; grep -n -E \"^\\s+[a-zA-Z_]+\\??[:(]\" engine/dev/inspector.ts | sed -n 1,90p; sed -n 1,60p engine/dev/inspector.ts | cut -c1-160; ls engine/dev; grep -n \"seed\" engine/app/headless.ts | head -30","description":"List inspector members and how seeds or restarts work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":221522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2018},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"c1aba1ba-163a-4b70-b838-f012e4a82da8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:37:31.039Z","request_id":"req_011CgjALQ9s6CVjqQTXWtP7g","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019mVk5243PL4d4kgww3YSBm":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; grep -n -E \"^\\s+[a-zA-Z_]+\\??[:(]\" engine/dev/inspector.ts | sed -n 1,90p; sed -n 1,60p engine/dev/inspector.ts | cut -c1-160; ls engine/dev; grep -n \"seed\" engine/app/headless.ts | head -30","description":"List inspector members and how seeds or restarts work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mVk5243PL4d4kgww3YSBm","type":"tool_result","content":"53:  DEV_NO_RENDERER: {\n54:    template: '__engine.{member} needs a renderer, and this engine has none ({runtime}, headless)',\n55:    fix: 'call it in a page started with createEngine (WP 2.7); headless, read state(), entities(), get(id) and hash() instead',\n57:  DEV_BAD_ARGS: {\n58:    template: '__engine.{member}: {problems}',\n59:    fix: 'call it as {signature}; __engine.help({name}) lists its arguments',\n60:    doc: 'Raised by every `__engine` member (engine/dev/inspector.ts) before it runs, when an argument does not match the schema its member declares: a wrong type, a value out of range, a missing required argument or one too many. Nothing has happened yet.',\n66:  version: string;\n67:  runtime: string;\n68:  headless: boolean;\n69:  adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\n70:  features: string[];\n71:  downgrades: string[];\n73:  deps: Record<string, string>;\n74:  scene: string;\n75:  seed: number;\n76:  tick: number;\n77:  hz: number;\n82:  id: number;\n83:  components: string[];\n88:  info(): EngineInfo;\n89:  pause(): void;\n90:  resume(): void;\n91:  step(n?: number, intents?: Intents | readonly Intents[]): number;\n92:  timeScale(k?: number): number;\n93:  seed(n?: number): number;\n94:  state(query?: string | readonly string[]): WorldState;\n95:  hash(): string;\n96:  trace(): WorldTrace;\n97:  entities(query?: string | readonly string[]): EntitySummary[];\n98:  get(id: number): EntityData | null;\n99:  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\n100:  capture(): WorldCapture;\n101:  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\n102:  describe(kind?: string, id?: string): unknown;\n103:  help(member?: string): string;\n130:    checkValue(field, args[i], name, problems);\n139:  memberKind(host.members);\n165:  type: 'any',\n166:  description: 'A component name, or a list of names an entity must all hold; every entity when absent.',\n177:  info: {\n178:    help: \"The engine's identity and health (version, runtime, adapter, features, downgrades, deps) and the run: scene, seed, tick, hz.\",\n179:    impl: (h): EngineInfo => ({\n180:      version: pkg.version,\n181:      runtime: h.runtime,\n182:      headless: !h.renderer,\n183:      adapter: h.adapter,\n184:      features: [...h.features],\n185:      downgrades: [...h.downgrades],\n186:      deps: { ...pkg.dependencies },\n187:      scene: h.session.scene.id,\n188:      seed: h.session.world.seed,\n189:      tick: h.session.world.tick,\n190:      hz: h.session.world.hz,\n193:  pause: {\n194:    help: 'Pauses sim time (the time.paused setting); step(n) still runs single steps.',\n195:    impl: (h) => h.clock.pause(),\n197:  resume: { help: 'Resumes sim time.', impl: (h) => h.clock.resume() },\n198:  step: {\n199:    help: 'Runs n sim steps through the clock, recorded in the session (without intents, what the virtual device holds: input.hold, input.axis…); returns the tick after them.',\n200:    args: {\n201:      n: { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'How many steps.' },\n202:      intents: {\n203:        type: 'any',\n204:        description:\n208:    impl: (h, n: number, intents: unknown) => {\n213:  timeScale: {\n214:    help: 'Sets sim seconds per real second (the time.scale setting) when k is given; returns it.',\n215:    args: { k: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, description: 'The new time scale: 0.5 is half speed.' } },\n216:    impl: (h, k: number | undefined) => {\n221:  seed: {\n222:    help: \"Starts the scene again with seed n (keeping the settings changed since it started) when n is given; returns the run's seed.\",\n223:    args: {\n224:      n: { type: 'integer', minimum: 0, description: 'The new seed: a whole number, 0 or more, as replays hold it.' },\n226:    impl: (h, n: number | undefined) => {\n231:  state: {\n232:    help: 'The sim as plain data, what the hash covers, with the entities the query matches.',\n233:    args: { query: QUERY },\n234:    impl: (h, query: unknown) => {\n240:  hash: { help: 'The state digest: 16 hex digits.', impl: (h) => h.session.world.hash() },\n241:  trace: {\n242:    help: 'Per-part and per-entity digests, to find where two runs part.',\n243:    impl: (h) => h.session.world.trace(),\n245:  entities: {\n246:    help: 'The live entities the query matches, in id order: each id and the components it holds.',\n247:    args: { query: QUERY },\n248:    impl: (h, query: unknown): EntitySummary[] =>\n250:        id: e.id,\n251:        components: Object.keys(e).filter((key) => key !== 'id'),\n254:  get: {\n/**\n * @file The inspector (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 1.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Verifiable): `window.__engine` in a page and\n * the object `createHeadless` returns in Node are one API, which `createInspector` assembles from the entries of the\n * registry kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts). Later WPs add members from their own files; this module\n * registers the core ones and never names another.\n *\n * A member is a call (`step(n, intents)`) or, with `value: true`, a property read without one (`errors`); a dotted\n * name (`scene.dump`) is a call on a namespace object. A call checks its arguments against the member's schema\n * (`DEV_BAD_ARGS` naming each problem and the signature, before anything happens), then runs `impl(host, ...args)`\n * with the arguments as given (absent ones as their default). A member that `needs: 'renderer'` throws\n * `DEV_NO_RENDERER` on a host without one, as `createHeadless` is. The core members map onto the kernel: `describe`\n * → the registry; `set` → the settings store through the session (text typed as `x set` types it, non-view changes\n * recorded); `errors` and `advice` → the log; `pause`, `resume`, `step` and `timeScale` → the clock (steps recorded\n * in the session); `capture` and `restore` → the session (a restore takes the recording back with the sim, and\n * refuses a capture this run did not take or one changed since: engine/sim/scene.ts); `state`, `hash`, `trace`,\n * `entities` and `get` → the world, read-only (a query names an undeclared component with the closest); `seed(n)`\n * starts the scene again. Every member that changes the sim goes through the session (engine/dev/members.ts).\n *\n * Invariants: the object holds its members and nothing else, so `help()` lists exactly what it has (`x docs --check`\n * compares them, tools/lib/docsHelp.ts), and the core table is typed against `Inspector`, so tsc refuses a core member\n * missing, extra or renamed. Members are read from `host.members` when the inspector is made: register before.\n * Results are plain data, copied (a capture is the session's own object, so it restores in place).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * import { defineMember, type InspectorHost } from './members';\n * const members = createRegistry();\n * const times = { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 1, description: 'How often.' } as const;\n * defineMember('ping', { help: 'Answers pong.', args: { times }, impl: (_h, n: number) => 'pong'.repeat(n) }, members);\n * const engine = createInspector({ members } as unknown as InspectorHost);\n * (engine.ping as (n?: number) => string)(2); // 'pongpong'; ping(0) throws DEV_BAD_ARGS\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\n */\nimport pkg from '../../package.json' with { type: 'json' };\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type AdviceRecord, type ErrorRecord } from '../core/log';\nimport { checkValue, copyValue, listProblems, show, type Problem } from '../core/schema';\nimport { createSettings, type SettingChange } from '../core/settings';\nimport type { Intents } from '../input/intents';\nimport type { WorldCapture } from '../sim/capture';\nimport type { EntityData, WorldState, WorldTrace } from '../sim/state';\nimport {\n  defineMember,\n  helpText,\n  memberKind,\n  signatureOf,\n  type InspectorHost,\n  type Member,\n  type MemberSpec,\n} from './members';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INSPECTOR_CODES = defineCodes('dev', {\n  DEV_NO_RENDERER: {\n    template: '__engine.{member} needs a renderer, and this engine has none ({runtime}, headless)',\n    fix: 'call it in a page started with createEngine (WP 2.7); headless, read state(), entities(), get(id) and hash() instead',\n  },\n  DEV_BAD_ARGS: {\n    template: '__engine.{member}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'call it as {signature}; __engine.help({name}) lists its arguments',\n    doc: 'Raised by every `__engine` member (engine/dev/inspector.ts) before it runs, when an argument does not match the schema its member declares: a wrong ty\nactions.ts\nbot.ts\nbotNav.ts\nbotSweep.ts\neye.ts\neyeFaces.ts\nfeel\ngallery.ts\ngalleryScene.ts\ngalleryShoot.ts\ngovernor.ts\ninspector.ts\nmembers.ts\noverlay.ts\nstats.ts\n3: * scene, seed, settings, view })` starts a scene as a recorded session (engine/sim/scene.ts) and returns its\n16: * goes with the next step, as in that playback. `seed(n)` starts the scene again with seed n, a new session and clock,\n18: * scene, seed and settings, keeping the view settings that differ, which never change play: a page's look stays) and\n28: * world (no interpolation from stale places), as a restart does. A seed is a whole number from 0 (`SIM_BAD_SEED`).\n34: * const h = await createHeadless({ scene: demo, seed: 3 });\n85:  /** The seed every sim RNG stream derives from (1). */\n86:  seed?: number;\n140:  /** Starts a replay's run (its scene, seed and settings), for playing it step by step; returns its session. */\n177:  const firstSeed = checkSeed(options.seed, 'createHeadless({ seed })');\n207:  const start = (scene: Scene, seed: number, settings: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | undefined) => {\n208:    const session = createSession(scene, { seed, settings, registry, log: options.log, probe: meter.probe });\n224:  const restart = (scene: Scene, seed: number, settings: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | undefined) => {\n228:    run = start(scene, seed, settings);\n235:    restart(getScene(replay.scene, registry), replay.seed, settings);\n343: * for a bad setting, `SIM_BAD_SEED` for a seed a replay cannot hold, and with a view `APP_NO_LEVEL` for a level not","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"d196ef2f-a5ef-43a0-9155-c254f43e94b1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:37:31.074Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"53:  DEV_NO_RENDERER: {\n54:    template: '__engine.{member} needs a renderer, and this engine has none ({runtime}, headless)',\n55:    fix: 'call it in a page started with createEngine (WP 2.7); headless, read state(), entities(), get(id) and hash() instead',\n57:  DEV_BAD_ARGS: {\n58:    template: '__engine.{member}: {problems}',\n59:    fix: 'call it as {signature}; __engine.help({name}) lists its arguments',\n60:    doc: 'Raised by every `__engine` member (engine/dev/inspector.ts) before it runs, when an argument does not match the schema its member declares: a wrong type, a value out of range, a missing required argument or one too many. Nothing has happened yet.',\n66:  version: string;\n67:  runtime: string;\n68:  headless: boolean;\n69:  adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\n70:  features: string[];\n71:  downgrades: string[];\n73:  deps: Record<string, string>;\n74:  scene: string;\n75:  seed: number;\n76:  tick: number;\n77:  hz: number;\n82:  id: number;\n83:  components: string[];\n88:  info(): EngineInfo;\n89:  pause(): void;\n90:  resume(): void;\n91:  step(n?: number, intents?: Intents | readonly Intents[]): number;\n92:  timeScale(k?: number): number;\n93:  seed(n?: number): number;\n94:  state(query?: string | readonly string[]): WorldState;\n95:  hash(): string;\n96:  trace(): WorldTrace;\n97:  entities(query?: string | readonly string[]): EntitySummary[];\n98:  get(id: number): EntityData | null;\n99:  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\n100:  capture(): WorldCapture;\n101:  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\n102:  describe(kind?: string, id?: string): unknown;\n103:  help(member?: string): string;\n130:    checkValue(field, args[i], name, problems);\n139:  memberKind(host.members);\n165:  type: 'any',\n166:  description: 'A component name, or a list of names an entity must all hold; every entity when absent.',\n177:  info: {\n178:    help: \"The engine's identity and health (version, runtime, adapter, features, downgrades, deps) and the run: scene, seed, tick, hz.\",\n179:    impl: (h): EngineInfo => ({\n180:      version: pkg.version,\n181:      runtime: h.runtime,\n182:      headless: !h.renderer,\n183:      adapter: h.adapter,\n184:      features: [...h.features],\n185:      downgrades: [...h.downgrades],\n186:      deps: { ...pkg.dependencies },\n187:      scene: h.session.scene.id,\n188:      seed: h.session.world.seed,\n189:      tick: h.session.world.tick,\n190:      hz: h.session.world.hz,\n193:  pause: {\n194:    help: 'Pauses sim time (the time.paused setting); step(n) still runs single steps.',\n195:    impl: (h) => h.clock.pause(),\n197:  resume: { help: 'Resumes sim time.', impl: (h) => h.clock.resume() },\n198:  step: {\n199:    help: 'Runs n sim steps through the clock, recorded in the session (without intents, what the virtual device holds: input.hold, input.axis…); returns the tick after them.',\n200:    args: {\n201:      n: { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'How many steps.' },\n202:      intents: {\n203:        type: 'any',\n204:        description:\n208:    impl: (h, n: number, intents: unknown) => {\n213:  timeScale: {\n214:    help: 'Sets sim seconds per real second (the time.scale setting) when k is given; returns it.',\n215:    args: { k: { type: 'number', minimum: 0, description: 'The new time scale: 0.5 is half speed.' } },\n216:    impl: (h, k: number | undefined) => {\n221:  seed: {\n222:    help: \"Starts the scene again with seed n (keeping the settings changed since it started) when n is given; returns the run's seed.\",\n223:    args: {\n224:      n: { type: 'integer', minimum: 0, description: 'The new seed: a whole number, 0 or more, as replays hold it.' },\n226:    impl: (h, n: number | undefined) => {\n231:  state: {\n232:    help: 'The sim as plain data, what the hash covers, with the entities the query matches.',\n233:    args: { query: QUERY },\n234:    impl: (h, query: unknown) => {\n240:  hash: { help: 'The state digest: 16 hex digits.', impl: (h) => h.session.world.hash() },\n241:  trace: {\n242:    help: 'Per-part and per-entity digests, to find where two runs part.',\n243:    impl: (h) => h.session.world.trace(),\n245:  entities: {\n246:    help: 'The live entities the query matches, in id order: each id and the components it holds.',\n247:    args: { query: QUERY },\n248:    impl: (h, query: unknown): EntitySummary[] =>\n250:        id: e.id,\n251:        components: Object.keys(e).filter((key) => key !== 'id'),\n254:  get: {\n/**\n * @file The inspector (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 1.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Verifiable): `window.__engine` in a page and\n * the object `createHeadless` returns in Node are one API, which `createInspector` assembles from the entries of the\n * registry kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts). Later WPs add members from their own files; this module\n * registers the core ones and never names another.\n *\n * A member is a call (`step(n, intents)`) or, with `value: true`, a property read without one (`errors`); a dotted\n * name (`scene.dump`) is a call on a namespace object. A call checks its arguments against the member's schema\n * (`DEV_BAD_ARGS` naming each problem and the signature, before anything happens), then runs `impl(host, ...args)`\n * with the arguments as given (absent ones as their default). A member that `needs: 'renderer'` throws\n * `DEV_NO_RENDERER` on a host without one, as `createHeadless` is. The core members map onto the kernel: `describe`\n * → the registry; `set` → the settings store through the session (text typed as `x set` types it, non-view changes\n * recorded); `errors` and `advice` → the log; `pause`, `resume`, `step` and `timeScale` → the clock (steps recorded\n * in the session); `capture` and `restore` → the session (a restore takes the recording back with the sim, and\n * refuses a capture this run did not take or one changed since: engine/sim/scene.ts); `state`, `hash`, `trace`,\n * `entities` and `get` → the world, read-only (a query names an undeclared component with the closest); `seed(n)`\n * starts the scene again. Every member that changes the sim goes through the session (engine/dev/members.ts).\n *\n * Invariants: the object holds its members and nothing else, so `help()` lists exactly what it has (`x docs --check`\n * compares them, tools/lib/docsHelp.ts), and the core table is typed against `Inspector`, so tsc refuses a core member\n * missing, extra or renamed. Members are read from `host.members` when the inspector is made: register before.\n * Results are plain data, copied (a capture is the session's own object, so it restores in place).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * import { defineMember, type InspectorHost } from './members';\n * const members = createRegistry();\n * const times = { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 1, description: 'How often.' } as const;\n * defineMember('ping', { help: 'Answers pong.', args: { times }, impl: (_h, n: number) => 'pong'.repeat(n) }, members);\n * const engine = createInspector({ members } as unknown as InspectorHost);\n * (engine.ping as (n?: number) => string)(2); // 'pongpong'; ping(0) throws DEV_BAD_ARGS\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\n */\nimport pkg from '../../package.json' with { type: 'json' };\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type AdviceRecord, type ErrorRecord } from '../core/log';\nimport { checkValue, copyValue, listProblems, show, type