{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XHv2mtJtA8yPLBAip4MP2n","type":"tool_result","content":"2: * @file The view of a run (PLAN.md §6.4's `view.update`, §8.3, WP 2.7): what a running scene looks like, built\n4: * stage of the scene (engine/gfx/stage.ts: lights, the level's meshes, actors as puppets, a stand-in per other placed\n8: * draws the crowd bodies as that camera sees them (engine/gfx/stageCrowd.ts: its level of detail and culling; after\n9: * steps with no frame, `dump` draws them first), then moves the stage's effects on by the frame (engine/gfx/stageFx.ts:\n11: * the page shakes its camera by them while it draws), returning what to draw (`{ scene, camera, alpha }`,\n17: * the stage's sky (engine/gfx/stageSky.ts, flickering at the frames' time, WP 7.8), and the level entry's looks (its\n18: * swaps, rooms' floors and recipes: `levelLooks`) reach the stage. The rig also gets the sim's read-only `QueryView` in\n19: * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n22: * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n29: * The level comes from the scene's `level` id (engine/world/level/level.ts), registered before the view starts\n33: * only: it reads the run, never writes it (its `QueryView` has no way in); one stage per view, a camera per projection.\n53:import { createStage, type Stage } from '../gfx/stage';\n69:    template: 'the scene {scene} loads the level {level}, which is not registered, so its view cannot be built',\n73:    template: '{member} needs the scene drawn as a view, and this engine has none',\n74:    fix: 'start it with createHeadless({ scene, view: true }) in Node; a page always has one',\n104:  /** Where the scene's level and the component kinds are declared. */\n124:  readonly stage: Stage;\n136:   * Moves the camera by one rendered frame and the stand-ins to `alpha`; returns what to draw. The stage's sky follows,\n137:   * lit by the hour of the scene's clock (engine/sim/lights.ts) and lighting the props' lamps that are on (WP 13.23).\n153:  /** The stage as text (engine/gfx/sceneDump.ts). */\n157:  /** Frees the stage. */\n161:/** The entities that a stage can place, each once, in id order. */\n171:  const scene = options.run().scene;\n173:  if (scene.level !== undefined && !known(scene.level)) {\n174:    throw codeError('APP_NO_LEVEL', { scene: scene.id, level: scene.level });\n176:  const level = scene.level === undefined ? null : getLevel(scene.level, registry);\n177:  const looks = scene.level === undefined ? {} : levelLooks(registry, scene.level);\n178:  const terrain = scene.terrain === undefined ? null : getTerrain(scene.terrain, registry);\n179:  const site = scene.site === undefined ? null : getSite(scene.site, registry);\n181:  const stage = createStage({ level, terrain, site, materials: options.materials, registry, log: options.log, fxRng, ...looks }); // prettier-ignore\nengine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts:213:export function createPuppet(compiled: CompiledBody, options: { materials: PuppetMaterials; name?: string }): Puppet {\nengine/gfx/instancing.ts:172:export function createInstancedBatch(options: InstancedBatchOptions): InstancedBatch {\n328:- `CROWD_BODY` (const from [`engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts`](../engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts)): The component `crowdBody`: an entity the stage draws through a crowd.\n431:- `Effectors` (interface from [`engine/anim/poses.ts`](../engine/anim/poses.ts)): The effector stage's targets: rig-local metres before `size`, in the model frame (+Z forward, +Y up).\n596:- `HumanoidWeights` (interface from [`engine/anim/locomotion.ts`](../engine/anim/locomotion.ts)): The weights the effector stage reads: each 0 (off) to 1 (full), eased toward its input by the humanoid.\n811:- `PHASES` (const from [`engine/sim/systems.ts`](../engine/sim/systems.ts)): The phases systems run in, in order; the engine's `timers` stage runs between `readback` and `rules`.\n1511:- `CROWD_BODY` (const from [`engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts`](../engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts)): The component `crowdBody`: an entity the stage draws through a crowd.\n1577:- `Effectors` (interface from [`engine/anim/poses.ts`](../engine/anim/poses.ts)): The effector stage's targets: rig-local metres before `size`, in the model frame (+Z forward, +Y up).\n1679:- `HumanoidWeights` (interface from [`engine/anim/locomotion.ts`](../engine/anim/locomotion.ts)): The weights the effector stage reads: each 0 (off) to 1 (full), eased toward its input by the humanoid.\n1816:- `PHASES` (const from [`engine/sim/systems.ts`](../engine/sim/systems.ts)): The phases systems run in, in order; the engine's `timers` stage runs between `readback` and `rules`.\n2318:- `Effectors` (interface from [`engine/anim/poses.ts`](../engine/anim/poses.ts)): The effector stage's targets: rig-local metres before `size`, in the model frame (+Z forward, +Y up).\n2357:- `HumanoidWeights` (interface from [`engine/anim/locomotion.ts`](../engine/anim/locomotion.ts)): The weights the effector stage reads: each 0 (off) to 1 (full), eased toward its input by the humanoid.\n2883:- `EffectorContext` (interface): What the effector stage reads: the build, the humanoid's state now and the anchors placed so far.\n2890:- `HumanoidWeights` (interface): The weights the effector stage reads: each 0 (off) to 1 (full), eased toward its input by the humanoid.\n3019:- `createEffectors` (function): A set of effectors for `effectorStage` to fill.\n3022:- `Effectors` (interface): The effector stage's targets: rig-local metres before `size`, in the model frame (+Z forward, +Y up).\n3023:- `effectorStage` (function): The effector stage: the gait's targets (locomotion.ts), then the layers over them in order, then a move's arm path (strike.ts `layArm`), into `out`, whose pelvis, chest, shoulders and hips must be `ctx`'s anchors.\n4173:- `fitCamera` (fu