{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U2qM1tTEp6V1S7fQkzPpe1","type":"tool_result","content":"x shot: ok: labs/game: 480×270, coverage 80.4%, luma 0.0784–0.5216, 16 of 37 objects visible\nvisible: level:arena/floor 19.1%, level:arena/wall@0,0-17,0:cut 16.6%, level:arena/wall@0,0-17,0 13.4%, level:arena/pillar@8,3-9,4 10.4%, … (12 more)\nunseen: level:arena/lowWall@12,6-12,7 (covered), level:arena/wall@17,1-17,13 (covered), level:arena/pillar@8,3-9,4:cut (hidden), … (18 more)\nfiles: out/shot/labs-game/frame.png, out/shot/labs-game/shot.json\nreport: out/shot/labs-game/report.json\nframe.png\nreport.json\nshot.json\n['set', 'title', 'format', 'credit', 'fps', 'sources', 'body', 'fit']\n{\"set\": \"MESH2MOTION\", \"title\": \"Mesh2Motion\", \"format\": 2, \"credit\": \"Mesh2Motion's human animations (mesh2motion.org, CC0 1.0): Quaternius' Universal Animation Library clips as Mesh2Motion re-exported them, clips its contributors animated, and its own motion captures. Each clip's src names which, and orig the Quaternius clip a re-export was made from.\", \"fps\": 30, \"sources\": {\"M2M_QUATERNIUS\": {\"file\": \"human-base-animations.glb\", \"rig\": \"unreal\", \"label\": \"Quaternius, via Mesh2Motion\", \"origin\": \"Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 as Mesh2Motion re-exported them on its human rig (human-base-animations.glb). Library 1's clips run 25% longer than in Quaternius' own files, and a few are trimmed or end back on their feet. Each clip's orig names the Quaternius clip it was made from\", \"license\": \"CC0 1.0\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app\", \"rest\": {\"H0\": \n{\"clip\": \"Pushup\", \"src\": \"M2M_ANIMATED\", \"dur\": 1.542, \"loop\": true, \"tags\": [\"emote\",\"exercise\"], \"desc\": \"push-ups: the body held straight, arms bending and pressing up\", \"fps\": 24, \"via\": \"source\", \"contact\n  {\"t\":0,\n   \"hips\":[-7,0,49], \"body\":[0,75,0], \"chest\":[0,-12,0], \"head\":[0,17,0], \"spine\":[0,1,0],\n   \"shL\":[0,0], \"shR\":[0,0], \"armL\":[88,26,-40,12,-55], \"armR\":[88,26,-40,12,55], \"handL\":[-71,45,-54], \"handR\":[-71,45,-54], \"gripL\":0, \"gripR\":0,\n   \"legL\":[-4,0,-100,8,-3], \"legR\":[-4,0,-100,8,3], \"footL\":[-3,0,48], \"footR\":[-3,0,48], \"rollL\":0, \"rollR\":0},\n  {\"t\":0.167,\n   \"hips\":[-7,0,47], \"body\":[0,78,0], \"chest\":[0,-11,0], \"head\":[0,14,0], \"spine\":[0,0,0],\n   \"shL\":[0,0], \"shR\":[0,0], \"armL\":[91,22,-36,44,-54], \"armR\":[91,22,-36,44,54], \"handL\":[-81,-15,6], \"handR\":[-81,-15,6], \"gripL\":1, \"gripR\":1,\n   \"legL\":[-1,0,-100,11,-3], \"legR\":[-1,0,-100,11,3], \"footL\":[-6,0,48], \"footR\":[-6,0,48], \"rollL\":0, \"rollR\":0},\n  {\"t\":0.4,\n   \"hips\":[-5,0,40], \"body\":[0,86,0], \"chest\":[0,-6,0], \"head\":[0,3,0], \"spine\":[0,-2,0],\n   \"shL\":[0,0], \"shR\":[0,0], \"armL\":[96,19,-22,92,-45], \"armR\":[96,19,-22,92,45], \"handL\":[-68,-79,73], \"handR\":[-68,-79,73], \"gripL\":1, \"gripR\":1,\n2: * @file How a clip reads (PLAN.md §10.2, WP 8.2): `LEGEND`, what every key field means, and each field's shape\n3- * (`KEY_ARRAYS`, `KEY_NUMBERS`, `ANGLE_ENTRIES`), which parsing, in-betweening and the validator read; `clipText`, the\n4- * text an agent reads and edits, ported from `my-3d2dge:src/mocap/readable.js`'s `text` with no change in its output;\n5- * and the normalized lens, every angle folded to (−180°, 180°] for reading, without changing the stored data.\n6- *\n7- * Importers unwrap angles so each key continues from the one before (a spin keeps counting past 360°), which keeps\n8- * the in-betweens right but makes a single key hard to read; the lens shows the same pose at every key.\n9- *\n10- * Invariants: `clipText` writes the header in the clip's own field order, then three lines per key (torso, arms,\n11- * legs), format 2's fields after format 1's, so a format-1 clip prints exactly as the source printed it. The lens\n12- * returns a copy; a folded angle differs from the stored one by whole turns, so each key decodes to the same body\n13- * points (to rounding), but the in-betweens differ: the lens is for reading, never for storing. Bends of 0° to 180°\n14- * read unchanged.\n15- *\n16- * @example\n17- * import { standing } from '../../../tests/unit/anim/clip-fixtures';\n18- * const clip = { dur: 0, keys: [{ ...standing(0), body: [450, 10, -370] }] };\n19- * normalizedLens(clip).keys[0].body; // [90, 10, -10]: the same pose, read at a glance\n20- * foldAngle(190); // -170\n21- * clipText(clip).split('\\n')[2]; // '   \"hips\":[0,0,100], \"body\":[450,10,-370], …': the stored numbers\n22- * @see engine/anim/clip/lens.test.ts\n23- */\n24-import type { Clip, ClipKey } from './readable';\n25-\n26-/** What each field means, one line each, as a set file or a reader shows it (shardfall's legend, format 2 added). */\n27:export const LEGEND: readonly string[] = [\n28-  'Readable key poses (the my-3D2dge format). Times in seconds; every other number is a whole number. Rig frame: forward, right, up.',\n29-  \"L and R are the figure's own sides. Directions are percentages and need not add up: [100, 0, 0] and [50, 0, 0] agree.\",\n30-  'hips   [forward, right, up]   the pelvis, in percent of standing hip height (100 = standing, 55 = sitting on a chair)',\n31-  'body   [turn, lean, tilt]     the pelvis, degrees: turn + = toward the right, lean + = forward, tilt + = toward the right',\n32-  'chest  [turn, lean, tilt]     the chest, relative to the pelvis; head [turn, lean, tilt] relative to the chest',\n33-  'shL shR    [reach, shrug]     degrees the shoulder swings forward (into a punch or an aim) and up, from rest',\n34-  'armL armR  [forward, out, up, bend, twist]  which way the arm points from the shoulder to the fist, in chest space (out + = away from the body on that side; [0, 0, \n35-  'legL legR  [forward, out, up, bend, twist]  hip to ankle in pelvis space; bend: the knee; twist: from pointing forward',\n36-  'footL footR [down, out, toes]   degrees the foot points down from standing, turns outward, and the toes bend up',\n37-  'blade  [forward, right, up]   (sword clips) the direction of a blade held in the right fist, in chest space',\n38-  'root   [forward, right]       (clips that travel) how far the whole body has moved, in percent of standing hip height',\n39-  \"speed  (a clip's header: loops that walk or run in place) how fast the capture travelled, percent of standing hip height a second\",\n40-  'format 2, each optional: handL handR [flex, side, roll] at the wrist; rollL rollR (foot roll); yaw (root); spine [turn, lean, tilt]; gripL gripR (0-100)',\n41-];\n42-\n43-/** Each array field of a key: its length and its shape, as an error names it. */\n44-export const KEY_ARRAYS: Record<string, [size: number, shape: string]> = {\n45-  hips: [3, '[forward, right, up] in % of standing hip height'],\n46-  ...Object.fromEntries(['body', 'chest', 'head', 'spine'].map((f) => [f, [3, '[turn, lean, tilt] in degrees']])),\n47-  ...Object.fromEntries(['shL', 'shR'].map((f) => [f, [2, '[reach, shrug] in degrees']])),\n48-  ...Object.fromEntries(['armL', 'armR', 'legL', 'legR'].map((f) => [f, [5, '[forward, out, up, bend, twist]']])),\n49-  ...Object.fromEntries(['footL', 'footR'].map((f) => [f, [3, '[down, out, toes] in degrees']])),\n50-  blade: [3, '[forward, right, up], the blade’s direction'],\n51-  root: [2, '[forward, right] in % of standing hip height'],","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"f9cf9324-8efd-44ba-b229-e310f96b08b6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:03.501Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"x shot: ok: labs/game: 480×270, coverage 80.4%, luma 0.0784–0.5216, 16 of 37 objects visible\nvisible: level:arena/floor 19.1%, level:arena/wall@0,0-17,0:cut 16.6%, level:arena/wall@0,0-17,0 13.4%, level:arena/pillar@8,3-9,4 10.4%, … (12 more)\nunseen: level:arena/lowWall@12,6-12,7 (covered), level:arena/wall@17,1-17,13 (covered), level:arena/pillar@8,3-9,4:cut (hidden), … (18 more)\nfiles: out/shot/labs-game/frame.png, out/shot/labs-game/shot.json\nreport: out/shot/labs-game/report.json\nframe.png\nreport.json\nshot.json\n['set', 'title', 'format', 'credit', 'fps', 'sources', 'body', 'fit']\n{\"set\": \"MESH2MOTION\", \"title\": \"Mesh2Motion\", \"format\": 2, \"credit\": \"Mesh2Motion's human animations (mesh2motion.org, CC0 1.0): Quaternius' Universal Animation Library clips as Mesh2Motion re-exported them, clips its contributors animated, and its own motion captures. Each clip's src names which, and orig the Quaternius clip a re-export was made from.\", \"fps\": 30, \"sources\": {\"M2M_QUATERNIUS\": {\"file\": \"human-base-animations.glb\", \"rig\": \"unreal\", \"label\": \"Quaternius, via Mesh2Motion\", \"origin\": \"Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 as Mesh2Motion re-exported them on its human rig (human-base-animations.glb). Library 1's clips run 25% longer than in Quaternius' own files, and a few are trimmed or end back on their feet. Each clip's orig names the Quaternius clip it was made from\", \"license\": \"CC0 1.0\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app\", \"rest\": {\"H0\": \n{\"clip\": \"Pushup\", \"src\": \"M2M_ANIMATED\", \"dur\": 1.542, \"loop\": true, \"tags\": [\"emote\",\"exercise\"], \"desc\": \"push-ups: the body held straight, arms bending and pressing up\", \"fps\": 24, \"via\": \"source\", \"contact\n  {\"t\":0,\n   \"hips\":[-7,0,49], \"body\":[0,75,0], \"chest\":[0,-12,0], \"head\":[0,17,0], \"spine\":[0,1,0],\n   \"shL\":[0,0], \"shR\":[0,0], \"armL\":[88,26,-40,12,-55], \"armR\":[88,26,-40,12,55], \"handL\":[-71,45,-54], \"handR\":[-71,45,-54], \"gripL\":0, \"gripR\":0,\n   \"legL\":[-4,0,-100,8,-3], \"legR\":[-4,0,-100,8,3], \"footL\":[-3,0,48], \"footR\":[-3,0,48], \"rollL\":0, \"rollR\":0},\n  {\"t\":0.167,\n   \"hips\":[-7,0,47], \"body\":[0,78,0], \"chest\":[0,-11,0], \"head\":[0,14,0], \"spine\":[0,0,0],\n   \