{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjAiE9ipikjfTMyosbHM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014RVX8A85AzWhiwY33khv7r","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; node x help shot 2>&1 | cut -c1-170 | head -40; git -C . status 2>/dev/null | head -3; grep -n \"scenes\\|play\" labs/game/main.ts | head -12; sed -n 140,212p labs/game/scenes/play.ts | cut -c1-130","description":"Read shot command manual and the starter scene definition"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6262,"cache_read_input_tokens":325940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6262},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"86a448f7-9697-4fa0-8796-2fd3d3423b1d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:21.354Z","request_id":"req_011CgjAiDtbG2QhJduVM7wbm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014RVX8A85AzWhiwY33khv7r":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/probe-game; node x help shot 2>&1 | cut -c1-170 | head -40; git -C . status 2>/dev/null | head -3; grep -n \"scenes\\|play\" labs/game/main.ts | head -12; sed -n 140,212p labs/game/scenes/play.ts | cut -c1-130","description":"Read shot command manual and the starter scene definition"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014RVX8A85AzWhiwY33khv7r","type":"tool_result","content":"x help: ok: node x shot <page> [--scene s] [--cam code] [--set k=v…] [--ids] [--metrics] [--marks] [--png] [--thumb case [--update]] [--ready-ms n]\nRenders a page on WebGPU in the platform's Chromium and reports what it drew as numbers and text: the look\nmetrics, the ID pass (which object covers which pixels) and a 48 × 27 text thumbnail; images only on demand.\n\n`node x shot <page>` serves the repository with Vite (tools/lib/vite.ts, on a free port), opens the page the way\nthe e2e fixture does (tools/lib/browser.ts: the WebGPU flags, the virtual clock, seed 1) with `--scene`, `--cam`\nand each `--set key=value` as URL parameters, waits for `window.__engine.ready`, and calls `__engine.shot(options)`\n(engine/gfx/shot.ts: the frame drawn into a render target and read back, the ID pass, the look metrics, the\nthumbnail). report.json gets the look metrics (coverage, luma P5 and P95 and their spread, the dark and blown-out\nshares, colours, palette, flat share, dithering, edge density, the largest object and its share, whether the\nprotagonist is visible), the ID-pass list (`px.<name>`, `share.<name>`, `bbox.<name>` as `x0,y0,x1,y1` from the\ntop left, `unseen.<name>`: `hidden`, `background`, `outside` or `covered`; a repeated name gets `#<id>`), and each\nlook note as a warning with its number and fix; `out/shot/<target>/shot.json` holds the whole result, thumbnail\nand object map included (out/ is never committed). A page without `__engine.shot` (labs/hello) is screenshotted\ninstead: look metrics and thumbnail, no ID pass. While `x inspect` runs, the shot is taken in its browser instead\nof a new one: on its open page when that shows the URL asked (so what `x set` changed shows), else in a new tab\n(§8.1).\n\n… 21 more in out/help/shot/output.txt\nreport: out/help/shot/report.json\nOn branch main\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.\n\n3: * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\n4: * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\n7: * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\n17: * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\n18: * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\n23:import { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n25:/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\n30:/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\n31:const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\n39:/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\n40:const store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\n46:/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\n    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n  });\n  return tiles;\n}\n\n/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\nfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n  const tiles = gemTiles();\n  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\nfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n  round.state = state;\n  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n    e.actor.player = false;\n    e.actor.intents = {};\n  }\n  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n}\n\n/**\n * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n */\nfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  const taken = new Set<number>();\n  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n      taken.add(gem.id);\n      w.despawn(gem.id);\n      round.collected += 1;\n      w.emit('gem', { id: gem.id, x: gem.gem.x, z: gem.gem.z, collected: round.collected });\n    }\n  }\n  if (round.collected >= round.gems) endRound(w, round, 'won');\n}\n\n/** Runs the clock down a step at a time (game time is whole steps, never summed seconds); at 0 the round is lost. */\nfunction clock(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  round.left = Math.max(0, round.left - 1);\n  if (round.left === 0) endRound(w, round, 'lost');\n}\n\n/** The starter game: collect every gem before the clock runs out. */\nexport const play = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:play', {\n  description: 'The starter game: run round the arena collecting the gems before the clock runs out.',\n  level: 'level:arena',\n  physics: true,\n  setup(w) {\n    addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), ARENA);\n    const gems = w.settings.get<number>('game.gems');\n    w.spawn({ round: { gems, left: Math.round(w.settings.get<number>('game.seconds') * w.hz) } });\n    scatterGems(w, gems);\n    spawnPlayer(w, [START[0], START[1], START[2]], w.settings.get<number>('game.speed'));\n    w.systems.add('game.collect', collect, { phase: 'rules' });\n    w.systems.add('game.clock', clock, { phase: 'rules' });\n  },\n});\n\nexport default play;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"49dfa9e9-44f6-4588-b864-86db113ec50f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:42:22.653Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"x help: ok: node x shot <page> [--scene s] [--cam code] [--set k=v…] [--ids] [--metrics] [--marks] [--png] [--thumb case [--update]] [--ready-ms n]\nRenders a page on WebGPU in the platform's Chromium and reports what it drew as numbers and text: the look\nmetrics, the ID pass (which object covers which pixels) and a 48 × 27 text thumbnail; images only on demand.\n\n`node x shot <page>` serves the repository with Vite (tools/lib/vite.ts, on a free port), opens the page the way\nthe e2e fixture does (tools/lib/browser.ts: the WebGPU flags, the virtual clock, seed 1) with `--scene`, `--cam`\nand each `--set key=value` as URL parameters, waits for `window.__engine.ready`, and calls `__engine.shot(options)`\n(engine/gfx/shot.ts: the frame drawn into a render target and read back, the ID pass, the look metrics, the\nthumbnail). report.json gets the look metrics (coverage, luma P5 and P95 and their spread, the dark and blown-out\nshares, colours, palette, flat share, dithering, edge density, the largest object and its share, whether the\nprotagonist is visible), the ID-pass list (`px.<name>`, `share.<name>`, `bbox.<name>` as `x0,y0,x1,y1` from the\ntop left, `unseen.<name>`: `hidden`, `background`, `outside` or `covered`; a repeated name gets `#<id>`), and each\nlook note as a warning with its number and fix; `out/shot/<target>/shot.json` holds the whole result, thumbnail\nand object map included (out/ is never committed). A page without `__engine.shot` (labs/hello) is screenshotted\ninstead: look metrics and thumbnail, no ID pass. While `x inspect` runs, the shot is taken in its browser instead\nof a new one: on its open page when that shows the URL asked (so what `x set` changed shows), else in a new tab\n(§8.1).\n\n… 21 more in out/help/shot/output.txt\nreport: out/help/shot/report.json\nOn branch main\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.\n\n3: * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\n4: * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\n7: * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\n17: * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\n18: * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\n23:import { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n25:/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\n30:/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\n31:const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\n39:/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\n40:const store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\n46:/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\n    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n  });\n  return tiles;\n}\n\n/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\nfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n  const tiles = gemTiles();\n  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\nfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n  round.state = state;\n  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n    e.actor.player = false;\n    e.actor.intents = {};\n  }\n  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n}\n\n/**\n * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n */\nfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  const taken = new Set<number>();\n  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n      taken.add(gem.id);\n      w.despawn(gem.id);\n      round.collected += 1;\n      w.emit('gem', { id: gem.id, x: gem.gem.x, z: gem.gem.z, collected: round.collected });\n    }\n  }\n  if (round.collected >= round.gems) endRound(w, round, 'won');\n}\n\n/** Runs the clock down a step at a time (game time is whole steps, never summed seconds); at 0 the round is lost. */\nfunction clock(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  round.left = Math.max(0, round.left - 1);\n  if (round.left === 0) endRound(w, round, 'lost');\n}\n\n/** The starter game: collect every gem before the clock runs out. */\nexport const play = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:play', {\n  description: 'The starter game: run round the arena collecting the gems before the clock runs out.',\n  level: 'level:arena',\n  physics: true,\n  setup(w) {\n    addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), ARENA);\n    const gems = w.settings.get<number>('game.gems');\n    w.spawn({ round: { gems, left: Math.round(w.settings.get<number>('game.seconds') * w.hz) } });\n    scatterGems(w, gems);\n    spawnPlayer(w, [START[0], START[1], START[2]], w.settings.get<number>('game.speed'));\n    w.systems.add('game.collect', collect, { phase: 'rules' });\n    w.systems.add('game.clock', clock, { phase: 'rules' });\n  },\n});\n\nexport default play;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014RVX8A85AzWhiwY33khv7r","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
