{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WWAu9gobSdsKkA4gNoWA6o","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The engine's dev actions (PLAN.md WP 5.6, §5.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Reproducible): the registry kind\n * `devAction`, a change a developer makes to a running scene between steps, recorded so that a replay makes it again,\n * and the engine's own five. An entry says what it changes:\n * - `run(w, args)`: the sim, inside `w.run`, through the session (`session.act(name, args)`: all or nothing, recorded\n *   as the change-point's `dev` with its `args`); a scene's own action of the same name wins (engine/sim/scene.ts);\n * - `settings(args)`: the settings it sets, by path, through the session's store (recorded as `set`, unless view).\n * Its `args` are a schema (engine/core/schema.ts): `devArgs` checks what it is given and fills the defaults before\n * anything changes. `__engine.actions` lists and runs them (engine/dev/actions.ts); `defineDevAction` adds a game's.\n *\n * The engine's, each on the player (the first actor whose `player` is set) unless given an `id`:\n * - `god { on, id }`: the entity holds the component `invulnerable`, so `damage` takes no hit on it\n *   (engine/sim/damage.ts); off, it lets go of it;\n * - `freeze { on }`: the setting `ai.frozen`, so the step skips the systems of the phase `ai` (engine/sim/world.ts),\n *   and the movers they drive stand: each actor that is not a player lets go of its AI's intents, and each living crowd\n *   agent (a component holding every field of `CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS`) stops across the ground;\n * - `spawn { prop, count, distance }`: `count` props of the entry `prop`, `distance` m from the player, 0.4 rad apart\n *   about the way it faces, each on the floor below (the physics' probe from 2 m over its feet, else at its feet);\n * - `travel { at, yaw, id }`: the actor put at `at` (its feet, m), facing `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest\n *   (`placeActor`, engine/sim/actors.ts);\n * - `timeScale { scale }`: the setting `time.scale`, the frame clock's speed (engine/core/time.ts): a view setting,\n *   so it never reaches the sim or a replay.\n *\n * Invariants: an action changes the sim only through `run`, inside the session's capture, so a throw leaves nothing\n * (settings included) and a replay's `dev` makes the same change; `settings` is a pure function of the args.\n * `defineDevActionKinds(registry)` declares the kind, the component `invulnerable`, the setting `ai.frozen` and the\n * engine's five on a registry (the shared one when this module loads; engine/sim/session.ts imports it, so every\n * session finds them). Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/62-developer.js:1-132` (the sandbox's switches, its\n * spawn in a fan before the hero, its travel) and `10-combat.js:106` (god mode: a hit takes nothing), mechanisms only.\n *\n * @example\n * import { registry } from '../core/registry';\n * listDevActions(registry).map((action) => action.id); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']\n * devArgs(findDevAction(registry, 'freeze')!, undefined, 'freeze'); // { on: true }: the default filled\n * // in a scene with a player actor: session.act('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }) puts him there, and record() holds\n * // the change-point { dev: 'travel', args: { at: [3, 0, 5] } }\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\nimport { CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS } from '../physics/crowd';\nimport { physicsOf } from '../physics/binding';\nimport { placeActor, type ActorComponent } from './actors';\nimport { spawnProp } from './props';\nimport { defineComponent } from './state';\nimport { AI_FROZEN, AI_FROZEN_SETTINGS } from './systems';\nimport type { World } from './world';\n\n----\n8: * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\n10: * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\n12: * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\n16: * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\n25: * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\n28: * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\n59:    doc: 'Advice from `createAudio` (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts) when there is no Web Audio, or the context could not be made.',\n63:/** The runtime's state: `locked` until a gesture, then the context's; `off` without Web Audio. */\n68:  /** The context to play into (an `OfflineAudioContext` in a test); one is made on the first gesture by default. */\n69:  context?: BaseAudioContext;\n87:  /** The context's sample rate, once there is one. */\n99:export interface Audio {\n101:  /** The context, once there is one. */\n102:  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\n115:  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\n121:  /** Stops listening and closes the context it made. */\n138:  const volumes = { ...BUS_VOLUMES };\n145:  let context: BaseAudioContext | null = null;\n153:  const stateOf = (): AudioState => (state !== 'open' ? state : context ? context.state : 'locked');\n155:    context = made;\n157:    for (const [bus, value] of Object.entries(volumes)) mixer.volume(bus as AudioBus | 'master', value);\n171:    if (!context) {\n181:    if (context && live(context) && context.state !== 'running') void context.resume().catch(() => {});\n184:  if (options.context) begin(options.context);\n185:  if (!options.context || live(options.context)) {\n187:    if (!options.context && (typeof AudioContext === 'undefined' || !target)) {\n207:    const c = context;\n240:    get context() {\n241:      return context;\n278:      if (!context || !pose) return;\n/**\n * @file A sound definition and its checks (PLAN.md WP 9.1; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a sound is plain data,\n * one voice or a list of voices played together, in the source chip synth's words (`wave`, `freq`, `to`, `dur`,\n * `vol`, `attack`, `hold`, `arp`, `step`, `loop`, `vib`, `filter`, `q`), so its effects, drums and songs copy over as\n * they are (WP 9.2), plus ADSR (`decay`, `sustain`, `release`), a start time `at`, an explicit filter, `fm`, `pluck`\n * and a `delay` echo. `normalizeSound` checks a definition and fills its defaults, throwing a coded error that names\n * the voice and the field.\n *\n * Defaults (the source's): wave `square`, freq 440 Hz, dur 0.15 s (at least 0.012 s), vol 0.3, attack 0.004 s, step\n * 0.06 s, q 1.1. The envelope falls away unless `hold` or an ADSR field is given; a pluck holds by default (`hold:\n * false` makes it fall), because a string fades by itself. A noise voice without `filter` goes through a bandpass that\n * follows its pitch, as in the source. A frequency is a number in Hz or a note name (`noteFreq`), and pitches below\n * 20 Hz are raised to 20 Hz, as in the source. A filter given by its type alone (`filter: 'lowpass'`) follows the\n * voice's pitch; an object gives it its own `freq` (and `to`, a sweep). `pluck` voices keep one pitch: `to`, `arp`,\n * `vib` and `fm` are refused on them, and `fm` on noise. The source's `delay` (a start offset) is `at` here, because\n * `delay` is the echo. Unknown fields and waves are refused with the closest name, never ignored.\n *\n * @example\n * const [voice] = normalizeSound({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 'A4', to: 880, dur: 0.14 }, 44100);\n * voice.f0; // 440\n * @see engine/audio/dsp/render.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\nimport { withSimMath } from '../../core/simMath';\nimport { FILTER_TYPES, type FilterType } from './biquad';\nimport type { EchoSpec } from './delay';\nimport { holdEnvelope, type Envelope } from './envelope';\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from './osc';\n\n/** The codes a definition's checks raise, with their fixes (collected into docs/ERRORS.md by `x docs`). */\nexport const VOICE_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_WAVE: {\n    template: '{where}: there is no wave \"{wave}\"{suggestion}',\n    fix: 'use one of {waves}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) when a voice names a wave the DSP does not make.',\n  },\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_FIELD: {\n    template: '{where} has no field \"{field}\"{suggestion}',\n    fix: 'use only the fields {fields}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a field a voice, filter, fm, pluck or delay does not have: usually a typo, which would otherwise be silently igno\n  },\n  AUDIO_BAD_VALUE: {\n    template: '{where}: {field} is {value}',\n    fix: 'make {field} {rule}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a value of the wrong type or outside its range, and for fields that do not apply to the voice (a pitch change on \n  },\n  AUDIO_BAD_NOTE: {\n    template: '{where}: \"{note}\" is not a note',\n    fix: 'write a frequency in Hz or a note name: a letter A–G, then # or b, then the octave (A4 = 440 Hz, C#5, Bb2)',\n    doc: 'Raised by `noteFreq` and `render` (engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts, render.ts) for a pitch that is neither a positive number nor a note name.',\n----\n/**\n * @file The `song` kind (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a looping tune as data, written\n * in tracker notation, its tracks played on the DSP core's waves and its drums from a kit of `sfx` entries. The\n * engine's five songs (songs.ts) are its entries; a game adds its own with `defineSong`, and `x new song` scaffolds one.\n *\n * A song has a tempo (`bpm`), `steps` per beat and `beats` per bar, and tracks. A track's `notes` hold one token per\n * step: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holding the note before it, `.` a rest, and `|` a bar line, which takes no\n * step. A `drums` track writes kit tokens instead (`k s h o c t`, engine/audio/data/drums.ts). Each track loops on its\n * own length; `intensity` is the music intensity from which a track joins (0: always), for the runtime's layers.\n *\n * Invariants:\n * - The checks (`songProblems`, run when a song is defined): every token is a note, a hold after a note, a rest or a\n *   kit token; a `|` falls on a bar line; each track fills whole bars or divides one; every track's length divides the\n *   song's (its longest track's), which is whole bars; a track's voice is one `render` accepts; ranges per field.\n * - A note plays from its step for its held steps times `gate`, on a held envelope with the track's attack, at the\n *   note's pitch times 2^octave. A drum token plays its kit entry's voices (engine/audio/data/sfx.ts), their gain\n *   times the track's `vol` / 0.18, so a track at the default 0.18 plays the kit as written. Holds never wrap round a\n *   track's end. `songVoices` lays out one pass of the song, track by track; `renderSong` renders it with the DSP,\n *   at least a pass long (passes played back to back keep time), so the same song, seed and rate give the same bits\n *   in Node and Chromium.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3792-3836` (`music`, `_note`: the notation, the hold, the gate, the drum\n * scaling), as data rendered offline; the scheduling belongs to the runtime (WP 9.3).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\n * const registry = createRegistry();\n * const riff = defineSong('song:riff', { beats: 2, tracks: [{ notes: 'C4 - E4 - G4 - E4 -', wave: 'pluck' }] }, registry);\n * songTiming(riff); // { stepSeconds: 0.125, barSteps: 8, steps: 8, seconds: 1 }: 120 bpm, 2 beats a bar\n * renderSong('song:title').length > 0; // true\n * @see engine/audio/data/song.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\nimport type { Schema } from '../../core/schema';\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from '../dsp/osc';\nimport { DEFAULT_RATE, render } from '../dsp/render';\nimport { MAX_SECONDS, normalizeSound, noteFreq, type Voice } from '../dsp/voice';\nimport { DRUM_KIT } from './drums';\nimport { sfxVoices } from './sfx';\nimport { SONGS } from './songs';\n2: * @file The engine's five songs as data (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23): original chiptune loops for a title screen, an\n3- * adventure, a dungeon, a boss fight and a victory jingle, each a `song` entry (engine/audio/data/song.ts) under the \n4- * `song:<name>`.\n5- *\n6- * Invariants: the tracks are the source's, note for note, in its tracker notation (one token per step: a note such as\n7- * `C5`, `-` holding the previous note, `.` a rest, `|` a bar line). Each song is in 4/4 at four steps per beat, so a\n8- * bar is 16 steps, and every track fills whole bars or divides one (song.ts checks it). `song:victory` plays once.\n9- *\n10- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3838-3856` (`E.songs`).\n11- *\n12- * @example\n13- * SONGS['song:dungeon'].bpm; // 96\n14: * Object.keys(SONGS); // ['song:title', 'song:adventure', 'song:dungeon', 'song:boss', 'song:victory']\n15- * @see engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts\n16- */\n17-import type { SongSpec } from './song';\n18-\n19-/** The engine's songs by id. */\n20-export const SONGS: Readonly<Record<string, SongSpec>> = {\n21:  'song:title': {\n22-    bpm: 112,\n23-    steps: 4,\n24-    tracks: [\n25-      {\n26-        wave: 'square',\n27-        vol: 0.16,\n28-        notes:\n29-          'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - \n30-      },\n31-      {\n32-        wave: 'triangle',\n33-        vol: 0.3,\n34-        notes:\n35-          'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2\n36-      },\n37-      { wave: 'drums', vol: 0.14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' },\n38-    ],\n39-  },\n40-  'song:adventure': {\n41-    bpm: 138,\n42-    steps: 4,\n43-    tracks: [\n----\n2: * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n3: * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n15: * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n17: * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n23: * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n26: * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n45:import { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\n46:import { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\n47:import { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\n49:import { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\n50:import { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\n51:import { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\n59:  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n60:  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n110:  /** The virtual device, merged into every sample (`__engine.input` drives it). */\n116:  /** The device used last: prompts follow it. */\n117:  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n135:  /** The label of `action`'s binding on the device used last: `Space`, `A`, `LMB`. */\n137:  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\n138:  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n6: * says what a prompt shows for an action on a device.\n96:  /** What a prompt shows for `action` on `device`: its first code of that device, labelled; `—` when unbound. */\n103: * What a prompt shows for an action bound to `codes` on `device`: its first code of that device, labelled (the","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"e3fb24a4-864e-494a-87c3-ca3431d8cc1d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:48:13.992Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The engine's dev actions (PLAN.md WP 5.6, §5.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Reproducible): the registry kind\n * `devAction`, a change a developer makes to a running scene between steps, recorded so that a replay makes it again,\n * and the engine's own five. An entry says what it changes:\n * - `run(w, args)`: the sim, inside `w.run`, through the session (`session.act(name, args)`: all or nothing, recorded\n *   as the change-point's `dev` with its `args`); a scene's own action of the same name wins (engine/sim/scene.ts);\n * - `settings(args)`: the settings it sets, by path, through the session's store (recorded as `set`, unless view).\n * Its `args` are a schema (engine/core/schema.ts): `devArgs` checks what it is given and fills the defaults before\n * anything changes. `__engine.actions` lists and runs them (engine/dev/actions.ts); `defineDevAction` adds a game's.\n *\n * The engine's, each on the player (the first actor whose `player` is set) unless given an `id`:\n * - `god { on, id }`: the entity holds the component `invulnerable`, so `damage` takes no hit on it\n *   (engine/sim/damage.ts); off, it lets go of it;\n * - `freeze { on }`: the setting `ai.frozen`, so the step skips the systems of the phase `ai` (engine/sim/world.ts),\n *   and the movers they drive stand: each actor that is not a player lets go of its AI's intents, and each living crowd\n *   agent (a component holding every field of `CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS`) stops across the ground;\n * - `spawn { prop, count, distance }`: `count` props of the entry `prop`, `distance` m from the player, 0.4 rad apart\n *   about the way it faces, each on the floor below (the physics' probe from 2 m over its feet, else at its feet);\n * - `travel { at, yaw, id }`: the actor put at `at` (its feet, m), facing `yaw` (its own when absent), at rest\n *   (`placeActor`, engine/sim/actors.ts);\n * - `timeScale { scale }`: the setting `time.scale`, the frame clock's speed (engine/core/time.ts): a view setting,\n *   so it never reaches the sim or a replay.\n *\n * Invariants: an action changes the sim only through `run`, inside the session's capture, so a throw leaves nothing\n * (settings included) and a replay's `dev` makes the same change; `settings` is a pure function of the args.\n * `defineDevActionKinds(registry)` declares the kind, the component `invulnerable`, the setting `ai.frozen` and the\n * engine's five on a registry (the shared one when this module loads; engine/sim/session.ts imports it, so every\n * session finds them). Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/62-developer.js:1-132` (the sandbox's switches, its\n * spawn in a fan before the hero, its travel) and `10-combat.js:106` (god mode: a hit takes nothing), mechanisms only.\n *\n * @example\n * import { registry } from '../core/registry';\n * listDevActions(registry).map((action) => action.id); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']\n * devArgs(findDevAction(registry, 'freeze')!, undefined, 'freeze'); // { on: true }: the default filled\n * // in a scene with a player actor: session.act('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }) puts him there, and record() holds\n * // the change-point { dev: 'travel', args: { at: [3, 0, 5] } }\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { defineSettings, type SettingValue } from '../core/settings';\nimport { CROWD_AGENT_FIELDS } from '../physics/crowd';\nimport { physicsOf } from '../physics/binding';\nimport { placeActor, type ActorComponent } from './actors';\nimport { spawnProp } from './props';\nimport { defineComponent } from './state';\nimport { AI_FROZEN, AI_FROZEN_SETTINGS } from './systems';\nimport type { World } from './world';\n\n----\n8: * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\n10: * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\n12: * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\n16: * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\n25: * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\n28: * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\n59:    doc: 'Advice from `createAudio` (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts) when there is no Web Audio, or the context could not be made.',\n63:/** The runtime's state: `locked` until a gesture, then the context's; `off` without Web Audio. */\n68:  /** The context to play into (an `OfflineAudioContext` in a test); one is made on the first gesture by default. */\n69:  context?: BaseAudioContext;\n87:  /** The context's sample rate, once there is one. */\n99:export interface Audio {\n101:  /** The context, once there is one. */\n102:  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\n115:  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\n121:  /** Stops listening and closes the context it made. */\n138:  const volumes = { ...BUS_VOLUMES };\n145:  let context: BaseAudioContext | null = null;\n153:  const stateOf = (): AudioState => (state !== 'open' ? state : context ? context.state : 'locked');\n155:    context = made;\n157:    for (const [bus, value] of Object.entries(volumes)) mixer.volume(bus as AudioBus | 'master', value);\n171:    if (!context) {\n181:    if (context && live(context) && context.state !== 'running') void context.resume().catch(() => {});\n184:  if (options.context) begin(options.context);\n185:  if (!options.context || live(options.context)) {\n187:    if (!options.context && (typeof AudioContext === 'undefined' || !target)) {\n207:    const c = context;\n240:    get context() {\n241:      return context;\n278:      if (!context || !pose) return;\n/**\n * @file A sound definition and its checks (PLAN.md WP 9.1; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a sound is plain data,\n * one voice or a list of voices played together, in the source chip synth's words (`wave`, `freq`, `to`, `dur`,\n * `vol`, `attack`, `hold`, `arp`, `step`, `loop`, `vib`, `filter`, `q`), so its effects, drums and songs copy over as\n * they are (WP 9.2), plus ADSR (`decay`, `sustain`, `release`), a start time `at`, an explicit filter, `fm`, `pluck`\n * and a `delay` echo. `normalizeSound` checks a definition and fills its defaults, throwing a coded error that names\n * the voice and the field.\n *\n * Defaults (the source's): wave `square`, freq 440 Hz, dur 0.15 s (at least 0.012 s), vol 0.3, attack 0.004 s, step\n * 0.06 s, q 1.1. The envelope falls away unless `hold` or an ADSR field is given; a pluck holds by default (`hold:\n * false` makes it fall), because a string fades by itself. A noise voice without `filter` goes through a bandpass that\n * follows its pitch, as in the source. A frequency is a number in Hz or a note name (`noteFreq`), and pitches below\n * 20 Hz are raised to 20 Hz, as in the source. A filter given by its type alone (`filter: 'lowpass'`) follows the\n * voice's pitch; an object gives it its own `freq` (and `to`, a sweep). `pluck` voices keep one pitch: `to`, `arp`,\n * `vib` and `fm` are refused on them, and `fm` on noise. The source's `delay` (a start offset) is `at` here, because\n * `delay` is the echo. Unknown fields and waves are refused with the closest name, never ignored.\n *\n * @example\n * const [voice] = normalizeSound({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 'A4', to: 880, dur: 0.14 }, 44100);\n * voice.f0; // 440\n * @see engine/audio/dsp/render.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\nimport { withSimMath } from '../../core/simMath';\nimport { FILTER_TYPES, type FilterType } from './biquad';\nimport type { EchoSpec } from './delay';\nimport { holdEnvelope, type Envelope } from './envelope';\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from './osc';\n\n/** The codes a definition's checks raise, with their fixes (collected into docs/ERRORS.md by `x docs`). */\nexport const VOICE_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_WAVE: {\n    template: '{where}: there is no wave \"{wave}\"{suggestion}',\n    fix: 'use one of {waves}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) when a voice names a wave the DSP does not make.',\n  },\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_FIELD: {\n    template: '{where} has no field \"{field}\"{suggestion}',\n    fix: 'use only the fields {fields}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a field a voice, filter, fm, pluck or delay does not have: usually a typo, which would otherwise be silently igno\n  },\n  AUDIO_BAD_VALUE: {\n    template: '{where}: {field} is {value}',\n    fix: 'make {field} {rule}',\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a value of the wrong type or outside its range, and for fields that do not apply to the voice (a pitch change on \n  },\n  AUDIO_BAD_NOTE: {\n    template: '{where}: \"{note}\" is not a note',\n    fix: 'write a frequency in Hz or a note name: a letter A–G, then # or b, then the octave (A4 = 440 Hz, C#5, Bb2)',\n    doc: 'Raised by `noteFreq` and `render` (engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts, render.ts) for a pitch that is neither a positive number nor a note name.',\n----\n/**\n * @file The `song` kind (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a looping tune as data, written\n * in tracker notation, its tracks played on the DSP core's waves and its drums from a kit of `sfx` entries. The\n * engine's five songs (songs.ts) are its entries; a game adds its own with `defineSong`, and `x new song` scaffolds one.\n *\n * A song has a tempo (`bpm`), `steps` per beat and `beats` per bar, and tracks. A track's `notes` hold one token per\n * step: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holding the note before it, `.` a rest, and `|` a bar line, which takes no\n * step. A `drums` track writes kit tokens instead (`k s h o c t`, engine/audio/data/drums.ts). Each track loops on its\n * own length; `intensity` is the music intensity from which a track joins (0: always), for the runtime's layers.\n *\n * Invariants:\n * - The checks (`songProblems`, run when a song is defined): every token is a note, a hold after a note, a rest or a\n *   kit token; a `|` falls on a bar line; each track fills whole bars or divides one; every track's length divides the\n *   song's (its longest track's), which is whole bars; a track's voice is one `render` accepts; ranges per field.\n * - A note plays from its step for its held steps times `gate`, on a held envelope with the track's attack, at the\n *   note's pitch times 2^octave. A drum token plays its kit entry's voices (engine/audio/data/sfx.ts), their gain\n *   times the track's `vol` / 0.18, so a track at the default 0.18 plays the kit as written. Holds never wrap round a\n *   track's end. `songVoices` lays out one pass of the song, track by track; `renderSong` renders it with the DSP,\n *   at least a pass long (passes played back to back keep time), so the same song, seed and rate give the same bits\n *   in Node and Chromium.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3792-3836` (`music`, `_note`: the notation, the hold, the gate, the drum\n * scaling), as data rendered offline; the scheduling belongs to the runtime (WP 9.3).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\n * const registry = createRegistry();\n * const riff = defineSong('song:riff', { beats: 2, tracks: [{ notes: 'C4 - E4 - G4 - E4 -', wave: 'pluck' }] }, registry);\n * songTiming(riff); // { stepSeconds: 0.125, barSteps: 8, steps: 8, seconds: 1 }: 120 bpm, 2 beats a bar\n * renderSong('song:title').length > 0; // true\n * @see engine/audio/data/song.test.ts\n */\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\nimport type { Schema } from '../../core/schema';\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from '../dsp/osc';\nimport { DEFAULT_RATE, render } from '../dsp/render';\nimport { MAX_SECONDS, normalizeSound, noteFreq, type Voice } from '../dsp/voice';\nimport { DRUM_KIT } from './drums';\nimport { sfxVoices } from './sfx';\nimport { SONGS } from './songs';\n2: * @file The engine's five songs as data (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23): original chiptune loops for a title screen, an\n3- * adventure, a dungeon, a boss fight and a victory jingle, each a `song` entry (engine/audio/data/song.ts) under the \n4- * `song:<name>`.\n5- *\n6- * Invariants: the tracks are the source's, note for note, in its tracker notation (one token per step: a note such as\n7- * `C5`, `-` holding the previous note, `.` a rest, `|` a bar line). Each song is in 4/4 at four steps per beat, so a\n8- * bar is 16 steps, and every track fills whole bars or divides one (song.ts checks it). `song:victory` plays once.\n9- *\n10- * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3838-3856` (`E.songs`).\n11- *\n12- * @example\n13- * SONGS['song:dungeon'].bpm; // 96\n14: * Object.keys(SONGS); // ['song:title', 'song:adventure', 'song:dungeon', 'song:boss', 'song:victory']\n15- * @see engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts\n16- */\n17-import type { SongSpec } from './song';\n18-\n19-/** The engine's songs by id. */\n20-export const SONGS: Readonly<Record<string, SongSpec>> = {\n21:  'song:title': {\n22-    bpm: 112,\n23-    steps: 4,\n24-    tracks: [\n25-      {\n26-        wave: 'square',\n27-        vol: 0.16,\n28-        notes:\n29-          'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - \n30-      },\n31-      {\n32-        wave: 'triangle',\n33-        vol: 0.3,\n34-        notes:\n35-          'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2\n36-      },\n37-      { wave: 'drums', vol: 0.14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' },\n38-    ],\n39-  },\n40-  'song:adventure': {\n41-    bpm: 138,\n42-    steps: 4,\n43-    tracks: [\n----\n2: * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n3: * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n15: * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n17: * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n23: * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n26: * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n45:import { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\n46:import { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\n47:import { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\n49:import { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\n50:import { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\n51:import { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\n59:  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n60:  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n110:  /** The virtual device, merged into every sample (`__engine.input` drives it). */\n116:  /** The device used last: prompts follow it. */\n117:  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n135:  /** The label of `action`'s binding on the device used last: `Space`, `A`, `LMB`. */\n137:  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\n138:  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n6: * says what a prompt shows for an action on a device.\n96:  /** What a prompt shows for `action` on `device`: its first code of that device, labelled; `—` when unbound. */\n103: * What a prompt shows for an action bound to `codes` on `device`: its first code of that device, labelled (the","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WWAu9gobSdsKkA4gNoWA6o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
