ngine/app/store.ts | cut -c1-170","description":"Read dev action calls, sky presets, pad cursor and store docs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MjheU9fm5vp8wiUmZkH8z5","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 5.6; doctrine: Agent-operable): the developer's tools\n * on the inspector, registered from this file as `inspectorMember` entries (engine/dev/members.ts), so a page\n * (`x eval \"__engine.actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] })\"`) and `createHeadless` reach the same calls.\n *\n * - `actions.list()`: the dev actions this run has, the scene's own (engine/sim/scene.ts `actions`) and then the\n *   engine's (engine/sim/devActions.ts: god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale, and any `defineDevAction` added), each\n *   with what it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action) or `settings` alone (recorded as set, view ones never).\n * - `actions.run(name, args)`: runs one between steps through the session (`session.act`: the args checked, its\n *   settings set, then its change to the sim, all or nothing), so the replay holds it; the view snaps to the world.\n * - `bot(plan)`: plays the player with the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) over the scene's level: the goals `to`, a `tour`,\n *   `back`, the stop condition `until` (`component.field`), `steps`, a `trace`, its options; through `step`, so each\n *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\n *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\n *\n * Invariants: members change the sim only through the session's recorded operations (engine/dev/members.ts); this\n * module registers them when it loads (engine/app/headless.ts loads it, so every engine has them).\n *\n * @example\n * import { createHeadless } from '../app/headless';\n * import { defineScene } from '../sim/scene';\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('dev-actions-demo', { setup: () => {} }) });\n * const actions = engine.actions as { list(): { name: string }[] };\n * actions.list().map((action) => action.name); // ['freeze', 'god', 'spawn', 'timeScale', 'travel']: none of its own\n * @see engine/dev/actions.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Field, Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { changesSim, listDevActions } from '../sim/devActions';\nimport { getLevel } from '../world/level/level';\nimport { getSite } from '../world/site';\nimport { runBot, type BotPlan } from './bot';\nimport { sweepBot } from './botSweep';\nimport { defineMember } from './members';\n\n/** One dev action as `actions.list()` shows it. */\nexport interface ActionRow {\n  name: string;\n  /** Whose it is: the scene's own, or the engine's. */\n  from: 'scene' | 'engine';\n75:export { defineSkies, defineSky, SKY_FIELDS, type BackdropSpec, type SkyEntry, type SkySpec } from './skyKind';\n/**\n * @file Skies (PLAN.md WP 7.1, §6.6 kind `sky`): what surrounds and lights a level, as presets of data, and\n * `createSky`, which puts a preset on a scene. A `sky` entry gives the background colour, a sky dome (three.js's\n * `SkyMesh` addon, the Preetham daylight model, on a sphere in place of its box: `keepNearPlane`), a backdrop\n * (silhouette layers round the horizon), a sun (a `DirectionalLight` the dome agrees with), the ambient light and fog\n * (engine/gfx/atmosphere.ts), and how bright the light pool's point lights shine (engine/gfx/lights.ts). The kind, its\n * fields and its presets (`sky:hall`, `sky:daylight`) are engine/gfx/skyKind.ts's.\n *\n * Switching presets, or showing the hour's sky (engine/gfx/daylight.ts), changes uniforms, colours and visibility\n * only: the dome and the backdrop stay in the scene, registered with the warm-up, the sun and the pool's lights are\n * made once, and the fog node stays installed. The one exception is who casts shadows (engine/gfx/shadows.ts): a\n * preset with a sun gives the sun the first caster, which changes the shader key, so the renderer warms up again\n * before the next frame instead of stalling it. Nothing here touches the sim, so no preset changes the hash. A look\n * may draw the dome as a clean gradient instead (`gradient`, WP 13.24: the cel look's), a uniform too.\n *\n * The backdrop is baked on the CPU into one strip (engine/gfx/backdrop.ts `bakeBackdrop`), which wraps three times\n * round an open cylinder that follows the camera, its foot just under eye level, drawn first and writing no depth\n * like the dome (`atFarPlane`), so the level always stands in front of both. With `feature:cascadedShadows` on, the sun casts through\n * cascades that follow the camera (engine/gfx/enhanced/csm.ts, through engine/gfx/features.ts); with tiled lighting,\n * the light pool holds 64 lights (engine/gfx/lights.ts). Both come from the renderer's feature report (`features`).\n *\n * Measured on r182 (WP 7.1): its lights node sorts its lights by id, in place, whenever it builds a shader, while the\n * render list gives them in scene order; where the two orders differ the light key flips from frame to frame, and\n * every instanced mesh rebuilds its pipelines (each build names its own instance buffer). So `createSky` adds its\n * lights in id order (the pool, the ambient light, then the sun), and a light made later belongs after them in the\n * scene. And a TSL uniform in the object group (the default) refreshes only when its object or material changes, so\n * a still floor keeps its first fog: the dome's knobs and the fog's numbers are render-group uniforms.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3859-3958` (§21b: the `day` preset's colours), as a cylinder round a 3D\n * camera. Invariants: equal presets bake equal strips; the scene's light count never changes after `createSky`.\n228:  let preset = registry.get('sky', 'sky:daylight') as SkyEntry;\n229-  let baked = ''; // the backdrop baked into the strip, as its spec's text\n230-  const hsl = { h: 0, s: 0, l: 0 };\n231-  let casters = shadowCasters({ shadowCasters: null });\n232-  let split: Casters = { sun: false, points: 0 };\n233-  const applyCasters = () => {\n234-    split = splitCasters(casters, { sun: preset.sun.intensity > 0, points: preset.pointLights > 0 });\n235-    sun.castShadow = split.sun;\n236-    pool.casters = split.points;\n237-  };\n238-\n239-  const sky: Sky = {\n240-    pool,\n241-    atmosphere,\n242-    sun,\n18: * `createRepeat()`, a held direction moving again after 0.35 s and every 0.1 s after; and `createPadCursor(root,\n19: * input)`: with a gamepad used last and a panel open, the left stick moves a cursor over the page (260 px/s, up to\n20: * 1,160 at a full push: shardfall's) and the pad's accept clicks what it is over, so a gamepad works any DOM panel.\n24: * `hearts`) as behaviour, and `shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/app.rs:438-530` (the pad's cursor), in HTML/CSS.\n41:  /** The device used last: the pad's cursor shows only for `gamepad`. */\n61:/** The widgets' stylesheet: the bar, the hearts, the box, the dialog, the menu and the pad's cursor. */\n76:.ui-box { padding: 0.45em 0.7em; }\n83:.ui-dialog { width: min(36em, 90%); min-height: 4.4em; padding: 0.7em 1em; box-sizing: border-box; }\n84:.ui-dialog-name { position: absolute; left: 0.8em; top: -1.1em; padding: 0.1em 0.6em; border: 2px solid #e8e4ff;\n89:.ui-dialog-choices { position: absolute; right: 0.4em; bottom: calc(100% + 0.6em); padding: 0.3em 0.4em; }\n90:.ui-menu { min-width: 10em; padding: 0.4em; }\n91:.ui-menu-title { text-align: center; padding: 0.2em 0.6em 0.4em; }\n/**\n * @file The store (PLAN.md WP 10.9, §9.1, ADR-0024): what a game keeps across sessions, outside the sim (high scores,\n * progress, its settings). `createStore({ prefix, version, mode, backend, migrate })` reads and writes plain data as\n * JSON under `prefix + key` in the page's `localStorage`, else in memory: in Node, where the page blocks storage\n * (advice `APP_STORE_BLOCKED`, once), and in the modes that must leave a player's saves alone, `demo` (a replay or an\n * attract loop), `sandbox` (a developer's throwaway play) and `gallery` (sheets and shots): their memory starts empty\n * and dies with the page, so what they play is never kept over what the player played.\n *\n * Every value is written in its envelope, `{ format: 'my3dge-store/1', version, data }`, and checked when read (shardfall\n * writes a version and never checks it): a value of another format or version is not handed back as it is. With\n * `migrate(data, version)` the store makes it the current version (and writes it back); without, the reader gets its\n * fallback, the value stays until `set` replaces it, and the advice `APP_STORE_VERSION` names the key once.\n *\n * Invariants: storage never throws here (a full or refused write returns false; a value that is not JSON reads as its\n * fallback); values go in and come out as copies (JSON), so a caller's object never aliases the store's; only keys\n * under the prefix are listed or cleared, so games and pages sharing an origin keep apart (pick a prefix of the game's\n * own, `my3dge-game:`). Sim-side code cannot import the app layer, so the sim never reads a store and nothing kept can\n * change a replay. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:196-200` (`store`: get with a fallback, set, remove,\n * never throwing), the fixed `my3d2dge:` prefix made the store's own.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createLog } from '../core/log';\n * const store = createStore({ prefix: 'demo-game:', backend: memoryBackend() });\n * store.set('best', { seconds: 12.5 }); // true\n * store.get('best', null); // { seconds: 12.5 }: a copy","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"a6d73ee7-faaf-48ee-8fb7-4ae2da8328ee","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:48:42.090Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file `__engine.actions` and `__engine.bot` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 5.6; doctrine: Agent-operable): the developer's tools\n * o