{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ApXsdAxMKvmCzC43Ug5mMR","type":"tool_result","content":"16: * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\n19: * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\n22: * screen. Following a player, the cutaways run (the stage's `frame`); `aim(rule, devices)` is his aim from the camera\n95:  /** First person: the player's joints whose body parts it hides from itself, and the ones his arms show. */\n136:   * Moves the camera by one rendered frame and the stand-ins to `alpha`; returns what to draw. The stage's sky follows,\n144:   * sim adds to his shots (the rig's `aimPose`, WP 13.20); undefined without a player.\n217:  /** The sim's read-only queries, for the follow cameras' walls and the puppets' ground; none without physics. */\n225:  /** What the player did last step, for the rig (`cameraPlayer`); null without one. */\n227:  /** The player's body, which his aim's ray skips; -1 without one. */\n229:  /** The doors standing shut after the last step, which stop the follow cameras as walls do (engine/sim/doors.ts). */\n231:  /** Reads the player after a step (`fresh`: after a restart, so nothing he did before counts as a landing), and the\n236:    const entity = run.world.query('actor').find((e) => (e.actor as { player?: boolean }).player === true);\n244:      const actor = other.actor as { player?: boolean; intents?: { look?: readonly [number, number] } };\n245:      if (actor.player === true) continue;\n253:  /** What the camera takes from the run this frame: whom it follows, his eye and what he does, the walls. */\n254:  const follow = (): {\n255:    follow: Vec3;\n259:    player: CameraPlayer | null;\n262:    const player = stage.actors.player();\n263:    const feet = player?.feet ?? stage.centre;\n264:    const eye: Vec3 | undefined = doing?.eye !== undefined ? [feet[0], feet[1] + doing.eye, feet[2]] : player?.posed?.eye; // prettier-ignore\n265:    return { follow: feet, eye, queries: queries(), also: shut, player: doing };\n267:  /** Steps the camera by `dt` with `input`, then draws the player for a first-person camera: his arms, his body hidden. */\n272:    const pose = rig.update({ ...follow(), ...input }, dt);\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts:155:export function cameraPlayer(entity: EntityData, aiming = false): CameraPlayer | null {\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-156-  const actor = entity.actor as { vx?: number; vy?: number; vz?: number; grounded?: boolean } | undefined;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-157-  if (!actor) return null;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-158-  const velocity: Vec3 = [actor.vx ?? 0, actor.vy ?? 0, actor.vz ?? 0];\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-159-  const grounded = actor.grounded === true;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-160-  const motion = entity.motion as Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | undefined;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-161-  const hitAt = (entity.melee as { hitAt?: number } | undefined)?.hitAt;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-162-  const struck = hitAt !== undefined && hitAt >= 0 ? { struck: hitAt } : {};\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-163-  const weapons = entity.weapons as { kick?: readonly number[]; shots?: number } | undefined;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-164-  const out = weapons ? weaponOut(entity) : null;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-165-  const [up, right] = weapons?.kick ?? [0, 0];\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-166-  const armed = !weapons ? {} : out ? { recoil: [up * DEG, -right * DEG] as const, zoom: out.zoom, shots: weapons.shots ?? 0 }\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-167-  const aims = aiming && (!weapons || out !== null); // with weapons, only one out aims\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-168-  if (!motion) {\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-169-    const mode = grounded ? 'ground' : 'air';\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-170-    return { velocity, grounded, mode, sprinting: false, sliding: false, boosted: false, aiming: aims, ...struck, ...armed }; \nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-171-  }\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-172-  const eye = CAMERA_EYE.stand + (CAMERA_EYE.crouch - CAMERA_EYE.stand) * crouchShare(motion);\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-173-  const sliding = motion.sliding === true;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-174-  const boosted = sliding && Number(motion.slideBoost) > 0;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-175-  return { velocity, grounded, eye, mode: String(motion.mode), sprinting: motion.sprinting === true, sliding, boosted, aiming:\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-176-}\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts-177-\n/**\n * @file Camera poses (PLAN.md WP 2.5, §6.3; doctrine: Common ground): what every camera computes each frame, as plain\n * data in three.js's camera words, and the pure math over it. A `CameraPose` is a position, a heading (`yaw`) and a\n * `pitch`, the lens (`projection`, `fov`, `frustumSize`, `zoom`, `near`, `far`, as `PerspectiveCamera` and\n * `OrthographicCamera` name them), the height `boost` (engine/gfx/cameras/boost.ts) and the `distance` to the point\n * it looks at. Every camera (engine/gfx/cameras/{presets,orbit,fly,fixed}.ts) is a pure step `(state, input, dt) →\n * state` and a pure `(state) → pose`, wrapped in a `Camera` object; engine/gfx/cameras/place.ts puts a pose on a\n * three.js camera. None of it needs a GPU, so all of it is tested in Node.\n *\n * Conventions (§6.3): metres, radians, +Y up. `roll` banks the picture about the view direction (+ tips its top right,\n * a lean into a right turn; WP 13.8's effects). `yaw` is the heading of the view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ cos θ,\n * sin θ, cos ψ cos θ) with θ the pitch (+ up), the same angle as the intents' `cam` (engine/input/intents.ts), so\n * `camera.yaw()` goes straight to `intents.fromCamera` and W walks away from the camera; three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y` is ψ + π, since a camera looks down its −Z. right = forward × up = (−cos ψ, 0, sin ψ).\n * `fov` is vertical and in degrees, as `PerspectiveCamera.fov`. A camera's input (`CameraInput`) is plain data that\n * presentation code builds from the devices: gfx never imports input/ (PLAN.md §6.1).\n *\n * Invariants: a pose is frozen and finite (`makePose` checks it: `GFX_BAD_CAMERA`); poses and camera state are view\n * state, never read by the sim or hashed; `dt` is real seconds since the last rendered frame, so a camera's smoothing\n * is the same at any frame rate.\nengine/gfx/cameras/codes.ts:82:  side: 'Side scrolling',\nengine/gfx/cameras/blend.ts:9: * round, its pitch, roll, distance, lens, zoom, boost and planes in step, and the camera stands `distance` back from\nengine/gfx/cameras/blend.ts:65:    roll: mix(p.roll, q.roll, w),\nengine/gfx/cameras/shoulder.ts:85:/** The effects it takes (engine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts): the lens, the sights, half the roll and the punch. */\nengine/gfx/cameras/shoulder.ts:86:export const SHOULDER_EFFECTS: EffectWeights = Object.freeze({ eye: 0, bob: 0, roll: 0.5, fov: 1, punch: 0.5, aim: 1 }); // prettier-ign\nengine/gfx/cameras/rail.ts:2: * @file The depth rail (PLAN.md WP 3.9; doctrine: Common ground): side scrolling with depth, a perspective camera on\nengine/gfx/cameras/blend.test.ts:18:  const east = makePose({ position: [10, 0, 0], yaw: -Math.PI / 2, distance: 10, fov: 40, roll: 0.2 });\nengine/gfx/cameras/blend.test.ts:26:    expect([half.fov, half.roll]).toEqual([50, expect.closeTo(0.1, 9)]);\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts:8: * roll and the punch; the platformer a little punch).\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts:11: * - the sprint lowers the eye `sprintDrop` and rolls up to `sprintRoll` into a turn of `sprintTurn` rad/s or faster;\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts:12: * - a boosted slide (its boost not yet taken back) widens the lens ×`slideFov` and rolls up to `slideRoll` toward a\nengine/gfx/cameras/effects.ts:23: * The drop, the rolls and the lens ease with a