{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBKGsQ2LKr76LP7QSgh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JrVfv7kyjnhEMt6w6XF2XS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; grep -n \"interface Character\\b\" -A36 engine/physics/character.ts | cut -c1-130 | head -60; sed -n 195,240p engine/sim/actors.ts | sed -n 26,46p | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"export function placeActor\" -B6 -A4 engine/sim/actors.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"export function defineTelegraph\\|TELEGRAPH_FIELDS\" engine/world/telegraphs.ts | head -3; sed -n 1,28p engine/world/telegraphs.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"telegraph\" engine/gfx/stage*.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"telegraph\" labs/box/scenes/fight.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-170","description":"Read character fields, placement, and how telegraphs are spawned"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1464,"cache_read_input_tokens":371827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1464},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"eff3a91e-d625-4813-89db-6e550109938d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:33.450Z","request_id":"req_011CgjBKGbn67dNxWEBtU6BC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JrVfv7kyjnhEMt6w6XF2XS":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/_scratch/my-3dge; grep -n \"interface Character\\b\" -A36 engine/physics/character.ts | cut -c1-130 | head -60; sed -n 195,240p engine/sim/actors.ts | sed -n 26,46p | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"export function placeActor\" -B6 -A4 engine/sim/actors.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"export function defineTelegraph\\|TELEGRAPH_FIELDS\" engine/world/telegraphs.ts | head -3; sed -n 1,28p engine/world/telegraphs.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"telegraph\" engine/gfx/stage*.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"telegraph\" labs/box/scenes/fight.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-170","description":"Read character fields, placement, and how telegraphs are spawned"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JrVfv7kyjnhEMt6w6XF2XS","type":"tool_result","content":" * Spawns an actor in a scene with a physics world: its body, and an entity with the component `actor`. Returns the id.\n * An actor on a movement model (engine/physics/movement/, WP 13.3) also holds `motion`, the model's state (holstered\n * unless spawned `holstered: false`), and reads `sprint` (held, pressed), `walk` and `crouch` (held), `crouchToggle`\n * (pressed), the view from `look`, the keys' frame from `cam` (else `look`) and what it faces from `aim` (else\n * `look`), under the live `movement.*` settings (WP 13.4); WP 13.7: the look's pitch and `interact` (pressed) too,\n * riding the scene's ziplines and ladders (engine/sim/rides.ts); WP 13.9: a player's sprint held only while held with\n * `input.sprint` at `hold`, and his crouch toggled by its press with `input.crouch` at `toggle`.\n */\nexport function spawnActor<C extends object>(world: World<C>, spec: ActorSpec): number {\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\n  const body = addCharacter(physics, spec.character, spec.at);\n  const { x, y, z } = feetOf(physics, body, spec.character);\n  const state = { ...createCharacterState(), yaw: spec.yaw ?? 0 };\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors')) {\n    w.systems.add('actors', moveActors, { phase: 'anim' });\n    w.systems.add('actors.readback', readActors, { phase: 'readback' });\n  }\n  const actor = { body, player: spec.player ?? true, character: spec.character, x, y, z, ...state };\n  const motion = spec.character.movement ? { motion: { ...createMotionState(), holstered: spec.holstered ?? true } } : {}; // prettier-ignore\n  if (!spec.anim) return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor });\n255- * shooter model its motion state starts again, holstered as it was, or ducked with `crouch`, its hull crouched from its\n256- * next step on and kept so until it has headroom, for a place no standing hull fits (a crawlspace). A place where the\n257- * level (the queries' as of the last step, one-way platforms aside) stands over its feet lower than its hull's top, up\n258- * its axis, throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` before it moves anything: the body would sink through the floor. For a scene's dev actions: a feel\n259- * course places its player where it measures (engine/dev/feel/course.ts).\n260- */\n261:export function placeActor<C extends object>(\n262-  world: World<C>,\n263-  id: number,\n264-  at: Vec3Like,\n265-  yaw?: number,\n48:export const TELEGRAPH_FIELDS = {\n83:export type Telegraph = Omit<Entry<typeof TELEGRAPH_FIELDS>, 'alpha'> & { readonly alpha: readonly number[] };\n155:    fields: TELEGRAPH_FIELDS,\n/**\n * @file Telegraphs (PLAN.md WP 6.4, §5.6, §6.6): the registry kind `telegraph`, the warning shapes an attack shows on\n * the floor before it lands, as data (an `arc`, a `ring`, a `line` or a `cone`, in metres), and the geometry sim code\n * tests them with: whether a body is inside one when it goes off, and whether it was a near miss (outside, but within\n * `near` metres: a perfect dodge). engine/gfx/fx draws the same shapes at floor height, filling as the wind-up runs.\n *\n * A telegraph is placed where its attacker stands on the floor (`TelegraphPlace`: `position`, the floor's height in\n * `position.y`, facing `yaw`, forward (sin yaw, 0, cos yaw), its wind-up share `u` from 0 to 1, lengths scaled by\n * `size`). The shapes, in that frame:\n * - `arc`: the floor from `inner` to `radius` within `halfAngle` either side of forward (a swing);\n * - `ring`: the floor from `inner` to `radius` all round (`inner` 0: a disc; a slam);\n * - `line`: a strip `width` wide from the place forward `length` metres (a charge, a beam);\n * - `cone`: an arc from the place itself (`inner` 0), the floor shape of a measured hit cone (`coneOf`).\n * Every shape reaches from `yMin` to `yMax` above the floor. `telegraphGap` is a body's signed distance to the shape\n * (exact on the floor, and above or below the heights to the extruded shape, minus the body's radius: below 0 it\n * overlaps); `inTelegraph` and `nearMiss` read it.\n * The fill a view draws is `telegraphFill`: the reach grows from `inner` to `radius` (a line from 0 to `length`).\n *\n * Carried as a concept from Emberdeep (`my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/10-combat.js:315-352`: `FX.telegraph`'s circle, arc,\n * line and ring and `teleNearMiss`'s gaps, a near miss within 16 units, 1 m) and the Stress test's walker arc\n * (`src/stress-world/35-effects.js:84-88`: from 0.6 of the body's radius out to the move's reach, ±0.8 rad, `#ff4a3a`,\n * alpha 0.25 to 0.7 as it fills), rebuilt with exact distances.\n *\n * Invariants: sim-side and pure: no clock, no random stream, no state; `Math.sin`, `Math.cos` called by name (the\n * sim's math swap reaches them). An entry is plain data, every field filled; `inner` stays below `radius`, `yMin`\n * below `yMax`. Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets `telegraph:arc` after a warning.\n *\n * @example\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:4: * a scene draws particles, telegraphs, trails and bolts with no view code of its own. The stage\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:12: * - **Telegraphs**: a component that declares `telegraph` (a string), `position` (an array), `yaw` and `u` (numbers),\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:13: *   and optionally `size`, is a `TelegraphPlace` (engine/world/telegraphs.ts) as plain data: drawn at floor height,\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:14: *   filling, while `telegraph` names one.\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:48:import type { TelegraphPlace } from '../world/telegraphs';\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:62:      'Draws the effects: particles, telegraphs, trails, bolts and camera shake. A view setting: never in the hash.',\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:66:/** The fields a component declares to be drawn as a bolt, and as a telegraph. */\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:68:const TELEGRAPH_FIELDS = { telegraph: 'string', position: 'array', yaw: 'number', u: 'number' } as const;\n9: *   telegraphing its attack on the floor while it winds up, the walkers and slimes taking turns through his attack\n111:    'Box 5: the hall, its hero with a sword, and 36 walkers, slimes and wisps that swing, pounce and shoot at him, telegraphed, as he cuts them down.',","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"07b8c051-f9e4-4c55-b501-bb249b75f32a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:51:33.573Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" * Spawns an actor in a scene with a physics world: its body, and an entity with the component `actor`. Returns the id.\n * An actor on a movement model (engine/physics/movement/, WP 13.3) also holds `motion`, the model's state (holstered\n * unless spawned `holstered: false`), and reads `sprint` (held, pressed), `walk` and `crouch` (held), `crouchToggle`\n * (pressed), the view from `look`, the keys' frame from `cam` (else `look`) and what it faces from `aim` (else\n * `look`), under the live `movement.*` settings (WP 13.4); WP 13.7: the look's pitch and `interact` (pressed) too,\n * riding the scene's ziplines and ladders (engine/sim/rides.ts); WP 13.9: a player's sprint held only while held with\n * `input.sprint` at `hold`, and his crouch toggled by its press with `input.crouch` at `toggle`.\n */\nexport function spawnActor<C extends object>(world: World<C>, spec: ActorSpec): number {\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\n  const body = addCharacter(physics, spec.character, spec.at);\n  const { x, y, z } = feetOf(physics, body, spec.character);\n  const state = { ...createCharacterState(), yaw: spec.yaw ?? 0 };\n  if (!w.systems.has('actors')) {\n    w.systems.add('actors', moveActors, { phase: 'anim' });\n    w.systems.add('actors.readback', readActors, { phase: 'readback' });\n  }\n  const actor = { body, player: spec.player ?? true, character: spec.character, x, y, z, ...state };\n  const motion = spec.character.movement ? { motion: { ...createMotionState(), holstered: spec.holstered ?? true } } : {}; // prettier-ignore\n  if (!spec.anim) return w.spawn({ ...spec.components, ...motion, actor });\n255- * shooter model its motion state starts again, holstered as it was, or ducked with `crouch`, its hull crouched from its\n256- * next step on and kept so until it has headroom, for a place no standing hull fits (a crawlspace). A place where the\n257- * level (the queries' as of the last step, one-way platforms aside) stands over its feet lower than its hull's top, up\n258- * its axis, throws `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` before it moves anything: the body would sink through the floor. For a scene's dev actions: a feel\n259- * course places its player where it measures (engine/dev/feel/course.ts).\n260- */\n261:export function placeActor<C extends object>(\n262-  world: World<C>,\n263-  id: number,\n264-  at: Vec3Like,\n265-  yaw?: number,\n48:export const TELEGRAPH_FIELDS = {\n83:export type Telegraph = Omit<Entry<typeof TELEGRAPH_FIELDS>, 'alpha'> & { readonly alpha: readonly number[] };\n155:    fields: TELEGRAPH_FIELDS,\n/**\n * @file Telegraphs (PLAN.md WP 6.4, §5.6, §6.6): the registry kind `telegraph`, the warning shapes an attack shows on\n * the floor before it lands, as data (an `arc`, a `ring`, a `line` or a `cone`, in metres), and the geometry sim code\n * tests them with: whether a body is inside one when it goes off, and whether it was a near miss (outside, but within\n * `near` metres: a perfect dodge). engine/gfx/fx draws the same shapes at floor height, filling as the wind-up runs.\n *\n * A telegraph is placed where its attacker stands on the floor (`TelegraphPlace`: `position`, the floor's height in\n * `position.y`, facing `yaw`, forward (sin yaw, 0, cos yaw), its wind-up share `u` from 0 to 1, lengths scaled by\n * `size`). The shapes, in that frame:\n * - `arc`: the floor from `inner` to `radius` within `halfAngle` either side of forward (a swing);\n * - `ring`: the floor from `inner` to `radius` all round (`inner` 0: a disc; a slam);\n * - `line`: a strip `width` wide from the place forward `length` metres (a charge, a beam);\n * - `cone`: an arc from the place itself (`inner` 0), the floor shape of a measured hit cone (`coneOf`).\n * Every shape reaches from `yMin` to `yMax` above the floor. `telegraphGap` is a body's signed distance to the shape\n * (exact on the floor, and above or below the heights to the extruded shape, minus the body's radius: below 0 it\n * overlaps); `inTelegraph` and `nearMiss` read it.\n * The fill a view draws is `telegraphFill`: the reach grows from `inner` to `radius` (a line from 0 to `length`).\n *\n * Carried as a concept from Emberdeep (`my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/10-combat.js:315-352`: `FX.telegraph`'s circle, arc,\n * line and ring and `teleNearMiss`'s gaps, a near miss within 16 units, 1 m) and the Stress test's walker arc\n * (`src/stress-world/35-effects.js:84-88`: from 0.6 of the body's radius out to the move's reach, ±0.8 rad, `#ff4a3a`,\n * alpha 0.25 to 0.7 as it fills), rebuilt with exact distances.\n *\n * Invariants: sim-side and pure: no clock, no random stream, no state; `Math.sin`, `Math.cos` called by name (the\n * sim's math swap reaches them). An entry is plain data, every field filled; `inner` stays below `radius`, `yMin`\n * below `yMax`. Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets `telegraph:arc` after a warning.\n *\n * @example\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:4: * a scene draws particles, telegraphs, trails and bolts with no view code of its own. The stage\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:12: * - **Telegraphs**: a component that declares `telegraph` (a string), `position` (an array), `yaw` and `u` (numbers),\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:13: *   and optionally `size`, is a `TelegraphPlace` (engine/world/telegraphs.ts) as plain data: drawn at floor height,\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:14: *   filling, while `telegraph` names one.\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:48:import type { TelegraphPlace } from '../world/telegraphs';\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:62:      'Draws the effects: particles, telegraphs, trails, bolts and camera shake. A view setting: never in the hash.',\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:66:/** The fields a component declares to be drawn as a bolt, and as a telegraph. */\nengine/gfx/stageFx.ts:68:const TELEGRAPH_FIELDS = { telegraph: 'string', position: 'array', yaw: 'number', u: 'number' } as const;\n9: *   telegraphing its attack on the floor while it winds up, the walkers and slimes taking turns through his attack\n111:    'Box 5: the hall, its hero with a sword, and 36 walkers, slimes and wisps that swing, pounce and shoot at him, telegraphed, as he cuts them down.',","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JrVfv7kyjnhEMt6w6XF2XS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
