{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJLtNtJJsGFG4bwT1Q1Zum","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/input/input.ts:12: * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\nengine/input/input.ts:161:  const values = new Map<string, number>();\nengine/input/input.ts:174:      const holds = new Set([...codes.values()].flat().flatMap((code) => heldBase(code) ?? []));\nengine/input/input.ts:175:      table = { of: bindings, version: bindings.version, codes, bound: new Set([...[...codes.values()].flat(), ...holds]), holds }; // prettier-\nengine/input/input.ts:216:      values.set(code, 1);\nengine/input/input.ts:223:        values.delete(each);\nengine/input/input.ts:228:      if (value > 0) values.set(code, value);\nengine/input/input.ts:229:      else values.delete(code);\nengine/input/input.ts:250:    values.clear();\nengine/input/input.ts:310:        values.set(hold, 1);\nengine/input/input.ts:320:        const strength = Math.max(own.held.includes(action) ? 1 : 0, ...codes.map((code) => values.get(code) ?? 0));\nengine/input/input.ts:357:      for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) if (level(action) > 0) out[key] = level(action);\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, those pressed since the last sample (a code that went\n * down, so a tap shorter than a frame still presses); `move`, the map's four move actions as `[right − left, forward −\n * back]` turned by `fromCamera(camera.yaw(), …)`, so W walks away from the camera; `cam`, the camera's heading; `look`\n * (its yaw and pitch) for maps with `look`; `aim`, the camera's point for the map's `aimWith` rule from the free\n * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\n * `view` actions and the system layer (pause, menus) are never buttons in it: `held`, `pressed` and `strength` give\n * every action to the app and the UI, and `onView` hears a view action as it is pressed (a key at once, a pad button at\n * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n * pointer lock and the right stick, scaled by the view settings `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts; the wheel; a map that\n * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n * `use(map)` switches the map live (one per camera mode, WP 13.9), what is held read through it from the next sample;\n * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n * on (WP 13.20) is held back as it goes down, until it is a tap or a hold (`sample`).\n *\n * Clearing: a page blur, the page going hidden and `clear()` let go of every held code and drop pending presses, so\n * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants: nothing here reads a clock; edges are counted per sample; a code is held only between its press and\n * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:482-512, 542-555, 594-622` (the input object, blur, `move`, `tick`),\n * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n *\n * @example\n * const window = new EventTarget();\n * const input = createInput({ window, document: new EventTarget(), element: new EventTarget() });\n * const key = (type: string, code: string) => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(type), { code }));\n * ['KeyW', 'Space'].forEach((code) => key('keydown', code)), key('keyup', 'Space'); // a tap between two frames\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => Math.PI / 2 }); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], cam: 1.5707963267948966, p: ['jump'] }\n * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => 0 }).move; // [0, 1]: still held; the camera turned, so W walks +Z now\n * @see engine/input/input.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SYSTEM_ACTIONS } from './actionMaps';\nimport { createBindings, pickLabel, type Bindings, type BindingsStorage } from './bindings';\nimport { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\nimport { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\nimport type { AimDevices, AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\nimport { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\nimport { fromCamera } from './intents';\nimport { lookOptions, scaleLook, type LookOptions } from './look';\n\n/** A camera as the input reads it (the app's, over its view): its heading, its pitch for the look, and the aim. */\nexport interface CameraLike {\n  yaw(): number;\n  pose?(): { readonly pitch: number };\n  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n}\n\n/** How an input is made; in a page every field has its default. */\n};\n\n/** The presets, by id. */\nexport const PRESETS: Readonly<Record<string, ActionMapSpec>> = {\n  'actionMap:thirdPerson': {\n    description: 'A third-person or top-down action game (the default): Space jumps, Shift dashes, the mouse fights.',\n    actions: {\n      ...WALK,\n      jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'],\n      dash: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'KeyK', 'PadEast', 'PadLeftTrigger'],\n      attack: ['MouseLeft', 'KeyJ', 'PadWest', 'PadRightTrigger'],\n      skill: ['MouseRight', 'KeyL', 'PadNorth', 'PadRightShoulder'],\n      interact: ['KeyE', 'PadLeftShoulder'],\n    },\n  },\n  'actionMap:firstPerson': {\n    description: 'A first-person game: the mouse looks (pointer lock), the left button fires, C crouches.',\n    actions: {\n      ...WALK,\n      jump: ['Space', 'PadSouth'],\n      crouch: ['KeyC', 'ControlLeft', 'PadEast'],\n      sprint: ['ShiftLeft', 'PadLeftStick'],\n      fire: ['MouseLeft', 'PadRightTrigger'],\n      aim: ['MouseRight', 'PadLeftTrigger'],\n      reload: ['KeyR', 'PadWest'],\n      interact: ['KeyE', 'PadNorth'],\n    },\n    look: true,\n    aimWith: 'centre',\n    lock: true,\n  },\n  'actionMap:platformer': {\n    description: 'Side-scrollers: Space, Z or K jump, X or J attack, Shift or C dash.',\n    actions: {\n      ...WALK,\n      jump: ['Space', 'KeyZ', 'KeyK', 'PadSouth'],\n      attack: ['KeyX', 'KeyJ', 'MouseLeft', 'PadWest'],\n      dash: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'KeyC', 'KeyL', 'PadEast', 'PadRightShoulder'],\n      skill: ['KeyE', 'KeyV', 'MouseRight', 'PadNorth'],\n    },\n  },\n  'actionMap:shmup': {\n    description: \"Shoot-'em-ups: Space, Z or J fire (hold for autofire), X or K bomb.\",\n    actions: {\n      ...WALK,\n      fire: ['Space', 'KeyZ', 'KeyJ', 'MouseLeft', 'PadSouth', 'PadRightTrigger'],\n      bomb: ['KeyX', 'KeyK', 'MouseRight', 'PadEast', 'PadLeftTrigger'],\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nfor (const [id, spec] of Object.entries(PRESETS)) {\n  if (!sharedRegistry.kinds().includes('actionMap') || !sharedRegistry.has('actionMap', id)) {\n    defineActionMap(id, spec);\n  }\n}\n/**\n * @file The mouse device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): buttons over the game's element as codes (`MouseLeft`…), the wheel as\n * taps (`WheelUp`, `WheelDown`) and zoom steps, the pointer's position for aiming, and pointer lock for mouse look:\n * while the element holds the lock, movement turns the view by `lookSpeed` radians per pixel.\n *\n * `lock()` asks for pointer lock (browsers grant it only inside a click or key handler, and let Escape out of it);\n * `locked` follows the document's `pointerlockchange`. `takeLook()` and `takeZoom()` return what gathered since the\n * last call and start again from zero, once per rendered frame: look is `[right, up]` radians (screen y is down, so up\n * is −y unless `invertY`; the page's input takes counts, `lookSpeed` 1, and scales them by the view settings\n * `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts), zoom is wheel notches (+ towards the screen, as a wheel pushed forward zooms in).\n * `pointer()` says where the pointer is, and with an element that has a box (a canvas) where on it as `at`, from −1\n * to 1 with +y up, as three.js's normalized device coordinates: where the pointer aims (engine/input/aim.ts).\n *\n * Invariants: a button is pressed only over the element, and released wherever it is let go; the context menu never\n * opens over the element, so the right button binds; wheel deltas in lines and pages are converted to pixels (40 and\n * 800 a unit) and one notch is 100 px, as Chromium scrolls. `attachMouse` returns the device; `detach()` removes its\n * listeners.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:501-507` (mouse buttons over the canvas, the context menu), with pointer\n * lock and the wheel added.\n *\n * @example\n * const element = new EventTarget();\n * const presses: string[] = [];\n * const sink = { press: (code: string) => presses.push(code), release() {}, analog() {}, used() {}, bound: () => true };\n * const mouse = attachMouse({ element, target: new EventTarget() }, sink);\n * element.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('pointerdown'), { pointerType: 'mouse', button: 2, clientX: 5, clientY: 6 }));\n * element.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event('wheel'), { deltaY: -200, deltaMode: 0 }));\n * presses; // ['MouseRight', 'WheelUp']\n * mouse.takeZoom(); // 2: two notches towards the screen","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"a32a2c5d-bc59-497c-a17e-5498778dbed8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:56:02.386Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"engine/input/input.ts:12: * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\nengine/input/input.ts:161:  const values = new Map<string, number>();\nengine/input/input.ts:174:      const holds = new Set([...codes.values()].flat().flatMap((code) => heldBase(code) ?? []));\nengine/input/input.ts:175:      table = { of: bindings, version: bindings.version, codes, bound: new Set([...[...codes.values()].flat(), ...holds]), holds }; // prettier-\nengine/input/input.ts:216:      values.set(code, 1);\nengine/input/input.ts:223:        values.delete(each);\nengine/input/input.ts:228:      if (value > 0) values.set(code, value);\nengine/input/input.ts:229:      else values.delete(code);\nengine/input/input.ts:250:    values.clear();\nengine/input/input.ts:310:        values.set(hold, 1);\nengine/input/input.ts:320:        const strength = Math.max(own.held.includes(action) ? 1 : 0, ...codes.map((code) => values.get(code) ?? 0));\nengine/input/input.ts:357:      for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) if (level(action) > 0) out[key] = level(action);\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, 