{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LZF6v6EEdKxmVmK8XCgpX4","type":"tool_result","content":"2: * @file Actors (PLAN.md WP 3.2; WP 3.7 adds the animator): entities that walk, jump and dash through the character\n3: * controller (engine/physics/character.ts). `spawnActor(w, { at, character, player })` adds a capsule body to the\n12: * sound map reads it). Gravity: `physics.characterGravity` unless the settings name one; the weight on dynamic floors\n24: * Carried from shardfall@fa2dab6 (`pavilion-lite/src/character.rs:179-399`: the order of a step, the events).\n26: * import { createCharacter } from '../physics/character';\n33: *     spawnActor(w, { at: [0, 0, 0], character: createCharacter({ speed: 5 }) });\n41:import { ANIMATOR_FIELDS, type AnimatorData, type AnimatorOptions } from '../anim/character';\n59:} from '../physics/character';\n79:  character: { type: 'any', default: createCharacter(), description: 'Its settings: what createCharacter returned.' },\n87:/** The component `actor`: an entity the character controller moves. */\n91:  character: Character;\n99:/** The component `animator`: an actor's character animator as plain data, and what its game code tells its body. */\n140: * `secondary` (engine/sim/reactions.ts), the setting `physics.characterGravity` and the controls' `input.sprint` and\n147:  if (!registry.kinds().includes('setting') || !registry.has('setting', 'physics.characterGravity')) {\n42:import { defineSchema, freezeValue, parse, type EntryOf, type Field, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\n154:  return freezeValue(parse(CHARACTER_FIELDS, applyMovement(spec, registry), 'createCharacter(spec)'));\n12: * - **`secondary`** (`SECONDARY_FIELDS`): the secondary motion the view hangs on an actor's puppet (engine/anim/\n13- *   secondary.ts `Secondary`: hair, a cape, a tail) and its colour. The sim only carries it, as it carries a build or\n14- *   a stand-in's material: the view steps the chains, so none of their motion reaches the hash.\n15- *\n16- * Invariants: everything a reaction remembers is in its component (the `Reactions` here are scratch, loaded at every\n17- * call), so a capture restores it exactly; a body at rest (no flinch, nothing playing) steps for nothing.\n18- *\n19- * @example\n20- * import { Vector3 } from '../core/math';\n21- * import { createWorld } from './world';\n22- * const w = createWorld({ seed: 1 });\n23- * const id = w.spawn({});\n24- * reactTo(w, id, (r) => r.knockDown(new Vector3(0, 0, -1), 0)); // struck from the front: it falls onto its back\n--\n74:export const SECONDARY_FIELDS = defineSchema({\n75-  hair: {\n76-    type: 'string',\n77-    enum: ['', 'long', 'ponytail'],\n78-    default: '',\n79-    description: 'Hair from the back of the head (engine/anim/secondary.ts HAIR: long or ponytail), or empty for none.',\n80-  },\n81-  cape: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'A cape from the backs of the shoulders.' },\n82-  tail: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'A tail from the back of the pelvis.' },\n83-  color: { type: 'string', default: '#7a2430', description: 'Their colour, a CSS hex colour.' },\n/**\n * @file The box's sound in its page (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 9.5, I-23): `createBoxSound()` makes the page's audio runtime\n * (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts: locked, silent, until the first key, click or end of a touch) and returns `frame`,\n * which the page runs once per rendered frame after the draw (labs/box/main.ts hands it to `createEngine`'s\n * `onFrame`). Each frame it:\n * - puts the listener at the camera, and gives the runtime the sim's read-only `QueryView`, so walls muffle sounds;\n * - plays the sim's new events as their sounds (labs/box/sounds/events.ts), each placed where it happened;\n * - sets the room's reverb from the scene's level (`BOX_ROOMS`: the hall's, the room's);\n * - keeps the torch ambience going: `sfx:boxTorch` looped on the `TORCH.voices` torches nearest the listener (the\n *   level's light spots tagged `torch`), a voice staying on its torch until another is `TORCH.keep` m nearer;\n * - plays the demo song `song:boxHall` (asked for at once, heard from the first gesture), at intensity 1 while\n *   blows land (`hit`, `shot`, `slam`, `slain`) and back to 0 once `MUSIC.calm` seconds pass without one.\n *\n * `info()` reports it as plain data: the runtime's own `info()`, what the events asked for and what played. In a page\n * it is published as `window.__boxSound`, which tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts reads; nothing else reads it.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only: it reads the frame and never changes the sim, so the box's hashes are the same with\n * sound or without. Every event is asked for once, played or not (still locked, or dropped by the voice limits).\n *\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the box's own files.\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/main.ts\n * // const sound = createBoxSound();\n * // await createEngine({ canvas, scenes, levels, onFrame: sound.frame });\n * // window.__boxSound.info().audio.state; // 'locked' until a key, then 'running'\n * @see labs/box/sounds/page.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  createAudio,\n3: * (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts: locked, silent, until the first key, click or end of a touch) and returns `frame`,\n11: * - plays the demo song `song:boxHall` (asked for at once, heard from the first gesture), at intensity 1 while\n15: * it is published as `window.__boxSound`, which tests/e2e/box-audio.spec.ts reads; nothing else reads it.\n26: * // window.__boxSound.info().audio.state; // 'locked' until a key, then 'running'\n134:  audio.music(MUSIC.song, { intensity });\n157:      const voice = audio.play(TORCH.sfx, { position: lights[i].position, loop: true, vol: TORCH.vol });\n166:      audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined);\n169:      if (next !== room) audio.room((room = next));\n176:        if (audio.play(event.sfx, position ? { vol, position, duck } : { vol, duck })) played++;\n180:      if (want !== intensity) audio.intensity((intensity = want));\n183:      audio: audio.info(),\n19: * const pad = createScriptedGamepad('2 left=0,-1 tap=South\\n1 rt=0.7', { index: 2 });\n20- * pad.next(); // true: frame 1, South down, the left stick forward\n21- * pad.gamepad.buttons[0].pressed; // true\n22- * pad.next(); // true: frame 2, the tap is over\n23- * pad.gamepad.buttons[0].pressed; // false\n24- * pad.next(); // true: frame 3\n25- * pad.gamepad.buttons[7].value; // 0.7: the right trigger\n--\n81:export function createScriptedGamepad(script: string, options: { index?: number; id?: string } = {}): ScriptedGamepad {\n82-  const lines = parsePadScript(script);\n83-  const buttons = PAD_BUTTONS.map(() => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\n84-  const pad = {\n85-    id: options.id ?? 'Scripted gamepad (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 045e Product: 02ea)',\n86-    index: options.index ?? 0,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"70466ed3-618e-4e65-a7cc-63ccc1b116cf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:03.955Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2: * @file Actors (PLAN.md WP 3.2; WP 3.7 adds the animator): entities that walk, jump and dash through the character\n3: * controller (engine/physics/character.ts). `spawnActor(w, { at, character, player })` adds a capsule body to the\n12: * sound map reads it). Gravity: `physics.characterGravity` unless the settings name one; the weight on dynamic floors\n24: * Carried from shardfall@fa2dab6 (`pavilion-lite/src/character.rs:179-399`: the order of a step, the events).\n26: * import { createCharacter } from '../physics/character';\n33: *     spawnActor(w, { at: [0, 0, 0], character: createCharacter({ speed: 5 }) });\n41:import { ANIMATOR_FIELDS, type AnimatorData, type AnimatorOptions } from '../anim/character';\n59:} from '../physics/character';\n79:  character: { type: 'any', default: createCharacter(), description: 'Its set