{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDnCRFTMhExue4uua6V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R1FWkCdgzq2HbQSfLHc6q1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","offset":215,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8927,"cache_read_input_tokens":551589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8927},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"67bd123f-3c3f-46cd-afa3-c92bda646cd7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:22:35.272Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDnC88hekD6WvQC4ZdU","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01R1FWkCdgzq2HbQSfLHc6q1":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","offset":215,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R1FWkCdgzq2HbQSfLHc6q1","type":"tool_result","content":"215\t    footr: ['KeyE', 'MouseRight', 'PadRightTrigger', 'PadRightShoulder', 'Space'],\n216\t    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'],\n217\t    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'PadSouth', 'PadEast', 'PadWest', 'PadNorth'],\n218\t  },\n219\t  values: { 'game:r': 'right', 'game:l': 'left', 'game:f': 'forward', 'game:b': 'back', 'game:fl': 'footl', 'game:fr': 'footr' },\n220\t  lock: true,\n221\t});\n222\t```\n223\t\n224\tThe sim reads raw lean as `game:r − game:l`, `game:f − game:b` (a key absent is 0), not the camera-turned `move`.\n225\tTriggers count as \"held\" from 0.5 but their `values` are analog below that.\n226\t\n227\t`actionMap:roam` is the same walk block plus `jump: ['Space', 'PadWest']`, `use: ['KeyE', 'Enter', 'MouseLeft', 'PadSouth']`,\n228\t`walk: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight']`, `plan: ['Tab', 'PadNorth']`, `wave: ['KeyC', 'PadEast']`, `lock: true`.\n229\t\n230\tFront-end screens use the engine's system layer (`uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, `uiUp`…), which no map can rebind, with a map that\n231\thas `lock: false`, or a click on the canvas behind a menu captures the pointer **[source]**. Sand Garden uses a copy of the\n232\tbalance map with `lock: false`, so the pointer stays visible: the page sends its place as `game:pointer`.\n233\t\n234\tInside activities, read only the map's actions, never `uiAccept`: Space is also breath. Skipping a demonstration is `act`.\n235\tThe first time a mouse player needs the lean, show \"Click to lean with the mouse\": browsers grant pointer lock only in a click.\n236\t\n237\t**Mouse lean:** while pointer-locked in an activity, the page adds `pointermove`'s `movementX/Y` per frame and sends\n238\tthem with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:mouse', [dx, dy])`. The sim keeps `mouseTarget += delta × sensitivity`,\n239\tdecaying with a 0.6 s time constant. Sensitivity lives in Settings.\n240\t\n241\t**Rumble:** a light `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` on topple, on beats in Step Class, and growing with\n242\t`r` near the edge; try/catch around it; a Settings toggle.\n243\t\n244\t---\n245\t\n246\t## 5. Structure\n247\t\n248\t**The Programme.** A five-day residency: a first full play takes about 45 minutes. Each day is a Morning Check plus three\n249\tactivities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\n250\t\n251\t| Day | Activities |\n252\t|---|---|\n253\t| 1 | Morning Check (tutorial) · Pose Class A (Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron) · Still Pond · a walk to find the Noticeboard |\n254\t| 2 | Morning Check · Reps Hall · Sand Garden · Pose Class B (Archer, Comma, Napkin) |\n255\t| 3 | Morning Check · Paddle Glide · The Line · Step Class |\n256\t| 4 | Morning Check · Hoop Patrol · Cliff Plunge · Island Jog with Gerald |\n257\t| 5 | Morning Check · Group Class (you and CPU guests) · Pose Class C (Bridge, Lighthouse) · The Great Tilt |\n258\t| After | Final Morning Check, credits, then Free Play with every activity and daily checks |\n259\t\n260\tFinishing all of a day lets you sleep at your hut (walk there, or pick it from the Programme). Every activity can also be\n261\treplayed from the Noticeboard once met. Activities have no fail state: finishing at any rank counts.\n262\t\n263\t**Getting around.** You may walk everywhere, and the island rewards it, but nothing requires it: every Programme and\n264\tNoticeboard item has \"Go\", which fades to the station. A controller player on a sofa never has to cross the island.\n265\t\n266\t**Wobble Age.** The Morning Check's result, from 18 to 82: `age = round(18 + 64 × (1 − s)^k)`, `k` is `game.age.k` (1.3).\n267\tOne big number, a remark, a stamp on the calendar, and a line graph of at most seven points. Always compared with yesterday,\n268\tin a tone of mild scientific surprise.\n269\t\n270\t**Pebbles and your Cairn.** Pebbles are the currency: 1 to 5 per activity by rank, plus 20 hidden around the island. You\n271\tnever spend them. They stack, one by one, on a physical cairn in the Plaza, with a satisfying clack. The cairn leans\n272\tslightly according to your last Wobble Age and stands true at 18. Thresholds unlock things, shown on the Noticeboard:\n273\t10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \"Unsettling\" stamp set.\n274\t\n275\t**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \"Did you know?\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\n276\tto watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\n277\t\n278\t**Tilt as story.** A value `island.tilt` starts at 0.4° on Day 1 and rises by 0.5° a day, so drinks slide, marbles roll,\n279\tloose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\n280\t\n281\t**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\n282\toutfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\n283\t(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\n284\t\n285\t**Built to grow.** Days, poses, charts, trays, courses, lines, lures and settings are all data tables, one file each, so\n286\tlater content is adding rows. Keep it that way: it is part of the brief.\n287\t\n288\t---\n289\t\n290\t## 6. Activities\n291\t\n292\tEvery activity is a module exposing the same shape: `{ id, title, station, camera, map, setup, step, teardown, score,\n293\tbot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\n294\tHUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\n295\t45-second form for rounds (section 9).\n296\t\n297\t| Activity | Station | Camera | Verbs |\n298\t|---|---|---|---|\n299\t| Morning Check | Plaza | Front, low, slow push-in | Lean, a foot |\n300\t| Pose Class | Pavilion | Three-quarter, drifting orbit round your mat | Lean, foot or both |\n301\t| Reps Hall | Annex | Side three-quarter, mirror behind | Lean scrubs the body |\n302\t| Step Class | Annex | Behind and above, class in view | Feet, both, some lean |\n303\t| Still Pond | Pond | Fixed portrait, front | Both, and nothing else |\n304\t| The Line | Lagoon | Behind and above, dolly along the line | Feet, lean x |\n305\t| Paddle Glide | Lagoon | Chase, low | Lean, feet |\n306\t| Sand Garden | Terrace | Top-down, slight perspective | Lean, or pointer |\n307\t| Cliff Plunge | North Cliff | Side dolly, falling follow, water-level splash | Both, lean |\n308\t| Hoop Patrol | Hoop Beach | Front, wide | Lean in circles, or feet |\n309\t| Island Jog | Whole coast | Chase (engine `cam3=chase`) | Stick, feet |\n310\t\n311\t### Morning Check (about 75 s)\n312\t\n313\tTare's Platform. Tare asks one yes/no question for the day (it changes only the remark). Then three tests:\n314\t\n315\t1. **Still Ring**, 12 s: stay inside a ring of r = 0.22, narrowing to 0.16 for the last 4 s. `A` = share of steps inside.\n316\t2. **Reach**, up to 24 s: six targets (r = 0.16) at radius 0.55 in a seeded order; hold each 0.5 s. `B` = 1 − time/24.\n317\t3. **One Foot**, 8 s: hold the foot Tare names; instability × 1.6; ring r = 0.3. Letting go pauses and drains. `C` = share inside.\n318\t\n319\t`s = 0.45A + 0.3B + 0.25C`; score `s × 1000`; Wobble Age as in section 5. Reveal: a large CSS dial spins past 100, \"recalibrating\",\n320\tovershoots, and settles. The Day 1 version introduces each verb with one line at a time.\n321\t\n322\t### Pose Class (about 2.5 min, three poses)\n323\t\n324\tPlumb demonstrates on the front mat (4 s, skippable). \"Now you.\"\n325\t\n326\t- **Enter:** a guide dot travels a curved path on the disc from centre to the pose's *seat*. Stay within 0.18 of it and\n327\t  progress advances; progress scrubs the pose strip, so the body goes into the pose exactly as your thumb does. If you never\n328\t  follow, Plumb waits 10 s and moves on: \"We will call that a start.\"\n329\t- **Hold:** `game.pose.hold` s (12) with the CoB in the seat ring (`game.pose.ring`, 0.2), breathing with the guide, while\n330\t  your off-seat lean visibly tips the body over. CPU guests hold too. Plumb does not move.\n331\t- **Release:** \"And rest.\" Score: `1000 × (0.7 × inRing + 0.3 × sync) − 60 × topples`, class mean is the result.\n332\t\n333\t| Pose (id) | What it is | Seat (x, y) | Rule |\n334\t|---|---|---|---|\n335\t| Seated Nothing (`nothing`) | Cross-legged, hands on knees | 0, 0 | Sway × 0.5; breath weighs 60% |\n336\t| The Patient Chair (`chair`) | Knees bent, arms forward | 0, −0.35 | Hold both feet throughout, so no breath; sway climbs with time |\n337\t| The Heron (`heron`) | One leg, foot on thigh, palms overhead | 0, 0 | Hold the standing foot; instability × 1.5 |\n338\t| The Archer (`archer`) | Long lunge, arms out | 0.35, 0.35 | Instability × 1.2 |\n339\t| The Sideways Comma (`comma`) | Side bend | 0.5, 0 then −0.5, 0 | Two holds, 8 s each |\n340\t| The Folded Napkin (`napkin`) | Forward fold | 0, 0.5 | Low camera; the Gull lands on your back halfway |\n341\t| The Polite Bridge (`bridge`) | On your back, hips lift | 0, 0 | Hips follow your lungs; breath weighs 70% |\n342\t| The Lighthouse (`lighthouse`) | Tiptoe, arms straight up | 0, 0 | Ring 0.14; sway × 1.2 |\n343\t\n344\t### Reps Hall (about 90 s, three exercises)\n345\t\n346\tThe signature \"thumb is the exercise\" activity. A tall gauge on the HUD shows a band moving at the tempo\n347\t(`game.reps.tempo`, 3 s a rep). Stick depth moves your marker and scrubs the body. Stay within 0.2 of the band to bank the\n348\trep. Gerald, beside you, does two for each of yours.\n349\t\n350\t- **Deep Knees** (10): pull back to squat, return to stand.\n351\t- **Polite Push-Ups** (8): hold both feet (\"palms on the floor\") and scrub the push-up clip with the stick.\n352\t- **Side Lunges** (10): stick x, alternating sides.\n353\t\n354\tThe band speeds up a little and sway rises near the end. Near the finish the counter cheats: \"9 of 10\" becomes \"10 of\n355\t11\". Plumb: \"Four more. I may be lying.\" Score: mean rep accuracy.\n356\t\n357\t### Step Class (about 100 s)\n358\t\n359\tRhythm on a step platform in the Annex, three phrases at 104, 112 and 120 BPM (`game.step.bpm` scales them), charts as\n360\tstrings in `labs/game/scenes/data/charts.ts`: `\"L . R . L . R . | L L R . B . . .\"`. Footprints scroll to a hit line on the\n361\tHUD, floor tiles light in the world. Notes: L, R, B (both, a jump) and side steps (lean plus foot).\n362\t\n363\tWindows: Perfect ±3 steps, Good ±7 (`game.step.perfect`, `game.step.good`). Combo adds up to × 1.5. The guests behind you\n364\tfollow your combo: lose it and they fall out of time, one by one, politely.\n365\t\n366\t**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\n367\tevents fire claps and kicks at full level. The bed has no drums, so nothing flams against it. Timing is in sim steps,\n368\tnever audio time.\n369\t\n370\t### Still Pond (75 s; 45 s in rounds)\n371\t\n372\tThe funniest thing in the game, and almost no input. You sit cross-legged on a jetty at dawn. **Composure** starts at 1000.\n373\tThe only correct input is breathing with the guide. Anything else is \"You moved\": stick past 0.25, any button, a stray\n374\tfoot, or mouse movement past a small threshold. Each costs `game.pond.penalty` (80), debounced 1 s, and sends a ripple\n375\tacross the pond while the Frog turns to look.\n376\t\n377\tScore: `Composure × (0.5 + 0.5 × sync)`, so doing nothing at all earns \"Adequate\".\n378\t\n379\tLures, from a seeded table, every 6–10 s, escalating:\n380\t\n381\t- A big glyph prompt for whichever device you use: \"PRESS NOW\".\n382\t- Tare: \"Psst. Is this on? Press ✕ for yes.\"\n383\t- The phone-shaped stone buzzes.\n384\t- The Frog sits on your knee. The Gull lands on your head.\n385\t- A fake pause menu slides in with \"Resume\" highlighted.\n386\t- \"Your controller appears to be disconnected. Press any button.\"\n387\t- Plumb, very quietly: \"You are doing it wrong.\"\n388\t- The credits roll. \"Thanks for playing! Press ✕ to continue.\"\n389\t\n390\tReal pause (Options, Esc) always works and costs nothing. Ending: \"You did nothing for seventy-five seconds. Nobody has\n391\tever been prouder of you. Nobody was watching.\"\n392\t\n393\t### The Line (about 75 s)\n394\t\n395\tA 40 m slackline across the lagoon with three flags. Alternate feet to step: each step moves 0.75 m and kicks you sideways\n396\t(`game.line.stepKick`, 0.35); the same foot twice is a stumble. Lean x fights it. Gusts every 6–10 s, telegraphed 1.5 s ahead\n397\tby ripples and a flag on Tare's little boat (`game.line.gust`). At 15 m the Gull lands on your arm, adding a steady bias\n398\tuntil you flick it off with a fast stick flip. Falling is a large splash, then Tare's boat takes you back to the last\n399\tflag: \"You have left the line. The line is fine.\" After 120 s the boat collects you: \"The line closes at this time.\"\n400\tScore: `1000 − 150 × falls − 8 × max(0, seconds − 50)`, times the share of the line crossed.\n401\t\n402\t### Paddle Glide (75 s)\n403\t\n404\tStand on a board. Forward lean is speed (`game.paddle.speed`, 6 m/s), side lean steers (1.2 rad/s), feet alternating at\n405\tabout 1.2 Hz give +30% and a kick. Twelve buoy gates round the lagoon with seeded jitter. A ferry wake at gate 7 and a\n406\tcrossing turtle at gate 9 shove your CoB. A topple is a splash and a 3-second remount. Score: gates × 60 + up to 280 for\n407\ttime.\n408\t\n409\t### Sand Garden (90 s, five trays)\n410\t\n411\tA raked sand tray on a stand, seen from above. Lean tilts it up to 12° (`game.garden.tilt`); the mouse pointer's place on\n412\tthe tray does the same. Marbles obey your own 2D integrator in the sim (slope × `game.garden.gravity`, friction, ridge\n413\tsegments, holes that catch below `game.garden.sink` speed). Trays are data, 1–3 marbles each, rising to moving rakes and a\n414\tgap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\n415\t\n416\t### Cliff Plunge (three dives)\n417\t\n418\tA 14 m cliff. **Compose:** hold ring and breath for 4 s to fill power. **Go:** release both feet as a swinging gauge peaks.\n419\t**Air** (about 2 s): lean y spins you, lean x twists, scrubbing a rotation strip. Enter the water within 15° of vertical.\n420\tThree Gulls hold up score cards, 0 to 10. Sum of all cards, scaled to 1000. Huge splash, water-level camera, one judge\n421\talways scores 4. This is the attract mode's best shot.\n422\t\n423\t### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\n424\t\n425\tHoops fly in from Tare. Spin your stick in circles: angular speed in the band (`game.hoop.bandMin` 5, `bandMax` 9 rad/s)\n426\tkeeps every hoop up; outside it they sink and fall. A new hoop every 8 s from a telegraphed side: lean that way within 0.6 s\n427\tto catch it. Up to eight at once. Score: hoops × seconds, scaled. The hip-circle strip scrubs with your stick's angle, so\n428\tthe character's hips follow your thumb, with increasing dignity. Keyboard and accessibility: alternate Q and E at 2.5 Hz or\n429\tmore counts as spinning. Mouse: circle it.\n430\t\n431\t### Island Jog (about 150 s)\n432\t\n433\tFollow Gerald round the coast path, a ring of flags past every landmark. Stick steers; alternating feet at about 2.5 Hz gives\n434\t+35% speed (swap `actor.character` for another `createCharacter` with the new speed **[tested]**). Stay within 8 m of him (\"the Pace Ribbon\").\n435\tScore: share of time in the ribbon. Tare hops beside you and talks, the plaques go by. At the end Gerald says: \"Nice weather\n436\tfor it.\" It is the only thing Gerald ever says.\n437\t\n438\t### Group Class\n439\t\n440\tSee section 9.\n441\t\n442\t---\n443\t\n444\t## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\n445\t\n446\tDay 5, evening. It uses every verb at the scale of the world. There is no fail state, only remarks.\n447\t\n448\t**How the tilt works.** `island.tiltX, tiltZ` are sim values. The island's geometry never moves. Instead:\n449\t\n450\t- Actors get a slope push: the pilot system (section 14) adds `slope × sin(tilt)`, downhill, to the move it writes.\n451\t- Dynamic props (sun loungers, crates, drinks) get a per-step impulse with `knock`. Rapier's own gravity stays straight\n452\t  down: `physics.gravity` has no sideways part **[source]**.\n453\t- A custom camera banks with `makePose({ roll })` **[source]**. The sea prop, on a kinematic body, counter-rotates\n454\t  so the horizon stays level on screen while the island visibly tips. Use a sky with no silhouette backdrop for this.\n455\t\n456\tTilt grows by `game.tilt.rate`, and each deed below takes some off.\n457\t\n458\t1. **Storm (20 s, cutscene).** The sky darkens, rain falls (`frame.emit`), the ferry horn sounds far away. Close-up: Plumb's\n459\t   plait swings. Plumb, flat as ever: \"The island is now six degrees out of true. Please remain calm. Calm is mandatory.\"\n460\t2. **Everyone East (75 s).** Slope push is on. Twelve guests (crowd agents; Gerald, Bex and Nan among them) drift downhill\n461\t   politely. **Calm Call:** hold both feet 2 s, release: a calm wave (radius 8 m) makes nearby guests follow you. Lead them to\n462\t   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\n463\t   already there.\n464\t3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\n465\t   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\n466\t4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \"Do not\". The camera pulls back to the\n467\t   whole island. **Now the tilt is your CoB:** the stick moves your weight, and your weight moves the island. Waves are the\n468\t   disturbance, breathing quiets them, the ring shrinks as the storm peaks, the lighthouse beam sweeps. Topple: the island lurches\n469\t   3° and Plumb says \"Again, please.\" Hold through to the end.\n470\t5. **Dawn.** It is level. The rain stops, the sea is glass. The plait stops. Plumb opens their eyes, looks at you, says \"Hm.\", and\n471\t   closes them. Tare: \"Everything is balanced now. Please do not tell anyone about the rock.\" The last Morning Check. Credits, with\n472\t   every guest holding a pose as the camera drifts past.\n473\t\n474\tSteps 2, 3 and 4 are time boxed: when one runs out, guests shuffle uphill by themselves, or the fade takes you to the stone with a\n475\tremark, so the ending always comes. Score: delivered guests, tilt at the end of step 4, breath. It feeds the final remark only.\n476\t\n477\t---\n478\t\n479\t## 8. Screens and UX\n480\t\n481\t**10-foot rules (test them at 1920 × 1080):** body text at least 2.6vh (28 px), prompts and menus 3.2vh or more; one idea per\n482\tscreen; at most six menu rows; 5% safe margins; focus unmistakable from a sofa. **No dense web-style data screens:** results are\n483\tone word, one number, one sentence, one small graph. The dev panel is the only busy screen, and only developers open it.\n484\t\n485\t**UI look:** pebble-shaped rounded panels in warm off-white with soft shadows, not the source's look. A rounded system stack\n486\t(`ui-rounded, \"SF Pro Rounded\", \"Segoe UI Rounded\", system-ui`); fonts are allowed but not needed. Screens are HTML/CSS under\n487\t`engine.ui.root`, with `createMenu` for lists (hover already moves its focus, click picks **[source]**) and a small\n488\tgrid of your own for the Noticeboard. `createDialog` is fine for speech: keep text on screen, always, with the voice.\n489\tRestyle the engine's widgets for 10 feet: their defaults are small.\n490\t\n491\t**The Balance Disc** is the HUD's heart, HTML/SVG, 30vh across at the lower centre: target ring, your dot with a short trail, a\n492\tguide ring swelling with the breath, a foot pill either side with analog fill. It reads the sim's `wobble` each frame. A\n493\tmatching ring also lies on the mat in the world (a component with `telegraph`, `position`, `yaw`, `u`, `size` is drawn on the\n494\tfloor). In Group Class each seat gets a smaller disc under its mat.\n495\t\n496\t**Flow:**\n497\t\n498\t```\n499\tLoad → Title ─┬─ Begin/Continue → Pier or the day's morning → Island ⇄ Activity → Results → … → Evening → next day\n500\t              ├─ Free Play (Noticeboard, after Day 1)\n501\t              ├─ Group Class → join on mats → three classes → podium\n502\t              ├─ Settings\n503\t              └─ About / Credits\n504\t      (10 s idle on any front-end menu) ⇄ Attract\n505\t```\n506\t\n507\t- **Load:** HTML first, immediately (\"Calibrating…\"), so the screen is never blank.\n508\t- **Title:** the game's title over a slow orbit of the island, the menu, \"Press any button\" until a pad wakes.\n509\t- **Island:** a small prompt near things (\"✕ Talk\"), Triangle or Tab for today's Programme, nothing else on screen.\n510\t- **Programme:** today's list as up to four cards with stamps, each with \"Go\". **Noticeboard:** a 3 × 2 page of activity cards with\n511\t  best rank; L1, R1 or Q, E page through them.\n512\t- **Results:** rank word, score, pebbles falling onto a little cairn, a line from Plumb or Tare; \"Again\" or \"Carry on\".\n513\t- **Evening:** calendar stamp, the age graph, a closing remark, \"Sleep\".\n514\t- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"33bdb491-783d-4e55-9802-6b07aa5a7120","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:22:35.278Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","content":"    footr: ['KeyE', 'MouseRight', 'PadRightTrigger', 'PadRightShoulder', 'Space'],\n    gentle: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'],\n    act: ['KeyF', 'Enter', 'PadSouth', 'PadEast', 'PadWest', 'PadNorth'],\n  },\n  values: { 'game:r': 'right', 'game:l': 'left', 'game:f': 'forward', 'game:b': 'back', 'game:fl': 'footl', 'game:fr': 'footr' },\n  lock: true,\n});\n```\n\nThe sim reads raw lean as `game:r − game:l`, `game:f − game:b` (a key absent is 0), not the camera-turned `move`.\nTriggers count as \"held\" from 0.5 but their `values` are analog below that.\n\n`actionMap:roam` is the same walk block plus `jump: ['Space', 'PadWest']`, `use: ['KeyE', 'Enter', 'MouseLeft', 'PadSouth']`,\n`walk: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight']`, `plan: ['Tab', 'PadNorth']`, `wave: ['KeyC', 'PadEast']`, `lock: true`.\n\nFront-end screens use the engine's system layer (`uiAccept`, `uiCancel`, `uiUp`…), which no map can rebind, with a map that\nhas `lock: false`, or a click on the canvas behind a menu captures the pointer **[source]**. Sand Garden uses a copy of the\nbalance map with `lock: false`, so the pointer stays visible: the page sends its place as `game:pointer`.\n\nInside activities, read only the map's actions, never `uiAccept`: Space is also breath. Skipping a demonstration is `act`.\nThe first time a mouse player needs the lean, show \"Click to lean with the mouse\": browsers grant pointer lock only in a click.\n\n**Mouse lean:** while pointer-locked in an activity, the page adds `pointermove`'s `movementX/Y` per frame and sends\nthem with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:mouse', [dx, dy])`. The sim keeps `mouseTarget += delta × sensitivity`,\ndecaying with a 0.6 s time constant. Sensitivity lives in Settings.\n\n**Rumble:** a light `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` on topple, on beats in Step Class, and growing with\n`r` near the edge; try/catch around it; a Settings toggle.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Structure\n\n**The Programme.** A five-day residency: a first full play takes about 45 minutes. Each day is a Morning Check plus three\nactivities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\n\n| Day | Activities |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Morning Check (tutorial) · Pose Class A (Seated Nothing, Patient Chair, Heron) · Still Pond · a walk to find the Noticeboard |\n| 2 | Morning Check · Reps Hall · Sand Garden · Pose Class B (Archer, Comma, Napkin) |\n| 3 | Morning Check · Paddle Glide · The Line · Step Class |\n| 4 | Morning Check · Hoop Patrol · Cliff Plunge · Island Jog with Gerald |\n| 5 | Morning Check · Group Class (you and CPU guests) · Pose Class C (Bridge, Lighthouse) · The Great Tilt |\n| After | Final Morning Check, credits, then Free Play with every activity and daily checks |\n\nFinishing all of a day lets you sleep at your hut (walk there, or pick it from the Programme). Every activity can also be\nreplayed from the Noticeboard once met. Activities have no fail state: finishing at any rank counts.\n\n**Getting around.** You may walk everywhere, and the island rewards it, but nothing requires it: every Programme and\nNoticeboard item has \"Go\", which fades to the station. A controller player on a sofa never has to cross the island.\n\n**Wobble Age.** The Morning Check's result, from 18 to 82: `age = round(18 + 64 × (1 − s)^k)`, `k` is `game.age.k` (1.3).\nOne big number, a remark, a stamp on the calendar, and a line graph of at most seven points. Always compared with yesterday,\nin a tone of mild scientific surprise.\n\n**Pebbles and your Cairn.** Pebbles are the currency: 1 to 5 per activity by rank, plus 20 hidden around the island. You\nnever spend them. They stack, one by one, on a physical cairn in the Plaza, with a satisfying clack. The cairn leans\nslightly according to your last Wobble Age and stands true at 18. Thresholds unlock things, shown on the Noticeboard:\n10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \"Unsettling\" stamp set.\n\n**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \"Did you know?\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\nto watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\n\n**Tilt as story.** A value `island.tilt` starts at 0.4° on Day 1 and rises by 0.5° a day, so drinks slide, marbles roll,\nloose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\n\n**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\noutfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\n(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\n\n**Built to grow.** Days, poses, charts, trays, courses, lines, lures and settings are all data tables, one file each, so\nlater content is adding rows. Keep it that way: it is part of the brief.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Activities\n\nEvery activity is a module exposing the same shape: `{ id, title, station, camera, map, setup, step, teardown, score,\nbot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\nHUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\n45-second form for rounds (section 9).\n\n| Activity | Station | Camera | Verbs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Morning Check | Plaza | Front, low, slow push-in | Lean, a foot |\n| Pose Class | Pavilion | Three-quarter, drifting orbit round your mat | Lean, foot or both |\n| Reps Hall | Annex | Side three-quarter, mirror behind | Lean scrubs the body |\n| Step Class | Annex | Behind and above, class in view | Feet, both, some lean |\n| Still Pond | Pond | Fixed portrait, front | Both, and nothing else |\n| The Line | Lagoon | Behind and above, dolly along the line | Feet, lean x |\n| Paddle Glide | Lagoon | Chase, low | Lean, feet |\n| Sand Garden | Terrace | Top-down, slight perspective | Lean, or pointer |\n| Cliff Plunge | North Cliff | Side dolly, falling follow, water-level splash | Both, lean |\n| Hoop Patrol | Hoop Beach | Front, wide | Lean in circles, or feet |\n| Island Jog | Whole coast | Chase (engine `cam3=chase`) | Stick, feet |\n\n### Morning Check (about 75 s)\n\nTare's Platform. Tare asks one yes/no question for the day (it changes only the remark). Then three tests:\n\n1. **Still Ring**, 12 s: stay inside a ring of r = 0.22, narrowing to 0.16 for the last 4 s. `A` = share of steps inside.\n2. **Reach**, up to 24 s: six targets (r = 0.16) at radius 0.55 in a seeded order; hold each 0.5 s. `B` = 1 − time/24.\n3. **One Foot**, 8 s: hold the foot Tare names; instability × 1.6; ring r = 0.3. Letting go pauses and drains. `C` = share inside.\n\n`s = 0.45A + 0.3B + 0.25C`; score `s × 1000`; Wobble Age as in section 5. Reveal: a large CSS dial spins past 100, \"recalibrating\",\novershoots, and settles. The Day 1 version introduces each verb with one line at a time.\n\n### Pose Class (about 2.5 min, three poses)\n\nPlumb demonstrates on the front mat (4 s, skippable). \"Now you.\"\n\n- **Enter:** a guide dot travels a curved path on the disc from centre to the pose's *seat*. Stay within 0.18 of it and\n  progress advances; progress scrubs the pose strip, so the body goes into the pose exactly as your thumb does. If you never\n  follow, Plumb waits 10 s and moves on: \"We will call that a start.\"\n- **Hold:** `game.pose.hold` s (12) with the CoB in the seat ring (`game.pose.ring`, 0.2), breathing with the guide, while\n  your off-seat lean visibly tips the body over. CPU guests hold too. Plumb does not move.\n- **Release:** \"And rest.\" Score: `1000 × (0.7 × inRing + 0.3 × sync) − 60 × topples`, class mean is the result.\n\n| Pose (id) | What it is | Seat (x, y) | Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Seated Nothing (`nothing`) | Cross-legged, hands on knees | 0, 0 | Sway × 0.5; breath weighs 60% |\n| The Patient Chair (`chair`) | Knees bent, arms forward | 0, −0.35 | Hold both feet throughout, so no breath; sway climbs with time |\n| The Heron (`heron`) | One leg, foot on thigh, palms overhead | 0, 0 | Hold the standing foot; instability × 1.5 |\n| The Archer (`archer`) | Long lunge, arms out | 0.35, 0.35 | Instability × 1.2 |\n| The Sideways Comma (`comma`) | Side bend | 0.5, 0 then −0.5, 0 | Two holds, 8 s each |\n| The Folded Napkin (`napkin`) | Forward fold | 0, 0.5 | Low camera; the Gull lands on your back halfway |\n| The Polite Bridge (`bridge`) | On your back, hips lift | 0, 0 | Hips follow your lungs; breath weighs 70% |\n| The Lighthouse (`lighthouse`) | Tiptoe, arms straight up | 0, 0 | Ring 0.14; sway × 1.2 |\n\n### Reps Hall (about 90 s, three exercises)\n\nThe signature \"thumb is the exercise\" activity. A tall gauge on the HUD shows a band moving at the tempo\n(`game.reps.tempo`, 3 s a rep). Stick depth moves your marker and scrubs the body. Stay within 0.2 of the band to bank the\nrep. Gerald, beside you, does two for each of yours.\n\n- **Deep Knees** (10): pull back to squat, return to stand.\n- **Polite Push-Ups** (8): hold both feet (\"palms on the floor\") and scrub the push-up clip with the stick.\n- **Side Lunges** (10): stick x, alternating sides.\n\nThe band speeds up a little and sway rises near the end. Near the finish the counter cheats: \"9 of 10\" becomes \"10 of\n11\". Plumb: \"Four more. I may be lying.\" Score: mean rep accuracy.\n\n### Step Class (about 100 s)\n\nRhythm on a step platform in the Annex, three phrases at 104, 112 and 120 BPM (`game.step.bpm` scales them), charts as\nstrings in `labs/game/scenes/data/charts.ts`: `\"L . R . L . R . | L L R . B . . .\"`. Footprints scroll to a hit line on the\nHUD, floor tiles light in the world. Notes: L, R, B (both, a jump) and side steps (lean plus foot).\n\nWindows: Perfect ±3 steps, Good ±7 (`game.step.perfect`, `game.step.good`). Combo adds up to × 1.5. The guests behind you\nfollow your combo: lose it and they fall out of time, one by one, politely.\n\n**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\nevents fire claps and kicks at full level. The bed has no drums, so nothing flams against it. Timing is in sim steps,\nnever audio time.\n\n### Still Pond (75 s; 45 s in rounds)\n\nThe funniest thing in the game, and almost no input. You sit cross-legged on a jetty at dawn. **Composure** starts at 1000.\nThe only correct input is breathing with the guide. Anything else is \"You moved\": stick past 0.25, any button, a stray\nfoot, or mouse movement past a small threshold. Each costs `game.pond.penalty` (80), debounced 1 s, and sends a ripple\nacross the pond while the Frog turns to look.\n\nScore: `Composure × (0.5 + 0.5 × sync)`, so doing nothing at all earns \"Adequate\".\n\nLures, from a seeded table, every 6–10 s, escalating:\n\n- A big glyph prompt for whichever device you use: \"PRESS NOW\".\n- Tare: \"Psst. Is this on? Press ✕ for yes.\"\n- The phone-shaped stone buzzes.\n- The Frog sits on your knee. The Gull lands on your head.\n- A fake pause menu slides in with \"Resume\" highlighted.\n- \"Your controller appears to be disconnected. Press any button.\"\n- Plumb, very quietly: \"You are doing it wrong.\"\n- The credits roll. \"Thanks for playing! Press ✕ to continue.\"\n\nReal pause (Options, Esc) always works and costs nothing. Ending: \"You did nothing for seventy-five seconds. Nobody has\never been prouder of you. Nobody was watching.\"\n\n### The Line (about 75 s)\n\nA 40 m slackline across the lagoon with three flags. Alternate feet to step: each step moves 0.75 m and kicks you sideways\n(`game.line.stepKick`, 0.35); the same foot twice is a stumble. Lean x fights it. Gusts every 6–10 s, telegraphed 1.5 s ahead\nby ripples and a flag on Tare's little boat (`game.line.gust`). At 15 m the Gull lands on your arm, adding a steady bias\nuntil you flick it off with a fast stick flip. Falling is a large splash, then Tare's boat takes you back to the last\nflag: \"You have left the line. The line is fine.\" After 120 s the boat collects you: \"The line closes at this time.\"\nScore: `1000 − 150 × falls − 8 × max(0, seconds − 50)`, times the share of the line crossed.\n\n### Paddle Glide (75 s)\n\nStand on a board. Forward lean is speed (`game.paddle.speed`, 6 m/s), side lean steers (1.2 rad/s), feet alternating at\nabout 1.2 Hz give +30% and a kick. Twelve buoy gates round the lagoon with seeded jitter. A ferry wake at gate 7 and a\ncrossing turtle at gate 9 shove your CoB. A topple is a splash and a 3-second remount. Score: gates × 60 + up to 280 for\ntime.\n\n### Sand Garden (90 s, five trays)\n\nA raked sand tray on a stand, seen from above. Lean tilts it up to 12° (`game.garden.tilt`); the mouse pointer's place on\nthe tray does the same. Marbles obey your own 2D integrator in the sim (slope × `game.garden.gravity`, friction, ridge\nsegments, holes that catch below `game.garden.sink` speed). Trays are data, 1–3 marbles each, rising to moving rakes and a\ngap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\n\n### Cliff Plunge (three dives)\n\nA 14 m cliff. **Compose:** hold ring and breath for 4 s to fill power. **Go:** release both feet as a swinging gauge peaks.\n**Air** (about 2 s): lean y spins you, lean x twists, scrubbing a rotation strip. Enter the water within 15° of vertical.\nThree Gulls hold up score cards, 0 to 10. Sum of all cards, scaled to 1000. Huge splash, water-level camera, one judge\nalways scores 4. This is the attract mode's best shot.\n\n### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\n\nHoops fly in from Tare. Spin your stick in circles: angular speed in the band (`game.hoop.bandMin` 5, `bandMax` 9 rad/s)\nkeeps every hoop up; outside it they sink and fall. A new hoop every 8 s from a telegraphed side: lean that way within 0.6 s\nto catch it. Up to eight at once. Score: hoops × seconds, scaled. The hip-circle strip scrubs with your stick's angle, so\nthe character's hips follow your thumb, with increasing dignity. Keyboard and accessibility: alternate Q and E at 2.5 Hz or\nmore counts as spinning. Mouse: circle it.\n\n### Island Jog (about 150 s)\n\nFollow Gerald round the coast path, a ring of flags past every landmark. Stick steers; alternating feet at about 2.5 Hz gives\n+35% speed (swap `actor.character` for another `createCharacter` with the new speed **[tested]**). Stay within 8 m of him (\"the Pace Ribbon\").\nScore: share of time in the ribbon. Tare hops beside you and talks, the plaques go by. At the end Gerald says: \"Nice weather\nfor it.\" It is the only thing Gerald ever says.\n\n### Group Class\n\nSee section 9.\n\n---\n\n## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\n\nDay 5, evening. It uses every verb at the scale of the world. There is no fail state, only remarks.\n\n**How the tilt works.** `island.tiltX, tiltZ` are sim values. The island's geometry never moves. Instead:\n\n- Actors get a slope push: the pilot system (section 14) adds `slope × sin(tilt)`, downhill, to the move it writes.\n- Dynamic props (sun loungers, crates, drinks) get a per-step impulse with `knock`. Rapier's own gravity stays straight\n  down: `physics.gravity` has no sideways part **[source]**.\n- A custom camera banks with `makePose({ roll })` **[source]**. The sea prop, on a kinematic body, counter-rotates\n  so the horizon stays level on screen while the island visibly tips. Use a sky with no silhouette backdrop for this.\n\nTilt grows by `game.tilt.rate`, and each deed below takes some off.\n\n1. **Storm (20 s, cutscene).** The sky darkens, rain falls (`frame.emit`), the ferry horn sounds far away. Close-up: Plumb's\n   plait swings. Plumb, flat as ever: \"The island is now six degrees out of true. Please remain calm. Calm is mandatory.\"\n2. **Everyone East (75 s).** Slope push is on. Twelve guests (crowd agents; Gerald, Bex and Nan among them) drift downhill\n   politely. **Calm Call:** hold both feet 2 s, release: a calm wave (radius 8 m) makes nearby guests follow you. Lead them to\n   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\n   already there.\n3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\n   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\n4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \"Do not\". The camera pulls back to the\n   whole island. **Now the tilt is your CoB:** the stick moves your weight, and your weight moves the island. Waves are the\n   disturbance, breathing quiets them, the ring shrinks as the storm peaks, the lighthouse beam sweeps. Topple: the island lurches\n   3° and Plumb says \"Again, please.\" Hold through to the end.\n5. **Dawn.** It is level. The rain stops, the sea is glass. The plait stops. Plumb opens their eyes, looks at you, says \"Hm.\", and\n   closes them. Tare: \"Everything is balanced now. Please do not tell anyone about the rock.\" The last Morning Check. Credits, with\n   every guest holding a pose as the camera drifts past.\n\nSteps 2, 3 and 4 are time boxed: when one runs out, guests shuffle uphill by themselves, or the fade takes you to the stone with a\nremark, so the ending always comes. Score: delivered guests, tilt at the end of step 4, breath. It feeds the final remark only.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Screens and UX\n\n**10-foot rules (test them at 1920 × 1080):** body text at least 2.6vh (28 px), prompts and menus 3.2vh or more; one idea per\nscreen; at most six menu rows; 5% safe margins; focus unmistakable from a sofa. **No dense web-style data screens:** results are\none word, one number, one sentence, one small graph. The dev panel is the only busy screen, and only developers open it.\n\n**UI look:** pebble-shaped rounded panels in warm off-white with soft shadows, not the source's look. A rounded system stack\n(`ui-rounded, \"SF Pro Rounded\", \"Segoe UI Rounded\", system-ui`); fonts are allowed but not needed. Screens are HTML/CSS under\n`engine.ui.root`, with `createMenu` for lists (hover already moves its focus, click picks **[source]**) and a small\ngrid of your own for the Noticeboard. `createDialog` is fine for speech: keep text on screen, always, with the voice.\nRestyle the engine's widgets for 10 feet: their defaults are small.\n\n**The Balance Disc** is the HUD's heart, HTML/SVG, 30vh across at the lower centre: target ring, your dot with a short trail, a\nguide ring swelling with the breath, a foot pill either side with analog fill. It reads the sim's `wobble` each frame. A\nmatching ring also lies on the mat in the world (a component with `telegraph`, `position`, `yaw`, `u`, `size` is drawn on the\nfloor). In Group Class each seat gets a smaller disc under its mat.\n\n**Flow:**\n\n```\nLoad → Title ─┬─ Begin/Continue → Pier or the day's morning → Island ⇄ Activity → Results → … → Evening → next day\n              ├─ Free Play (Noticeboard, after Day 1)\n              ├─ Group Class → join on mats → three classes → podium\n              ├─ Settings\n              └─ About / Credits\n      (10 s idle on any front-end menu) ⇄ Attract\n```\n\n- **Load:** HTML first, immediately (\"Calibrating…\"), so the screen is never blank.\n- **Title:** the game's title over a slow orbit of the island, the menu, \"Press any button\" until a pad wakes.\n- **Island:** a small prompt near things (\"✕ Talk\"), Triangle or Tab for today's Programme, nothing else on screen.\n- **Programme:** today's list as up to four cards with stamps, each with \"Go\". **Noticeboard:** a 3 × 2 page of activity cards with\n  best rank; L1, R1 or Q, E page through them.\n- **Results:** rank word, score, pebbles falling onto a little cairn, a line from Plumb or Tare; \"Again\" or \"Carry on\".\n- **Evening:** calendar stamp, the age graph, a closing remark, \"Sleep\".\n- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):","numLines":300,"startLine":215,"totalLines":1043}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R1FWkCdgzq2HbQSfLHc6q1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
