{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDoVtVaKxiCtmNEbY33","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FXAgT7rwpCQxp3bE6DiAWv","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","offset":514,"limit":120},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10814,"cache_read_input_tokens":560516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10814},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"3e2091e9-64a6-40fc-89e9-b0d0985ff330","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:22:52.619Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDoVVgc7d4p73EinD3L","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FXAgT7rwpCQxp3bE6DiAWv":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","offset":514,"limit":120}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXAgT7rwpCQxp3bE6DiAWv","type":"tool_result","content":"514\t- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):\n515\t  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\n516\t- **Settings:** Music (**10% by default**), Effects, Voices, Button icons, Mouse sensitivity, Invert look, Rumble, Steadier Hands (an\n517\t  assist: halves the sway), Reduced Motion (no camera roll or shake), Fullscreen, Erase Save.\n518\t- **Controls:** shows the bindings per scheme; keyboard rebinding through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind`, `listen`.\n519\t- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\n520\t  (section 19).\n521\t\n522\t**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n523\t\n524\t- **Live sliders with Reset**, per group and for all: every setting named `game.*` in this plan, plus `game.pebbles.mult` and\n525\t  `game.age.k`. They are sim settings with `when: 'now'`, changed by `inspector.set(path, value)`, so they apply at once and replays\n526\t  hold them. Defaults come from `inspector.describe('setting', path)` **[tested]**.\n527\t- **Jumps:** to any day, any activity, any finale step. Finish activity now at a chosen rank.\n528\t- **Cheats:** bot plays for me, no topple, unlock all, give pebbles, reset save, a throwaway save mode (`createStore` `sandbox`).\n529\t- **Tools:** time scale (0.25, 1, 4), pause and frame step, free camera (`cam3=fly`), state overlay (CoB, calm, sync, tilt, event,\n530\t  phase, tick, hash), seed and new seed, copy tuned settings as JSON.\n531\t\n532\t**Attract mode.** 10 s with no input on any front-end menu starts it; any key, mouse movement, click or pad input leaves it, back to\n533\twhere you were. Set `game.auto` and restart the scene with `inspector.seed(n)` (restarts the sim, keeps settings **[tested]**).\n534\tThe sim's director runs a loop with the bot cheating freely: island flyby and jog, Pose Class, Still Pond with its lures, The Line,\n535\tPaddle Glide, Sand Garden, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, then the Great Tilt's Centre Stone, about 15 s each, then round\n536\tagain. Banner: the game's title, \"DEMO\", \"Press any button\" with the current glyph. It never touches the save.\n537\t\n538\t**Touch-only devices** (`(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)`, no pad or key seen yet): no touch controls, no touch play. The title\n539\tshows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button that works by tap. Attract still starts and loops behind it. A key or pad\n540\tinput at any time returns to normal. Always pass `touch=off` in the engine's query, or it draws its own touch stick **[source; the setting is accepted: tested]**.\n541\t\n542\t**No WebGPU:** a plain, friendly page: \"This game needs a browser with WebGPU, such as current Chrome or Edge.\" Never a blank page.\n543\t\n544\t---\n545\t\n546\t## 9. Multiplayer\n547\t\n548\tThe game has two kinds, both up to four players. They share one module: `labs/game/scenes/round.ts`.\n549\t\n550\t**A Round** is three classes dealt from `w.rng('deal')` (same seed, same deal): Still Ring, then one of Heron, Hoop or Step, then Still\n551\tPond, each in its `short` 45 s form with a 6 s lead-in. About 2.7 minutes. Score: the sum, 0–3000. They all play on mats, so they need\n552\tnothing but the pavilion.\n553\t\n554\t### On its own: Group Class\n555\t\n556\tSame screen, up to four pads (keyboard and mouse can hold one seat). Walk up to the Pavilion or pick it from the title. Mats light in\n557\tseat colours as people press Cross or Space to join. Empty seats go to CPU guests (Settings can turn them off); Day 5 fields Gerald,\n558\tBex and Nan. CPU guests are the bot with extra sway per character. Podium at the end, and a sash reading \"Least Wobbly\".\n559\t\n560\tThe engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\n561\teach seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\n562\t\n563\t### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n564\t\n565\tRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n566\t`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n567\tfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n568\t\n569\tWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\n570\twobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\n571\t\n572\t**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\n573\t\n574\t```html\n575\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n576\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n577\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n578\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n579\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\n580\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\">\n581\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n582\t```\n583\t\n584\tGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\n585\t\n586\t**Startup** **[tested: this exact shape passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n587\t\n588\t```ts\n589\tconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n590\tfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\n591\tsearch.set('touch', 'off');\n592\tconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\n593\tconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n594\tif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\n595\tconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\n596\tengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\n597\tif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\n598\t```\n599\t\n600\t**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\n601\tunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\n602\tanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\n603\t`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n604\t\n605\t**The round in a session:**\n606\t\n607\t- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\n608\t  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\n609\t  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\n610\t  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n611\t  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\n612\t- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\n613\t  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n614\t- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \"Class 2 · 640\"), and every 100 ms\n615\t  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\n616\t- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\n617\t  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\n618\t  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\n619\t- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\"Wobble Age\", \"Best hold\", \"Breath\"),\n620\t  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\"Unnervingly Still\").\n621\t- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\n622\t- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\n623\t- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\n624\t  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\n625\t  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\n626\t- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\n627\t\n628\t**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\n629\tgame alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\n630\tpavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n631\t\n632\t---\n633\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"2880a365-fdc1-4e92-a089-9fc2c5e7fc70","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:22:52.626Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211902__xe334ec/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):\n  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\n- **Settings:** Music (**10% by default**), Effects, Voices, Button icons, Mouse sensitivity, Invert look, Rumble, Steadier Hands (an\n  assist: halves the sway), Reduced Motion (no camera roll or shake), Fullscreen, Erase Save.\n- **Controls:** shows the bindings per scheme; keyboard rebinding through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind`, `listen`.\n- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\n  (section 19).\n\n**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n\n- **Live sliders with Reset**, per group and for all: every setting named `game.*` in this plan, plus `game.pebbles.mult` and\n  `game.age.k`. They are sim settings with `when: 'now'`, changed by `inspector.set(path, value)`, so they apply at once and replays\n  hold them. Defaults come from `inspector.describe('setting', path)` **[tested]**.\n- **Jumps:** to any day, any activity, any finale step. Finish activity now at a chosen rank.\n- **Cheats:** bot plays for me, no topple, unlock all, give pebbles, reset save, a throwaway save mode (`createStore` `sandbox`).\n- **Tools:** time scale (0.25, 1, 4), pause and frame step, free camera (`cam3=fly`), state overlay (CoB, calm, sync, tilt, event,\n  phase, tick, hash), seed and new seed, copy tuned settings as JSON.\n\n**Attract mode.** 10 s with no input on any front-end menu starts it; any key, mouse movement, click or pad input leaves it, back to\nwhere you were. Set `game.auto` and restart the scene with `inspector.seed(n)` (restarts the sim, keeps settings **[tested]**).\nThe sim's director runs a loop with the bot cheating freely: island flyby and jog, Pose Class, Still Pond with its lures, The Line,\nPaddle Glide, Sand Garden, Step Class, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, then the Great Tilt's Centre Stone, about 15 s each, then round\nagain. Banner: the game's title, \"DEMO\", \"Press any button\" with the current glyph. It never touches the save.\n\n**Touch-only devices** (`(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)`, no pad or key seen yet): no touch controls, no touch play. The title\nshows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button that works by tap. Attract still starts and loops behind it. A key or pad\ninput at any time returns to normal. Always pass `touch=off` in the engine's query, or it draws its own touch stick **[source; the setting is accepted: tested]**.\n\n**No WebGPU:** a plain, friendly page: \"This game needs a browser with WebGPU, such as current Chrome or Edge.\" Never a blank page.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Multiplayer\n\nThe game has two kinds, both up to four players. They share one module: `labs/game/scenes/round.ts`.\n\n**A Round** is three classes dealt from `w.rng('deal')` (same seed, same deal): Still Ring, then one of Heron, Hoop or Step, then Still\nPond, each in its `short` 45 s form with a 6 s lead-in. About 2.7 minutes. Score: the sum, 0–3000. They all play on mats, so they need\nnothing but the pavilion.\n\n### On its own: Group Class\n\nSame screen, up to four pads (keyboard and mouse can hold one seat). Walk up to the Pavilion or pick it from the title. Mats light in\nseat colours as people press Cross or Space to join. Empty seats go to CPU guests (Settings can turn them off); Day 5 fields Gerald,\nBex and Nan. CPU guests are the bot with extra sway per character. Podium at the end, and a sash reading \"Least Wobbly\".\n\nThe engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\neach seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\n\n### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n\nRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\nfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n\nWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\nwobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\n\n**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\nGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\n\n**Startup** **[tested: this exact shape passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n\n```ts\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\nconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\nconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\nif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\nconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\nif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\n```\n\n**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\nunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\nanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\n`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n\n**The round in a session:**\n\n- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\n  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\n  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\n  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\n- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\n  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \"Class 2 · 640\"), and every 100 ms\n  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\n- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\n  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\n- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\"Wobble Age\", \"Best hold\", \"Breath\"),\n  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\"Unnervingly Still\").\n- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\n- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\n- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\n  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\n  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\n- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\n\n**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\ngame alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\npavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n\n---\n","numLines":120,"startLine":514,"totalLines":1043}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FXAgT7rwpCQxp3bE6DiAWv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
