{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQncwei3edBmaN54UKzGu1","type":"tool_result","content":"17:## 1. The game\n57:## 2. World and cast\n108:## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\n176:## 4. Controls\n246:## 5. Structure\n290:## 6. Activities\n444:## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\n479:## 8. Screens and UX\n546:## 9. Multiplayer\n634:## 10. Art direction\n682:## 11. Animation\n732:## 12. Audio\n774:## 13. Writing\n819:## 14. Tech\n909:## 15. Engine traps (all met on this machine)\n937:## 16. Testing\n973:## 17. Build order\n994:## 18. Done\n1004:## 19. Reports\n1016:## 20. Brief-to-plan map\n  | Bex | 210 Hz | 80 ms | Monotone with a sigh at the end |\n  | Nan | 170 Hz | 120 ms | Vibrato |\n  | PA | Plumb through a narrow band | | The finale's loudspeaker |\n\n- **`say(speaker, text)`** in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`: one syllable per two letters, hashed from the letters so the same line always babbles the same way; `audio.play(id, { pitch, when, vol, bus: '\n\n**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thum\n\nIn `onFrame`: `audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined)`, then play each new sim event by `seq` from `frame.world.events.trace()`. Reset your `seq` when `frame.world` changes (after a re\n\n**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voic\n\n---\n\n## 13. Writing\n\n**Voice.** Short declarative sentences in the second person. Polite, level, a beat too honest. Statements of fact that turn into mild judgement, then keep going as if nothing happened. \"Did you know?\"\n\nSeed lines, use and add to them:\n\n**Tare**\n- \"Welcome to Little Fulcrum. I am Tare. I used to weigh people. We don't talk about that.\"\n- \"I no longer measure weight. It made people sad, and it made me sad. Now I only measure how much you wobble.\"\n- \"Please step on me. Not like that. Actually, like that is fine.\"\n- \"Your Wobble Age is 61. Yesterday it was 64. You have become three years younger by standing still. Science.\"\n- \"That was your best score so far. It is also your only score so far. Well done on both.\"\n- \"You came back. A lot of people say they will.\"\n- \"Have you been leaning toward anything lately? A person? A decision?\"\n- \"Did you sleep on your left side? You don't have to answer. I can tell. I can't tell. Did you?\"\n- \"Please keep to the centre. No reason.\"\n- \"Have you ever stood on one foot when nobody was looking?\" Yes: \"I know.\" No: \"I know.\"\n- \"Everything is fine. If anyone asks, everything was always fine.\"\n\n**Plumb**\n- \"Good. Now do that again, but as though you meant it.\"\n- \"Breathe in. Breathe out. You have been doing this for years, and yet.\"\n- \"Your knee is where it should be. I mention it because it is rare.\"\n- \"And rest. You may stop wobbling now. Thank you for stopping.\"\n- \"You fell. The mat forgives you. The mat is not me.\"\n- \"That was adequate. I chose that word carefully.\"\n- \"Four more. I may be lying. We will both find out.\"\n\n**Others**\n- Gerald: \"Morning.\"\n- Bex: \"My mum says this is good for me.\" / \"I got a 98. I wasn't trying.\"\n- Nan: \"I've been standing here since Tuesday.\" \"Which Tuesday?\" \"Yes.\"\n\n**Plaques and notices**\n- \"Did you know? The average person leans two degrees toward the things they want.\"\n- \"Did you know? This plaque was four centimetres to the left on Tuesday.\"\n- \"Did you know? A flamingo stands on one leg because it has been told it is being watched.\"\n- \"Did you know? Gulls do not have a Wobble Age. They have been asked.\"\n- \"Notice: Guests are reminded to distribute themselves evenly.\"\n- \"Notice: The east lawn is fully booked. Please enjoy the east lawn.\"\n- \"Notice: If your drink slides, that is a feature of the drink.\"\n- Evening: \"Today you wobbled less than you might have. Goodnight.\"\n\n---\n\n## 14. Tech\n\n**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compar\n\n**Setup [tested], in the empty dev folder:**\n\n```sh\nsrc=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <short-lowercase-name>\nnpm ci           # 10 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh here: it downloads Node and Chromium outside your folder.\nnpm test         # 5 s\nnpm run check    # 22 s\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21849288-0c8f-4994-9d0f-3ff83c647ec0","uuid":"e8a39cb1-bf83-4b76-a841-4b121574874d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:22:54.199Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"17:## 1. The game\n57:## 2. World and cast\n108:## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\n176:## 4. Controls\n246:## 5. Structure\n290:## 6. Activities\n444:## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\n479:## 8. Screens and UX\n546:## 9. Multiplayer\n634:## 10. Art direction\n682:## 11. Animation\n732:## 12. Audio\n774:## 13. Writing\n819:## 14. Tech\n909:## 15. Engine traps (all met on this machine)\n937:## 16. Testing\n973:## 17. Build order\n994:## 18. Done\n1004:## 19. Reports\n1016:## 20. Brief-to-plan map\n  | Bex | 210 Hz | 80 ms | Monotone with a sigh at the end |\n  | Nan | 170 Hz | 120 ms | Vibrato |\n  | PA | Plumb through a narrow band | | The finale's loudspeaker |\n\n- **`say(speaker, text)`** in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`: one syllable per two letters, hashed from the letters so the same line always babbles the same way; `audio.play(id, { pitch, when, vol, bus: '\n\n**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thum\n\nIn `onFrame`: `audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined)`, then play each new sim event by `seq` from `frame.world.events.trace()`. Reset your `seq` when `frame.world` changes (after a re\n\n**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voic\n\n---\n\n## 13. Writing\n\n**Voice.** Short declarative sentences in the second person. Polite, level, a beat too honest. Statements of fact that turn into mild judgement, then keep going as if nothing happened. \"Did you know?\"\n\nSeed lines, use and add to them:\n\n**Tare**\n- \"Welcome to Little Fulcrum. I am Tare. I used to weigh people. We don't talk about that.\"\n- \"I no longer measure weight. It made people sad, and it made me sad. Now I only measure how much you wobble.\"\n- \"Please step on me. Not like that. Actually, like that is fine.\"\n- \"Your Wobble Age is 61. Yesterday it was 64. You have become three years younger by standing still. Science.\"\n- \"That was your best score so far. It is also your only score so far. Well done on both.\"\n- \"You came back. A lot of people say they will.\"\n- \"Have you been leaning toward anything lately? A person? A decision?\"\n- \"Did you sleep on your left side? You don't have to answer. I can tell. I can't tell. Did you?\"\n- \"Please keep to the centre. No reason.\"\n- \"Have you ever stood on one foot when nobody was looking?\" Yes: \"I know.\" No: \"I know.\"\n- \"Everything is fine. If anyone asks, everything was always fine.\"\n\n**Plumb**\n- \"Good. Now do that again, but as though you meant it.\"\n- \"Breathe in. Breathe out. You have been doing this for years, and yet.\"\n- \"Your knee is where it should be. I mention it because it is rare.\"\n- \"And rest. You may stop wobbling now. Thank you for stopping.\"\n- \"You fell. The mat forgives you. The mat is not me.\"\n- \"That was adequate. I chose that word carefully.\"\n- \"Four more. I may be lying. We will both find out.\"\n\n**Others**\n- Gerald: \"Morning.\"\n- Bex: \"My mum says this is good for me.\" / \"I got a 98. I wasn't trying.\"\n- Nan: \"I've been standing here since Tuesday.\" \"Which Tuesday?\" \"Yes.\"\n\n**Plaques and notices**\n- \"Did you know? The average person leans two degrees toward the things they want.\"\n- \"Did you know? This plaque was four centimetres to the left on Tuesday.\"\n- \"Did you know? A flamingo stands on one leg because it has been told it is being watched.\"\n- \"Did you know? Gulls do not have a Wobble Age. They have been asked.\"\n- \"Notice: Guests are reminded to distribute themselves evenly.\"\n- \"Notice: The east lawn is fully booked. Please enjoy the east lawn.\"\n- \"Notice: If your drink slides, that is a feature of the drink.\"\n- Evening: \"Today you wobbled less than you might have. Goodnight.\"\n\n---\n\n## 14. Tech\n\n**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compar\n\n**Setup [tested], in the empty dev folder:**\n\n```sh\nsrc=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <short-lowercase-name>\nnpm ci           # 10 s. Do NOT run scripts/setup.sh here: it downloads Node and Chromium outside your folder.\nnpm test         # 5 s\nnpm run check    # 22 s\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VQncwei3edBmaN54UKzGu1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
