ts, outfits.\n12. **Finish.** Section 18 and 19.\n\n**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → H\n\n---\n\n## 18. Done\n\n- Every feature in this plan is real: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. `grep -rEi \"todo|fixme|placeholder|stub\" labs/game` is clean (except test words).\n- A new player can reach the credits from the title with a pad alone, and again with keyboard and mouse alone.\n- `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` reports zero failures; `npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the engine is unchanged or its patch is declared.\n- The single HTML is in the place your TASK.md names, opens from `file://`, and fetches nothing.\n- `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is and the calls you made. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is honest and specific.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Reports\n\nYour TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and th\n\n**Keep a running tally as you go** of the issues testing catches, and which were critical: you will be asked for both, and for your most and least helpful test. Note engine surprises in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` whe\n\nAnswers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the \n\nHub catalogue suggestions: type `Game`; genre `Sports`; source `Wii Fit`; series empty (the source is its own franchise); players `1–4`; controls \"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse but\n\n**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius 